{"number": 1, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1a", "red": "RED_0001", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "Red first for 001 §B 'Physics is pure data' (.spec-md §3.1): a tabulated import becomes axis data. Facts only; no production file changes. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs` (module `MaterialImportTests`, beside the tabulated facts at `:35-59`) add three facts. (1) `a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`: `(readYaml \"Si.yml\").importMaterial` MUST be `Ok entry` whose `entry.complexity` is `Some c` with `c.eps = EpsWithDispValue (IsotropicDispersive [ segment ])`, `c.magnetic = None` and `c.active = None`; `segment.wavelengthInterval.lower.value` and `.upper.value` MUST be the first and last tabulated wavelengths of `fixtures/Si.yml` (0.250 µm and 0.700 µm) in metres, within 1e-15 m; `c.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864`) MUST be false, because a table is not editable term data, and the import stays view-only as its `complexity = None` keeps it today (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:193`); and `entry.properties.epsWithDisp.getEps w` MUST equal `c.toProperties.epsWithDisp.getEps w` at every tabulated wavelength (the seed invariant `properties = complexity.toProperties`). The fact MUST NOT name an `EpsAxisDispersion` case that does not exist yet, so it compiles on the start tree. (2) `an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`: the same assertions over `(readCsv \"sample-nk.csv\").importMaterial` and its range, 400 nm to 700 nm. (3) `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours`: for every row of `Si.yml` and of `sample-nk.csv`, `epsAt entry` at the row's wavelength MUST equal `nkSquared` of the row's n and k, and at the midpoint of every pair of neighbouring rows it MUST equal `nkSquared` of the two rows' mean n and mean k, each within the file's `closeC 1e-12`. The fact writes the rows out from the fixtures; it does not parse the fixtures a second way. Facts (1) and (2) are red on the start tree, because `entryFromTabulated` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:183-194`) sets `complexity = None`. Fact (3) passes on the start tree's closure (`buildTabulatedClosure`, `:158-179`) and MUST stay green when the closure becomes data in step 2: it proves that no number moves.", "acceptance": "After the three facts land, constructor-unit-tests (MaterialImportTests) MUST fail with exactly `a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range` and `an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`, each failing on a `None` complexity; `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours` and every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 2, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1a", "closes": "RED_0001", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [1], "how_to": "The tabulated n,k table becomes an axis case of the core, and the import builds it (001 §B; .spec-md §3.1). The kernel MOVES from Storage into the core in this step, so one implementation exists. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, before `EpsAxisDispersion` (`:365`): (a) `TabulatedInterpolation`, a one-case union `LinearInWaveLengthClamped` (linear in λ, clamped to the end samples), with `member value : int` = 1 and `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : TabulatedInterpolation option` answering `None` for any other tag. (b) `TabulatedTableError` with `EmptyTableErr`, `SampleCountMismatchErr` and `UnsortedSamplesErr`, each `of reason : string` naming the counts or the first offending index. (c) `TabulatedNkTable`, a record marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]` with `wavelengths : float<meter> array` (ascending), `n : float array`, `k : float array` and `interpolation : TabulatedInterpolation`. `static member tryCreate (wavelengths : float<meter> array) (n : float array) (k : float array) : Result<TabulatedNkTable, TabulatedTableError>` refuses an empty table, columns of unequal length and a wavelength column that decreases anywhere, sets `interpolation = LinearInWaveLengthClamped`, and does not sort. `member sampleRange : WaveLengthInterval` answers the first to the last sample, each as `WaveLength.nm`. `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex` is the arithmetic of `buildTabulatedClosure` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:160-179`) moved verbatim, answering the index instead of its `Eps`: a one-sample table answers that sample; at or below the first sample, the first; at or above the last, the last; otherwise the same forward scan for the bracketing pair, with t = (λ − a)/(b − a) and t = 0 when the pair shares one wavelength. (d) `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `TabulatedNK of TabulatedNkTable`, and `complexIndex` (`:371-378`) calls the table. While the custom equality stays (until step 9), `Equals` (`:380-388`) compares two `TabulatedNK` values structurally and `GetHashCode` (`:390-394`) hashes the table structurally. The doc comment at `:346-356` names the new case. (2) Every match on `EpsAxisDispersion` follows the new case: `DispersionModel.parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:427-435`) answers `[]` for it, because a table has no editable term scalars; `EpsAxisDispersion.facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:91-95`) answers `DiscreteKey \"Tabulated n/k\"`; and `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats it as the evaluated case is treated, as data that is not editable term data. Their doc comments name the new case. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs`: `entryFromTabulated` (`:183-194`) sorts its rows by wavelength with the `Array.sortBy` `buildTabulatedClosure` used (`:159`), builds the table through `TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate`, and answers `Result<MaterialEntry, ImportError>`; a `TabulatedTableError` maps to `NoDataErr` carrying its reason. The entry's `complexity` is `Some` with one isotropic dispersive segment over `table.sampleRange` whose axis is `TabulatedNK table`, `magnetic = None` and `active = None`, and `properties = complexity.toProperties`, as `entryOfAxis` (`:455-469`) does for formula imports. The two call sites (`:502`, `:544`) drop their `Ok` wrapper. `buildTabulatedClosure` is deleted. The closure wording of the module doc (`:18-26`) and of `entryFromTabulated` (`:190-192`) is rewritten, and `NkTableRow`'s carrier reason (`:84`) no longer names a closure. Formula imports are untouched. A tabulated import now has a defined band, its sample range, so the out-of-band diagnostic flags a request outside it (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:166-177`). This is intended: outside its range the table clamps. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains five: `A tabulated axis returns each sample at its own wavelength and interpolates linearly between neighbours`, `A tabulated axis clamps to its first sample below the table and to its last sample above it`, `A single-sample tabulated axis is constant at every wavelength`, `TabulatedNkTable tryCreate refuses an empty table, unequal columns and a decreasing wavelength column` and `The tabulated interpolation rule round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag`. They use a hand-written table (for example 400, 500 and 700 nm, n 1.50, 1.60 and 1.90, k 0.00, 0.10 and 0.30), compute each expected value in the fact, and compare through `BerremanTests.MatrixComparison`'s helpers. The interpolating fact also builds the engine `Eps` through `EpsWithDispValue.toEpsWithDisp` and compares it with `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of the interpolated index. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs` gains `a tabulated axis lands on the tabulated n,k facet key`. `MaterialImportTests` gains `the imported table holds the samples sorted by wavelength in metres under the linear clamped rule`, which matches `TabulatedNK table` on the `Si.yml` import and checks its three columns against the fixture rows. No number moves: step 1's facts are the proof.", "acceptance": "After the table becomes axis data, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the two MaterialImportTests facts step 1 left red, `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours`, the two new facts, and every other MaterialImportTests, LibraryFacetsTests and ExportImportTests fact; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass with the five new tabulated facts; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.A tabulated axis returns each sample at its own wavelength and interpolates linearly between neighbours", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.A tabulated axis clamps to its first sample below the table and to its last sample above it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.A single-sample tabulated axis is constant at every wavelength", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.TabulatedNkTable tryCreate refuses an empty table, unequal columns and a decreasing wavelength column", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The tabulated interpolation rule round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests.a tabulated axis lands on the tabulated n,k facet key", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.the imported table holds the samples sorted by wavelength in metres under the linear clamped rule", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 3, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.1b", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "`AbscissaKind` MOVES from the Domain into the core, so the transcendental laws of steps 5 and 7 can carry their abscissa as data (.spec-md §3.1). No number moves and no behaviour changes. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, after `ComplexDispersionFormula` (`:272-280`): the public union `AbscissaKind` with `LinearInX of wavelengthScale : float<meter>` and `ReciprocalInX of ReciprocalAbscissa`, and the record `ReciprocalAbscissa`, marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]`, with `wavelengthScale : float<meter>` and `numerator : float`. The doc comment of `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:582-585` moves with it. (2) `DispersionModels.fs`: the private `AbscissaKind` (`:586-602`) is deleted. Its `ofUnit` becomes a static extension member of the core type, `static member ofUnit (u : UnitOfMeasure) : AbscissaKind`, declared in `DispersionModels.fs` before its first use, because it reads the `Units` seam and the core cannot reference it. Its body is unchanged, except that it builds the reciprocal case as `ReciprocalInX { wavelengthScale = nanometer; numerator = (fromMeters u nanometer).value }`. The five lowering sites that match it (`:697`, `:706`, `:723`, `:738`, `:753`) read `r.wavelengthScale` and `r.numerator` where they read `(scale, numerator)` and `numerator.value`. The `AC-B5` grid facts of `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` (`:181-298`), over micrometre and electron-volt abscissas, are the proof and stay unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the move, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B5 lowering facts unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 4, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1c", "red": "RED_0002", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [3], "how_to": "Red first: an analytic model lowers to DATA, so equal models lower to equal axes (001 §B 'Physics is pure data'; .spec-md §3.1). Facts only. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` add `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data`. It uses the Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator coefficient sets of `AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`:306-326`). For each model, lowering it twice through `toEpsAxis`, and lowering two separately built equal models, MUST give equal `EpsAxisDispersion` values with equal hashes, and `toEpsValue` MUST give equal `EpsWithDispValue` values. A model whose `bandGap` (Tauc-Lorentz) or `energy` (Gaussian) differs MUST lower to an unequal axis. The fact is red on the start tree: both models lower to `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:766-769`), a fresh closure on every call, which the custom equality compares by reference (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:386`).", "acceptance": "After the fact lands, constructor-unit-tests (DispersionModelsTests) MUST fail with exactly `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data`, failing on the first equality of two lowered axes; every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 5, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1c", "closes": "RED_0002", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [4], "how_to": "The Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models become axis data, evaluated by kernels that MOVE into the core, so one implementation exists (.spec-md §3.1). (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: (a) `AbscissaKind` gains `member abscissaAt (w : WaveLength) : float`: `LinearInX scale` answers `w.value / scale`, and `ReciprocalInX r` answers `r.numerator / (w.value / r.wavelengthScale)`. For every `UnitOfMeasure` this is the same floating-point arithmetic as `fromMeters` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/Units.fs:104-114`) over the scale and numerator `ofUnit` derives, so the abscissa is bit-identical. (b) Two records marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]`: `TaucLorentzLaw` (`epsInf`, `amplitude`, `resonance`, `broadening`, `bandGap`, `abscissa : AbscissaKind`) and `GaussianOscillatorLaw` (`epsInf`, `amplitude`, `energy`, `broadening`, `abscissa : AbscissaKind`). Each has `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex`, whose body is its arm of `baseIndex` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:508-517`) moved verbatim over `x = this.abscissa.abscissaAt w`. (c) `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `TaucLorentzAxis of TaucLorentzLaw` and `GaussianOscillatorAxis of GaussianOscillatorLaw`. `complexIndex` calls the law, and the custom `Equals` / `GetHashCode` compare and hash both structurally. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs`: `TaucLorentzCoefficients` and `GaussianOscillatorCoefficients` gain `member toTaucLorentzLaw : TaucLorentzLaw` and `member toGaussianOscillatorLaw : GaussianOscillatorLaw`. Each copies the coefficients and takes `abscissa = AbscissaKind.ofUnit this.wavelengthUnit`. `thermoOptic` is not carried, because lowering stays isothermal: `evaluateAt` (`:552-559`) still adds the correction on top of `baseIndex`. `baseIndex`'s two arms answer the law's index, and their bodies are deleted there. `toEpsAxis` (`:766-769`) lowers `TaucLorentz c` to `TaucLorentzAxis c.toTaucLorentzLaw` and `GaussianOscillator c` to `GaussianOscillatorAxis c.toGaussianOscillatorLaw`; `ForouhiBloomer` and `BrendelBormann` still lower to the evaluated case until step 7. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`:427-435`) answers `[]` for both new cases. The doc comments of `baseIndex`, `toEpsAxis`, `toEpsValue` and `toOpticalProperties` (`:485-489`, `:669-686`, `:763-765`, `:793-812`) say that these two models lower to their law. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` `facetKey` (`:91-95`) maps both new cases to the existing `DiscreteKey \"Evaluated (transcendental)\"`, so `every DispersionModel kind lands on the vocabulary key its lowering denotes` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs:464-482`) stays green unchanged. `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats both as data that is not editable term data, as today. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `The Tauc-Lorentz law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap`, `The Tauc-Lorentz law over a micrometre abscissa reproduces its reference index` and `The Gaussian-oscillator law reproduces its reference index`. They build the laws directly in the core. The first and third use the Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian sets of `DispersionModelsTests.fs:306-326` over the electron-volt abscissa `ReciprocalInX { wavelengthScale = 1.0e-9<meter>; numerator = 1239.84 }`. The second uses a Tauc-Lorentz set over `LinearInX 1.0e-6<meter>` whose band gap lies between 0.3 µm and 2.0 µm. Each compares `complexIndex` at 300, 450, 600, 900 and 2000 nm, with exact `Assert.Equal`, against G17 literals the worker records from the start tree's `DispersionModel.evaluate` before moving the arms. In `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`:300-337`) matches each model's own law case where it matched `EpsAxisEvaluated _`, and `AC-B5 toEpsValue short-circuits ConstantNK and builds a single-segment tree otherwise` (`:380-382`) matches `TaucLorentzAxis _`. Their exact `Assert.Equal((f w).value, (axis.complexIndex w).value)` and 1e-12 assertions are unchanged, and their comments (`:302-305`, `:378-379`) no longer name `EpsAxisEvaluated`.", "acceptance": "After the two laws land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data` (red since step 4), with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B6 reference facts and LibraryFacetsTests unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the three new law facts equal to their literals; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Tauc-Lorentz law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Tauc-Lorentz law over a micrometre abscissa reproduces its reference index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Gaussian-oscillator law reproduces its reference index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.AC-B5 toEpsValue short-circuits ConstantNK and builds a single-segment tree otherwise", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 6, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1d", "red": "RED_0003", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [5], "how_to": "Red first, as in step 4, for the two remaining transcendental models (001 §B; .spec-md §3.1). Facts only. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` add `equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data`. Lowering `forouhiBloomerASi` and `brendelBormannGold` (`:403-430`) twice each, and lowering a separately built equal copy of each, MUST give equal `toEpsAxis` values with equal hashes and equal `toEpsValue` values. A copy whose `bandGap` (Forouhi-Bloomer) or first `broadening` (Brendel-Bormann) differs MUST lower to an unequal axis. The fact is red on the tree step 5 leaves: both models still lower to `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate`, which the custom equality compares by reference (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:386`).", "acceptance": "After the fact lands, constructor-unit-tests (DispersionModelsTests) MUST fail with exactly `equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data`, failing on the first equality of two lowered axes; every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 7, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1d", "closes": "RED_0003", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [6], "how_to": "The Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models become axis data, so no model lowers to the evaluated case (.spec-md §3.1). (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: `ForouhiBloomerLaw` (`nInf`, `a`, `b`, `c`, `bandGap`, `abscissa`) and `BrendelBormannLaw` (`plasmaFrequency`, `intrabandStrength`, `intrabandDamping`, then `strength`, `resonance`, `damping` and `broadening` as `float list`, then `abscissa`), marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]`. Each has a `complexIndex` whose body is its arm of `baseIndex` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:518-538`) moved verbatim over `this.abscissa.abscissaAt w`. Weideman's Faddeeva series (`faddeevaTermCount`, `FaddeevaSeries`, `faddeevaSeries` and `faddeeva`, `:437-483`) moves into `Dispersion.fs` beside `BrendelBormannLaw`, stays private there, and is deleted from the Domain. `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `ForouhiBloomerAxis of ForouhiBloomerLaw` and `BrendelBormannAxis of BrendelBormannLaw`, with `complexIndex`, `Equals` and `GetHashCode` arms as in step 5. (2) `DispersionModels.fs`: `ForouhiBloomerCoefficients.toForouhiBloomerLaw` and `BrendelBormannCoefficients.toBrendelBormannLaw`, built as step 5's members are. `baseIndex`'s two arms answer the law's index. `toEpsAxis` lowers both models to their cases, so its `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate` line (`:766-769`) is gone and every model lowers to data. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm answers `[]` for both cases. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` maps both cases to `DiscreteKey \"Evaluated (transcendental)\"`, and `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats both as data that is not editable term data. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `The Forouhi-Bloomer law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap` and `The Brendel-Bormann law reproduces its reference index`. They use the `forouhiBloomerASi` and `brendelBormannGold` sets (`DispersionModelsTests.fs:403-430`) over the electron-volt abscissa, at 300, 450, 600, 900 and 2000 nm, exact against G17 literals recorded from the pre-move `DispersionModel.evaluate`. Three arms that matched `EpsAxisEvaluated _` follow the law cases: `AC-B6 ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`DispersionModelsTests.fs:534-552`); `step 015: a transcendental dispersive segment derives and evaluates without rejection` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs:321-340`), which also asserts `Assert.False(c.isEditable)`, pinning the unchanged view-only behaviour; and `ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann are pickable and lower to the evaluated segment` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs:305-317`). Their other assertions are unchanged, and their comments no longer name `EpsAxisEvaluated`.", "acceptance": "After the two laws land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data` (red since step 6), with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B6 reference facts unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the two new law facts equal to their literals; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Forouhi-Bloomer law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Brendel-Bormann law reproduces its reference index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.AC-B6 ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.step 015: a transcendental dispersive segment derives and evaluates without rejection", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann are pickable and lower to the evaluated segment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 8, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.1e", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalProperties", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "The built-in Silicon and Langasite carry their dispersion as data. This section's brief does not name them, but their complexities hold `EpsAxisEvaluated` closures (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:455`, `:476-477`). Step 9 deletes that case, so they must become data first, and 001 §A ships them as catalogue files. Their indices are the engine's published closed forms (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs`), not finite term sums: Silicon's k is a ratio of polynomials, and Langasite's k is a Gaussian in λ. They become a closed set of published laws. The kernels MOVE into the core from `Dispersive.fs`, and the re-statements in `MaterialLibrary.fs` (`:422-447`) are deleted, so each closed form exists once. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: `PublishedIndexLaw` with `SiliconIndexLaw`, `LangasiteOrdinaryIndexLaw` and `LangasiteExtraordinaryIndexLaw`, with `member value : int` (1, 2, 3), `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : PublishedIndexLaw option` (`None` for any other tag) and `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex`. The arms of `complexIndex` are the closed forms of `Dispersive.fs` moved verbatim: Silicon's `nSi`, `xiSiFinal` and `refrIndexSi` (`:78-87`), and Langasite's `refrIndexLa3Ga5SiO14Ordinary` and `refrIndexLa3Ga5SiO14ExtraOrdinary` (`:27-37`, with `numberE = exp 1.0` from `:22`). `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `PublishedLawAxis of PublishedIndexLaw`, with `complexIndex`, `Equals` and `GetHashCode` arms. (2) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs`: `Silicon`'s eps is `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of `SiliconIndexLaw.complexIndex`, and its three lets are deleted. `Langasite`'s `epsLa3Ga5SiO14` (`:51-55`) reads the two Langasite laws. `g11La3Ga5SiO14` and `g33La3Ga5SiO14` (`:40-49`) read the real parts of the two laws' indices where they re-state those expressions, and the two index lets are deleted. Every preset number is unchanged, because the same expressions are evaluated. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `siliconComplexity` (`:453-458`) carries `PublishedLawAxis SiliconIndexLaw`, and `langasiteComplexity` (`:469-481`) carries `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteOrdinaryIndexLaw` and `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteExtraordinaryIndexLaw`. The private re-statements `siliconRefractionIndex`, `langasiteOrdinaryIndex` and `langasiteExtraordinaryIndex` (`:422-447`) are deleted. The coded-preset comment block (`:388-411`), the doc of `codedPresetInterval` (`:413-418`) and both complexities' docs (`:449-452`, `:460-468`) are rewritten: the dispersion is the published law the engine preset evaluates, and no closure remains, so the file no longer names `EpsAxisEvaluated`. (4) The matches follow the case. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:427-435`) answers `[]`. `facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:91-95`) answers `DiscreteKey \"Evaluated (transcendental)\"`, so Silicon's facet key is unchanged (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs:492`). `isEditable` treats the case as data that is not editable term data, so Silicon stays view-only (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs:480-484`). (5) Facts in `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs`: `The silicon published law reproduces the engine Silicon index` and `The langasite published laws reproduce the engine Langasite ordinary and extraordinary indices`. Each compares the law's `complexIndex` at 400, 500, 600, 800 and 1000 nm, with exact `Assert.Equal`, against G17 literals the worker records from the start tree's closures before moving them. Each also compares the engine preset's `getEps` (`siliconOpticalProperties` / `langasiteOpticalProperties`) with `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of those literals, through `MatrixComparison`. A third fact, `The published index law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag`, covers the tags. The constructor facts that pin Silicon and Langasite to the engine presets stay unchanged and green: `the silicon library entry reproduces the engine Silicon preset bit-for-bit` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs:48-55`) and `the re-seeded silicon and langasite eps reproduce the engine presets` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs:151-161`).", "acceptance": "After the published laws land, unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the three new facts and the laws equal to their literals; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, with the Silicon and Langasite reproduction facts and LibraryFacetsTests unchanged; ui-tests (MaterialsWindowTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The silicon published law reproduces the engine Silicon index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-PUBLISHED-LAWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The langasite published laws reproduce the engine Langasite ordinary and extraordinary indices", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-PUBLISHED-LAWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The published index law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-PUBLISHED-LAWS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 9, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.1f", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [2, 7, 8], "how_to": "`EpsAxisEvaluated` and the custom equality are deleted, so every axis is data and `EpsAxisDispersion` takes F#'s structural equality (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1, first row). After steps 2, 5, 7 and 8, nothing produces the case. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: delete `EpsAxisEvaluated` (`:369`), its `complexIndex` arm, `[<CustomEquality; NoComparison>]` (`:365`) and the `Equals` / `GetHashCode` overrides (`:380-394`). The doc comment above `RealNkFormulas` (`:346-356`) moves above `EpsAxisDispersion` and lists its data cases: term data (`RealNK`, `ComplexEps`), the tabulated table, the four oscillator laws and the published laws. (2) The dead arms are deleted: `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:433-435`), `facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:95`) and `isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:867`). `isEditable`'s predicate then reads: an axis is editable exactly when it is `RealNK` or `ComplexEps` term data. Every doc comment that names the evaluated closure is rewritten: `DispersionModels.fs`' module doc (`:10-23`) and the docs of `toEpsAxis`, `toEpsValue` and `toOpticalProperties`; `LibraryFacets.fs:82-90` and `:99-104`; and `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:854-863`. (3) The two out-of-band fixtures build a flat data axis where they built `EpsAxisEvaluated (fun _ -> …)`: `OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs:37-38` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs:52-53`. The axis is a constant `RealNK` with n = 1.5 and k = 0, because the diagnostic reads only the segment intervals. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `Equal axis data of every case is equal and hashes equal, and a changed value breaks equality`. For `RealNK`, `ComplexEps`, `TabulatedNK`, the four law cases and `PublishedLawAxis`, two separately built equal values MUST be equal with equal hashes, and changing one coefficient, sample or law MUST make them unequal. (5) Afterwards no file under `Berreman/` names `EpsAxisEvaluated`, in code or in a comment. S1.2's invariant `s02-no-eps-axis-evaluated` greps for it from S1.2's first step on.", "acceptance": "After the case is deleted, unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass with the structural-equality fact; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-tests (OutOfBandBadgeTests, MaterialEditorWindowTests, MaterialsWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.Equal axis data of every case is equal and hashes equal, and a changed value breaks equality", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-NO-CLOSURE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 10, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2a", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalProperties", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [8, 9], "how_to": "Langasite's dispersive gyration becomes data, so that the engine Langasite preset can be stated as a `MaterialComplexity` once step 13 derives `properties` from the complexity (001 §B 'Physics is pure data'; .spec-md §3.2). The section brief does not name it; the deviation is recorded in `.history`. `FsxAcceptanceTests` stores the engine preset itself as a library material (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:386`) and compares the table with `LangasiteOnSilicon.fsx`, whose film is that preset (`Berreman/Analytics/StandardSystems.fs:40-53`). `RhoWithDispValue` (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:RhoWithDispValue`) carries only `DispersionFormula` components, while the preset's ρ (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs:58-63`, `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14`) is diag(i·g₁₁(λ), 0, i·g₃₃(λ)) with the transcendental g₁₁ and g₃₃ of `:40-49`. The kernels MOVE into the core, as S1.1 step 8 moved the index laws, so one implementation exists. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, after `GyrotropicValue` and before `RhoWithDispValue`: `PublishedGyrationLaw`, a one-case union `LangasiteGyrationLaw` with `member value : int` = 1, `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : PublishedGyrationLaw option` (`None` for any other tag) and `member rhoAt (w : WaveLength) : Rho`. Its body is `g11La3Ga5SiO14`, `g33La3Ga5SiO14` and `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14` moved verbatim, reading the two Langasite `PublishedIndexLaw` cases as step 8 left those lets. `RhoWithDispValue` gains `PublishedLawRho of PublishedGyrationLaw`, and its doc names the case. (2) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Active.fs:146-156`: `toRhoWithDisp` answers `RhoWithDisp law.rhoAt` for the case, and its doc says so. (3) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs`: `Langasite`'s `rhoWithDisp` (`:70`) is `RhoWithDisp LangasiteGyrationLaw.rhoAt`, and the three lets are deleted. Every engine number is unchanged, because the same expressions are evaluated. (4) Every match follows the case. A published law is data the editor ladder cannot carry. `MaterialComplexityEditError` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:182-187`) gains `PublishedGyrationNotEditableErr of reason : string`. `ofComplexity`'s active arm answers it, naming the law, and its `caption` arm is added at `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:372-375`. `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:MaterialComplexity.isEditable`) answers false when the active aspect is a published law, so such an entry opens view-only. The gyration-class and handedness facets (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:materialGyrationClassDef`, `materialHandednessDef`) still apply to it but extract no value, because a published law has no editor class and no handedness field. `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs:164-167`) answers `allGyrationComponents` for it. (5) The built-in Langasite keeps the constant uniaxial gyration its seed carries, so no library number moves. The doc of `langasiteComplexity` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:langasiteComplexity`) says so and names the published law as the engine preset's ρ. The comment at `OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs:464-469` no longer says the ρ has no value-tree form. (6) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs` gains two. `The langasite gyration law reproduces the engine Langasite rho`: at 400, 500, 600, 800 and 1000 nm, Im ρ₁₁ and Im ρ₃₃ of `LangasiteGyrationLaw.rhoAt` MUST equal, with exact `Assert.Equal`, G17 literals the worker records from `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14` before moving it; every other entry and every real part MUST be zero; and `(PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw).toRhoWithDisp.getRho w` and `langasiteOpticalProperties.rhoWithDisp.getRho w` MUST equal `rhoAt w` through `MatrixComparison`. `The published gyration law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag` covers the tag. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law keeps a complexity view-only and refuses to seed the editor`: for a constant isotropic eps with `active = Some (PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw)`, `isEditable` MUST be false and `ofComplexity` MUST be `Error (PublishedGyrationNotEditableErr _)`. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law offers the activity facets but extracts no class or handedness`, over an entry built by `materialEntryWith` (`:85-93`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law opens the editor view-only`: `initMaterialEditor` over such an entry MUST give `ViewOnlyMaterial _`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law draws every gyration component`: `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` of that complexity MUST equal `allGyrationComponents`.", "acceptance": "After the gyration law lands, unit-tests (RhoWithDispValueTests, EpsWithDispValueTests) MUST pass with the two new facts and the law equal to its literals; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with the MaterialComplexityTests and LibraryFacetsTests facts; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests, NkDispersionChartTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass with the two new facts and both LangasiteOnSilicon facts; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalProperties/Active.fs", "Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests.The langasite gyration law reproduces the engine Langasite rho", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests.The published gyration law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a published gyration law keeps a complexity view-only and refuses to seed the editor", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests.a published gyration law offers the activity facets but extracts no class or handedness", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a published gyration law opens the editor view-only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.a published gyration law draws every gyration component", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "Berreman.Dispersion.RhoWithDispValue", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialComplexityEditor.MaterialComplexityEditError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 11, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [10], "how_to": "Every place that builds a `MaterialEntry` from engine properties states its physics as `MaterialComplexity` data first, while `properties` is still a field (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`). The script comparisons then prove that no number moves before step 13 changes the record (.spec-md §3.2). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`: `material` (`:85-88`) takes a `MaterialComplexity` and saves `properties = complexity.toProperties` with the complexity. Each caller passes the script's material as data, and the script side keeps the script's own properties. `constantN 1.78052` (`:273`) becomes `EpsWithoutDispValue (IsotropicTransparent (RefractionIndex 1.78052))`. `dispersiveGlass` (`:357`; the script's n² = 1 + Σ bᵢλ²/(λ² − cᵢ) in µm, `:344-353`) becomes one isotropic dispersive segment over 300–700 nm whose axis is the Domain Sellmeier lowering `(Sellmeier { b = [ 1.43; 0.65 ]; c = [ 0.073 * 0.073; 0.12 * 0.12 ]; wavelengthUnit = Micrometer; thermoOptic = None }).toEpsAxis` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:DispersionModel.toEpsAxis`). `langasiteOpticalProperties` (`:386`) becomes one uniaxial dispersive segment over 250–600 nm with `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteOrdinaryIndexLaw` and `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteExtraordinaryIndexLaw`, and `active = Some (PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw)` (step 10). `siliconOpticalProperties` (`:387`) becomes one isotropic dispersive segment over 250–600 nm with `PublishedLawAxis SiliconIndexLaw`. The glasses and the vacuum spacer (`:410-411`, `:442-443`) become `IsotropicTransparent` of `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass`, `RefractionIndex.vacuum`, `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass175` and `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass150`. For the EUV layers, `euvStack`, `euvAgainstIncidence` and `euvAgainstWaveLength` (`:477-509`) take each layer as a `ComplexRefractionIndex`. The table stores `IsotropicAbsorbing` of it, and the script's system builds it as the scripts do: `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex`, then `OpticalProperties.fromEpsion` (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Standard.fs:91`, `:110`). The EUV.fsx facts pass 1 − δ + iβ from `Eps.euvMolybdenumDelta` / `Eps.euvMolybdenumBeta` and `Eps.euvSiliconDelta` / `Eps.euvSiliconBeta`, and the EUV__002 facts pass their own (0.100, 0.045) and (0.006, 0.002); `euvComplex` (`:492-494`) is deleted. Every magnetic aspect is `None`, and so is every active aspect except Langasite's. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `a minted MaterialId round-trips create-store-lookup through the library` (`:141-160`): the entry carries a constant `IsotropicTransparent (RefractionIndex 1.5)` complexity with `properties = complexity.toProperties`. The lookup assertion compares the resolved `getEps` at 400, 600 and 800 nm with the complexity's own, through the file's `epsClose 1e-12` (`:28`), not by reference, because step 13 derives `properties` on every read. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs`: `vacuumProperties` (`:46-56`) becomes `vacuumPlaceholderComplexity : MaterialComplexity` = `{ eps = EpsWithoutDispValue (IsotropicAbsorbing (ComplexRefractionIndex (Complex.create 1.0 0.0))); magnetic = None; active = None }`. Its composition is the same `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of 1 + 0i under the vacuum μ and ρ. `dtoToEntry` (`:93-111`) sets `properties` from it and carries it as the complexity, and the 'view-only until the §D.9 mapping lands' comment (`:106-107`) is deleted. Such an entry is now vacuum term data, editable like any constant material. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs` gains `a metadata-only library file re-imports each entry as vacuum data`. It exports the described `builtInEntries` (filtered as `:96-98` filters them) to a file under the test run's output directory and re-imports it; every imported entry's `complexity` MUST equal the vacuum value of (3).", "acceptance": "After every fixture states its physics as data, ui-tests (FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass, with every script comparison within its 1e-6 tolerance; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with the new ExportImportTests fact and the reworked minted-id fact; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExportImportTests.a metadata-only library file re-imports each entry as vacuum data", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExportImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-DATA-FIXTURES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.a minted MaterialId round-trips create-store-lookup through the library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-DATA-FIXTURES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 12, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "The view-only Edit gating of the domain-free materials control is deleted, with nothing replacing it (.spec-md §3.2). Its stated purpose was the `complexity = None` built-ins (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/MaterialsControls.fs:27-29`), and no product view hosts the control: `materialsControlsView` is mounted only by `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs:154` and `:190`. The Materials window keeps its own gate, `MaterialsWindowModel.editableSelection` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs:258-264`), which reads `MaterialComplexity.isEditable`. (1) `MaterialsControls.fs`: delete `MaterialEditability` (`:32-36`) and `MaterialsControlsRow.editability` (`:44`). `verbRow` (`:213-235`) always lists the Edit verb, offered on a selection exactly as Remove and View are. The module doc's view-only sentences (`:27-29`) and `verbRow`'s doc clause on Edit (`:213-215`) are deleted. The verb row's membership no longer changes, so `verbButton` drops `withKey` and its comment (`:157-159`). (2) `MaterialsControlsTests.fs`: `knownRows` (`:26-33`) lose `editability`, and their doc loses the view-only row; `matchesId`'s doc (`:20-22`) loses the Edit-removal example. The fact `a view-only selection carries no Edit affordance — the button is removed, not greyed` (`:183-201`) becomes `every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial`: with the silicon row selected, the Edit verb MUST be present and a click on it MUST record the edit handler's tag, as `recorder` (`:60`) records the others.", "acceptance": "After the gating is deleted, ui-smoke MUST pass with `every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial` in place of the view-only fact; ui-tests (MaterialsControlsTests) MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/MaterialsControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "migrate", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests.a view-only selection carries no Edit affordance — the button is removed, not greyed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests.every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial", "obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.MaterialsControls.MaterialEditability", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"], "preserves_obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.MaterialsControls.MaterialsControlsRow.editability", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"], "preserves_obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 13, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [10, 11, 12], "how_to": "`MaterialEntry.complexity` becomes mandatory, and `properties` becomes a member computed from it (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1 'MaterialLibrary.fs' row, §3.2). After steps 10 and 11 every construction already sets `properties = complexity.toProperties` with a present complexity. The record and all its consumers change in this one step, so the build stays green. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`: the field `properties` is deleted, and `complexity : MaterialComplexity` replaces the option. The record gains `member this.properties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp = this.complexity.toProperties`, so its readers (`resolveMaterialWithDisp`, `MaterialEntry.dispersion`, `Propagation.fs`, the views and the tests) keep compiling unchanged. Its doc says the complexity is the entry's physics and `properties` its engine composition. `builtInEntries` drops each `properties = …` line and each `Some`. Every field is now data, so `MaterialEntry` gains F#'s structural equality. (2) Every other construction drops `properties = …` and `Some`: `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs` (`entryFromTabulated`, `entryOfAxis`), `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs` `dtoToEntry` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs` `entryUnder` (`:416-424`). So do the fixtures: `LibraryFacetsTests.fs` `materialEntryWith`, the dispersive fixture of `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs` `dispersiveMaterial` (`:64-72`), the minted-id fact of `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` `material` and the step-10 fact of `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`. The copy-and-updates `MaterialProxyTests.fs:52` and `SampleProxyTests.fs:487` keep only `complexity = …`. (3) Every reader of the option reads the value, and every `None` arm that stood for a coded, view-only preset is deleted with nothing replacing it. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs`: `payloadOf` (`:76-80`) is `VersionPayload<MaterialComplexity, MaterialMetadata>` and compares the complexity directly, and the `MaterialMetadata` doc (`:28-34`) drops its coded-preset sentences. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs`: the four private entry members (`constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt`, `magneticOpt`) and the anisotropy facet read `entry.complexity`, and the anisotropy doc's defensive-`None` sentence goes. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:84-90`: `ofEntry` is `ReachableMaterial.definedSegmentsOf entry.complexity`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs`: `previewAnisotropy` (`:101-110`) is deleted, and its callers `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs:1114` and `:1151` read `shownEntry.complexity.anisotropy`. The docs that describe the coded-preset fallback or name `previewAnisotropy` (`NkDispersionChart.fs:156-163`, `:170-175`, `:208-211`; `MaterialEditorView.fs:266-270`) are rewritten: every component is drawn when a complexity names no gyration class. `MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `editableSelection` (`:253-264`) and the view panel's editability (`:1115-1120`) read `isEditable` off the complexity, and the caption ` (view-only engine preset)` becomes ` (view-only)`. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:MaterialComplexity.isEditable`: its doc no longer contrasts the gate with complexity presence. (4) `MaterialEditorView.fs`: the view-only case carries the complexity it shows, `ViewOnlyMaterial of reason : ControlCaption * shown : MaterialComplexity` (`:64-69`). The fields `presetProperties` and `viewOnlyComplexity` (`:147-152`) are deleted. `previewProperties`, `previewGyrationComponents` and `previewMuKind` (`:256-290`) read `shown`, so their `None` arms go. `initMaterialEditor` (`:321-387`) seeds an editable entry through `ofComplexity`, whose `Error e` gives `ViewOnlyMaterial (e.caption, entry.complexity)`. Any other entry opens as `ViewOnlyMaterial (ControlCaption \"this entry's physics is not editable term data — view-only\", entry.complexity)`. The binders at `:411` and `:1289` take `(reason, _)`, and `complexitySummary`'s view-only caption (`:295`) becomes `view-only`. The module doc (`:1-20`), the `EditorMode` doc (`:64-66`) and the inline comments (`:360-363`, `:373-375`) describe the view-only case as a complexity that is not editable term data, and so does `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs:12-19`. (5) Test readers follow: `MaterialComplexityTests.fs` `AC-B7 every re-expressed built-in's toProperties reproduces the original preset at reference wavelengths`; `MaterialImportTests.fs` `assertEditableDispersive`, `formula 2 segment carries the page's wavelength_range in µm` and the facts S1.1 steps 1 and 2 added, which now match the record itself; `LibraryFacetsTests.fs` `anisotropyOf reads the re-seeded coded presets from data`; and `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs` `a coded-preset material (spectrum-spanning band) never flags`, which drops its option match and its comment's former-`None` clause. In `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `ofComplexity round-trips the editable built-ins value-identically through toComplexity`, `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry` and the two Save facts read the value. (6) Two facts lose their subject and are deleted. `every built-in carries Some complexity after the step-004 re-seed` (`MaterialComplexityTests.fs:132-148`) is now guaranteed by the type. `spec 0040 006: a coded preset with no stored tree still renders all components` (`MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs:1053-1064`) needs an entry without a complexity, which no longer exists; the view-only class restriction stays covered by `spec 0040 006: a view-only entry reads the class off its stored complexity tree — Langasite carries g₁₁ / g₃₃`. Three facts are renamed because their names state the option: `Save adds a NEW material with complexity Some, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing` becomes `Save adds a NEW material with its complexity, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing`; `acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with complexity Some` becomes `acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with its complexity`; and `a complexity-less entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder` becomes `a non-editable entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder`. (7) In every file this step edits, each comment and failure message that says `complexity = None`, `complexity = Some` or `Some complexity` is rewritten or deleted.", "acceptance": "After `complexity` becomes mandatory, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, one fact fewer for the deleted MaterialComplexityTests fact; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests, MaterialsWindowTests, NkDispersionChartTests, OutOfBandBadgeTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass, one fact fewer for the deleted coded-preset fact and with the renamed Save fact; ui-smoke MUST pass with the two renamed facts; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.every built-in carries Some complexity after the step-004 re-seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.spec 0040 006: a coded preset with no stored tree still renders all components", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.Save adds a NEW material with complexity Some, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.Save adds a NEW material with its complexity, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with complexity Some", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with its complexity", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a complexity-less entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a non-editable entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialEntry.complexity", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialEditorView.EditorMode", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.NkDispersionChart.previewAnisotropy", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 14, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [13], "how_to": "The last mentions of the optional complexity go, so `git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing; from S1.3's first step its invariant `s03-complexity-mandatory` runs that grep after every step. No code changes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs:459` and `:480`: the comments say Silicon is view-only because its complexity is not editable term data. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs`: `siliconEntry`'s doc (`:27`) says Silicon's dispersion is the published silicon law. `spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components for a coded preset with no stored class` (`:194-200`) is renamed `spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components when every component is requested`, and its comment no longer names a coded preset; its assertions are unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj:120-124`: the existing comment ends at 'Save round-trips through MaterialProxy'. No comment is added.", "acceptance": "After the sweep, ui-tests MUST pass over every class the test project compiles, because the step edits its project file, with the renamed NkDispersionChartTests fact; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMovementTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FacetedTreeControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RayPositionControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererTestTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RotationControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToBeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToReflectedTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components for a coded preset with no stored class", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components when every component is requested", "obligations": ["S12-SWEEP"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 15, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "One place names each built-in identity (.spec-md §3.3; 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'). This step moves the identity literals into two well-known id modules and deletes the Ui's `SeedEntryIds`. The preset ids keep their current text until step 20 mints their GUIDs, so every value and every fact is unchanged here. `SeedEntryIds` goes in the same step that adds `PresetIds`, because their shared names (`source600`, `detectorIntensity`, `polarizerLp`, `polarizerCpLeft`, `polarizerCpRight`) may not coexist (ELEV015). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, module `Library`, directly after `newSampleId` (`:47`): add `module SampleIds` and `module PresetIds`, plain modules shaped like `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:50-62`): no `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]`, no `[<Literal>]`, every member a typed value. They sit here and not in `MaterialLibrary.fs` because `SampleId` is declared at `:36` and this file compiles after `MaterialLibrary.fs`; `MaterialIds` and `CategoryIds` stay where they are. (a) `SampleIds` holds eleven `SampleId` values whose literals MOVE out of `SeedSamples` (each `id = Guid.Parse \"…\" |> SampleId` at `:655`, `:665`, `:675`, `:685`, `:695`, `:705`, `:732`, `:758`, `:768`, `:778`, `:788`): `glassPlate1mmId`, `glassPlate2mmId`, `glassFilm600Id`, `glassVacuumId`, `glassFilm200Id`, `multilayerQwId`, `euvMoSiId`, `uniaxialId`, `biaxialId`, `activeCrystalPlateId` and `langasiteSiliconId`. The `Id` suffix keeps each public name unique beside the same-named `SeedSamples` value (ELEV015), which S1.7 deletes. Each `SeedSamples` record reads its member (`id = SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId`). (b) `PresetIds` holds 33 `ElementValueId` values, one per seeded preset, each written `ElementValueId \"<its current id>\"`: `source600` src-600; the `lasers` (`:832-846`) `heNe633` src-hene-633, `heNe543` src-hene-543, `argon488` src-ar-488, `argon515` src-ar-515, `heCd442` src-hecd-442, `heCd325` src-hecd-325, `diode405` src-diode-405, `ruby694` src-ruby-694, `tiSapphire800` src-tisa-800, `ndYag1064` src-ndyag-1064, `ndYag532` src-ndyag-532, `ndYag355` src-ndyag-355, `ndYag266` src-ndyag-266, `erbium1550` src-er-1550, `co2Laser10600` src-co2-10600; the `lithography` sources (`:853-860`) `mercuryG436` src-hg-g-436, `mercuryH405` src-hg-h-405, `mercuryI365` src-hg-i-365, `krf248` src-krf-248, `arf193` src-arf-193, `f2Excimer157` src-f2-157, `euv13p5` src-euv-13p5, `beuv6p7` src-beuv-6p7; the `tunables` (`:867-870`) `xenonMonochromator` src-xe-mono, `tiSapphireTunable` src-tisa-tunable, `supercontinuum` src-supercontinuum, `euvBeamline` src-euv-beamline; and (`:887-891`) `detectorIntensity` det-intensity, `detectorEllipsometer` det-ellipsometer, `polarizerLp` pol-lp, `polarizerCpLeft` pol-cp-left and `polarizerCpRight` pol-cp-right. `SeedSources` passes the members to `source` and `tunable` (`:827-870`); `seedEntries`' five detector and polarizer records (`:887-891`) and `seedTrees`' five detector and polarizer leaves (`:954-962`) read them, so each id is written once. (c) Docs, one to three lines each: `PresetIds` is the frozen identity of every seeded light-source, detector and polarizer preset, the one place a built-in preset's entry id is written (spec 0050 §3.3); `SampleIds` is the frozen identity of every seeded sample. `SampleId`'s doc (`:31-35`) and the `SeedSamples` doc (`:646-650`) say the fixed literals live in `SampleIds`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`, `detectorKindOf`'s doc (`:23-27`): the intensity and ellipsometer presets are named `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` / `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`, not by their id text. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `module SeedEntryIds` and its doc (`:985-1000`) are deleted. `CatalogueKind.defaultSeedEntry` (`:1009-1014`) returns `Some Library.PresetIds.source600`, `detectorIntensity`, `polarizerLp` and `polarizerCpLeft`, and its doc's `pol-cp-right` (`:1008`) reads `PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. `paletteButtons`' CPL and CPR prebinds (`:2052-2053`) are `Some Library.PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft` and `Some Library.PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. (4) The four test files that named `SeedEntryIds` read `PresetIds`, and every other seeded preset id in them switches too, comments included. A fixture holds a preset or sample id as an `ElementValueId`, and a helper that wrapped a `string` id takes the `ElementValueId`, so no fixture re-wraps `.value` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin', which holds for fixtures). (a) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainSceneMsgTests.fs`: the theory `AddElement lands PRE-BOUND to the kind's seeded default entry` (`:108-121`) cannot take a member through `InlineData`, so its rows carry the kind code only (\"S\", \"D\", \"LP\", \"CP\") and a private `expectedSeedOf (code : string) : ElementValueId` maps each code to its member; its name, its four rows and its assertions are unchanged. `AddElementBoundTo carries an explicit pre-bind — the CPR palette button's path` (`:135-140`), the palette fact (`:151-153`) and the detector binds (`:479-496`, `:587-593`) read the members. (b) `TableAndElementRotationTests.fs:532`: the expected prebinds are `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`, `Some PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft` and `Some PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. (c) `ExperimentControlsTests.fs`: `bind` (`:31-32`) takes `entryId : ElementValueId`; `glassFilm200Id`, `glassFilm600Id`, `glassPlate1mmId` and `euvMirrorId` (`:40-47`) hold the sample's `entryId` itself, and `BindValueId (ElementValueId glassFilm200Id)` (`:631`) passes `glassFilm200Id`. `withTunableSource` (`:36`) binds `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`, `:109` binds `PresetIds.heNe633` and `:280` binds `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`; `:308` and `:347` read the members, and the comments at `:307`, `:308` and `:318` name them. (d) `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`: `TableRun.sourceEntry` becomes an `ElementValueId`; `tableRun`'s `source` parameter follows, and `userSource` returns the `ElementValueId` it saves. `runOnTable` binds `run.sourceEntry` and `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` directly; `glassOnTable` and the two 600 nm runs pass `PresetIds.source600`; `xenon` is `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `euvAgainstWaveLength` passes `PresetIds.euvBeamline`. Its test-local user source \"src-test-10nm\" stays.", "acceptance": "After the identities move, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke and ui-tests over the selected classes MUST pass with unchanged counts and every fact holding its assertion, the theory `AddElement lands PRE-BOUND to the kind's seeded default entry` keeping its four rows; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainSceneMsgTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 16, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [15], "how_to": "The constructor suite names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text, so every fact keeps its meaning and its result. Every occurrence in the files below, comments included, switches. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests` lists only ids that are not seeded presets, and they stay: the test-local user sources of `SourceLibraryTests.fs` (\"src-user-1\", \"src-a\", \"src-b\", \"src-c\", \"src-user-krf\"), the tunable fixture \"src-t\" (`ExperimentRunTests.fs:79`), and the `SourceSpecId`s of `EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs:64` and `:106` and `SourceProjectionTests.fs:25`, which name spectral source specs (`SourceSpec.fs:243`), not Library presets. A fixture holds an id as an `ElementValueId` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). (1) `ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs:46-48`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs:56-60` and `:76-79`, and `ExperimentProxyTests.fs:38-39`, `:197-219`, `:238`, `:338` and `:365`: each `BoundByEntryId (ElementValueId \"…\")` is `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.source600`, `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.polarizerLp` or `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.detectorIntensity`. (2) `LibraryProxyTests.fs`, `tryGetEntry hits a known id and misses an unknown id` (`:63-69`): it looks up `PresetIds.source600` and asserts `Assert.Equal(PresetIds.source600, s.id)`; the unknown id \"no-such-id\" stays. (3) `PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs`: `entry` (`:25-28`) and `bind` (`:67-68`) take an `ElementValueId`; `mirrorId`, `thinFilmId` and `plateId` (`:31-35`) hold the sample's `entryId`, and `sourceId` (`:37`) is `PresetIds.source600`. (4) `PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs`: the expected protected ids (`:140-143`) are the `.value` of the five detector and polarizer members plus the seeded sources' ids, sorted as today. `polarizer` (`:147-152`) and `extractedLabels` (`:173-177`) take an `ElementValueId` and compare ids, and their callers (`:153-158`, `:178-180`) pass the members. (5) `SceneProxyTests.fs:32` and `SceneRoundTripTests.fs:32`, `:38` and `:105`: `Some PresetIds.source600` and `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`. (6) `SourceLibraryTests.fs`: `wavelengthOf` (`:38`) takes an `ElementValueId`, and its seven checks (`:39-45`) read `PresetIds.source600`, `heNe633`, `ndYag1064`, `mercuryI365`, `krf248`, `arf193` and `euv13p5`; the live-Library fact's detector (`:114`) is `PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, in its record and in the lookup.", "acceptance": "After the switch, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with an unchanged count, every fact of ExperimentCollectionProxyTests, ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests, ExperimentProxyTests, LibraryProxyTests, PlacedSampleEmissionTests, PolarizerBehaviorTests, SceneProxyTests, SceneRoundTripTests and SourceLibraryTests holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 17, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [15], "how_to": "`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs` names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text, so every fact keeps its result. Every occurrence, comments included, switches; afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs` finds nothing. (1) Each `ElementValueId \"src-600\"`, `\"pol-lp\"`, `\"pol-cp-left\"`, `\"det-intensity\"` and `\"det-ellipsometer\"` is its member, inside `ConstructorUiId.libraryEntryNode`, `.libraryEntryCode`, `SelectLibraryEntry` and `SelectLibraryEntryNode` as well. (2) Text compared with `filteredEntryIds` (`:227-228`) or with the `onSelected` recorder (`:214`) is built from the member: `PresetIds.source600.value` (`:437`, `:623`), `PresetIds.polarizerLp.value` (`:447`), `[ PresetIds.polarizerLp.value ]` (`:1080`), and `\"selected:\" + PresetIds.detectorIntensity.value` (`:1102`, `:1106`) or `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer.value` (`:1151`). The two lists the facts sort (`:1072-1074`, `:1143-1145`) are written `List.sort [ PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft.value; PresetIds.polarizerCpRight.value ]` and `List.sort [ PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer.value; PresetIds.detectorIntensity.value ]`, so they hold whatever the ids spell. (3) The id-format facts build their expected text from the member: `\"FacetTreeNode_entry:\" + PresetIds.source600.value` (`:251`) and `\"branch:\" + entryKindFacetKey.value + \":Source:entry:\" + PresetIds.source600.value` (`:369-371`). (4) The Select-bay rows (`:1372`, `:1383`) are `ConstructorUiId.libraryEntry PresetIds.detectorIntensity.uiKey`, the key the bay gives its leaf rows (`ElementValueId.uiKey`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:28`).", "acceptance": "After the switch, ui-tests (LibraryWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass with unchanged counts, every fact holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 18, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [15], "how_to": "The rest of the UI suite names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text. Every occurrence in the files below, comments included, switches. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` lists only test-local ids, which stay: the user sources \"src-new-1\", \"src-x\", \"src-y\", \"src-u\", \"src-mine\" and \"src-typed\" of `LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, \"src-x\" of `ScrollExtentTests.fs:149`, \"src-test-10nm\" of `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` and \"src-tune\" of `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs:289-292`. A fixture holds an id as an `ElementValueId`, and a helper that wrapped a `string` id takes the `ElementValueId` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). (1) `ElementRendererBindingTests.fs`: `drawableOf` (`:26-27`) takes `valueId : ElementValueId option`; `stateOf` (`:63-64`) follows, wrapping its test-local ids where it writes them (`Some (ElementValueId \"lib:sample\")`); the HideNormals fact (`:92`) draws `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`. (2) `InverseConstructorTests.fs:155`: `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`. (3) `LightSourceEditorTests.fs:173`: `PresetIds.euv13p5`; `:210`: `PresetIds.arf193`. (4) `SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`: `baseExperiment` (`:61`) takes `srcBind : ElementValueId option` and `detBind : ElementValueId option`, `bindOne` binds the id it receives, and every call (`:134-259`) passes `Some PresetIds.source600` with `Some PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, or `Some PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer` at `:182`. (5) `WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:253-261` and `WireUiCompositionTests.fs:197`: `ConstructorUiId.libraryEntryNode PresetIds.source600`, `PresetIds.polarizerLp` and `PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft`. (6) `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs`: `bind` (`:40`) and `filmOnR2` (`:158`) take an `ElementValueId`; `glassFilm200Id` and `glassPlate1mmId` (`:41-42`) hold the sample's `entryId`; the binds and lookups read `PresetIds.heNe633` (`:68`, `:123-125`, `:176`, `:185`), `arf193` (`:79`), `krf248` (`:137`, `:150`), `xenonMonochromator` (`:167`, `:184`), `source600` (`:190`, `:254`), `detectorEllipsometer` (`:202`) and `detectorIntensity` (`:129`).", "acceptance": "After the switch, ui-tests (ElementRendererBindingTests, InverseConstructorTests, LightSourceEditorTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests) and ui-smoke, which holds WireUi0040CompositionTests and WireUiCompositionTests, MUST pass with unchanged counts, every fact holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementRendererBindingTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 19, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.3e", "red": "RED_0004", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [16, 18], "how_to": "Red first for 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash' (.spec-md §3.3): every seeded entry id, and every minted source id, is the canonical string of a GUID. Facts only; no production file changes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs`, beside the seeded-sources facts: (a) `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal`: for every entry of `seedEntries`, `Guid.TryParse e.entryId.value` succeeds (matched, never `.IsSome`) and the parsed GUID's `string` equals `e.entryId.value`, the lowercase hyphenated form `SampleId.toElementValueId` writes (`ElementId.fs:43`); and the ids are distinct. The samples pass; it fails today on the presets' text ids. (b) `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`: two `newSourceId ()` calls each parse as a GUID whose `string` equals the id, and the two differ. It fails today on the `src-` prefix (`ElementId.fs:594`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id` (`:144-149`): its name and its first two assertions stay; `Assert.StartsWith(\"source-add:src-\", calls.[0])` becomes: `calls.[0]` starts with `source-add:` and the rest is the canonical string of a GUID. It fails today.", "acceptance": "After the facts land, constructor-unit-tests (SourceLibraryTests) MUST fail with exactly `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal` and `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`, every other SourceLibraryTests fact passing; ui-tests (LightSourceEditorTests) MUST fail with exactly `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id`, every other LightSourceEditorTests fact passing; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests"]}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests.every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests.newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests.Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 20, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.3e", "closes": "RED_0004", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [19], "how_to": "Every seeded preset gets its frozen GUID, and a new user source is a plain GUID (.spec-md §3.3; 001 §B). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, `PresetIds`: the text of each of the 33 members becomes a GUID minted once while implementing (`[guid]::NewGuid()`), written `ElementValueId \"<guid>\"` in the lowercase hyphenated form a `Guid`'s `string` prints. No two are equal, and none equals a `MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds` or `SampleIds` literal. From this step the literals are frozen: S1.5 exports them byte-for-byte. (2) `newSourceId` (`:592-594`) mints `ElementValueId (string (Guid.NewGuid ()))`; its doc says the id is a plain GUID string, as a sample's is (`SampleId.toElementValueId`, `:43`). (3) `LibraryEntry.entryId`'s doc (`:355-356`) says every entry id is the string of a GUID: a sample's `SampleId`, a preset's `PresetIds` member, a user source's minted id. `liveLibrary` (`:1130-1168`) keeps its code: its `Guid.TryParse` probe (`:1159`) now parses a preset id too, finds no sample (`SampleStore.fs:119` answers `Ok None` for an unknown id) and falls through to the presets. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs` gains `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`: over `liveLibrary (createInMemory ()) samples sources`, with a user source saved under `newSourceId ()` and a sample saved under `newSampleId ()`, `tryGetEntry` returns the ellipsometer detector for `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`, the user source for its id and the sample for `toElementValueId` of its id, and `Ok None` for a fresh GUID that names nothing. (5) No product ordering changes. A fact that fails only because it relied on the old ids' alphabetical order compares order-independently, with its assertion otherwise unchanged. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"` finds nothing; from S1.4's first step its invariant `s04-no-seeded-string-preset-ids` runs that grep after every step.", "acceptance": "After the GUIDs are minted, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal` and `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`, which step 19 left red, and `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`; ui-tests over the selected classes MUST pass, including `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id`; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMovementTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FacetedTreeControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RayPositionControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererTestTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RotationControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToBeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToReflectedTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests.the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 21, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [20], "how_to": "One serializer options value, owned by a new canonical-JSON module (001 §B: the System.Text.Json + FSharp.SystemTextJson + JsonSchema.Net stack in `ProjectJson` is REUSED; .spec-md §5 'Canonical JSON + SHA-256', §6 'JSON + schema'). This step is a MOVE and changes no output. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`, `module CanonicalJson` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `SchemaValidation.fs` and before `ProjectJson.fs` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:22-23`): one `<Compile Include=\"CanonicalJson.fs\" />` line and no new comment. `ProjectJson.options` (`ProjectJson.fs:125-145`) and its five private converters (`BeamBranchConverter`, `RotationLockConverter`, `BeamPresenceConverter`, `ToggleStateConverter`, `ComplexMatrixConverter`, `ProjectJson.fs:24-123`) MOVE there verbatim. Their docs say that this is the one options value every JSON store of the app reads. They are deleted from `ProjectJson.fs`, whose `parseProject` and `serializeProject` (`:158-182`) now read `CanonicalJson.options`; any `open` that is no longer used goes. (2) Every other reader re-points, with no other change: `GroupsLibrary.fs` (`:82`, `:90`, `:93`), `RecentFiles.fs` (`:55`, `:70`), the three reads in `Report.fs` module `MaterialLibrary` (`importMaterials` / `exportMaterials`), `OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs` (`:367`, `:377`, `:380`) and `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` (`AC-D8 only dndT and referenceTemperature persist through JSON (operating T unstored)`). The inventory's census of `ProjectJson.options` is exactly these files and `ProjectJson.fs`. (3) Every comment that names the moved value or one of its converters names `CanonicalJson` instead: `GroupsLibrary.fs:17` and `:86`, `RecentFiles.fs:12`, the two `Report.fs` docs that name the shared options, `UserEnvironment.fs:13`, `:141`, `:250` and `:373`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui/Localization.fs:39`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Groups.fs:16`, `:23` and `:123`, and `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Placement.fs:279`. No other comment is swept. Afterwards `git grep -n -F \"ProjectJson.options\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing. No converter is added and no option changes, so every existing JSON round-trip fact (`ProjectJsonRoundtripTests`, `RoundTripTests`, `GroupsRoundTripTests`, `EnvironmentRoundTripTests`, `ExportImportTests`, `DispersionModelsTests`) passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the move, `CanonicalJson.options` MUST be the only serializer options value, with nothing under Berreman/ naming `ProjectJson.options`, and every existing JSON round-trip fact MUST pass unchanged; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, the selected ui-tests classes and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/GroupsLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/Localization.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Groups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Placement.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 22, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.4b", "red": "RED_0005", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [21], "how_to": "Red first: two kinds of number that the shared options cannot carry and that entry files hold (001 §B: 'Any entry that cannot serialise is a test failure'). Facts only; no production file changes. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs`: `module CanonicalJsonTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended to `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list after `PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs`, with no new comment. It holds three facts over `CanonicalJson.options` (step 21). (1) `a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts`: `Complex(1.5, -0.25)` serialized and read back is equal, and its JSON is a two-element number array. It is red today, because System.Text.Json writes `Real`, `Imaginary`, `Magnitude` and `Phase` and reads back zero. (2) `a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows`: the Mueller matrix `Propagation.analyzerMueller IdealLinear` at 30° (built as `PolarizerBehaviorTests` builds `lp0`), serialized and read back, is equal element for element, with bit-identical doubles, and its JSON is four arrays of four numbers. It is red today, because reading `Matrix<double>` throws `NotSupportedException` (an abstract type): only `Matrix<Complex>` has a converter. (3) `an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options`: the complexity of the `builtInEntries` entry `MaterialIds.euvMolybdenum` (an `IsotropicAbsorbing` complex index) serialized and read back is equal. It is red today for the reason of (1). No fact catches an exception: a throw is the failure.", "acceptance": "After the facts land, constructor-unit-tests (CanonicalJsonTests) MUST fail with exactly `a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts`, `a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows` and `an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options`, the class's only facts; and build, elevation and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-NUMBERS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-NUMBERS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-NUMBERS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 23, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.4b", "closes": "RED_0005", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage"], "depends_on": [22], "how_to": "`CanonicalJson.options` gains two converters (001 §B; .spec-md §5). They sit beside `ComplexMatrixConverter` and are written as it is: private `JsonConverter` classes, registered before the `JsonFSharpConverter`. (1) `ComplexConverter` writes a `System.Numerics.Complex` as `[re, im]` and reads that pair back. (2) `RealMatrixConverter` writes a MathNet `Matrix<double>` as an array of rows and reads it back through `Matrix<double>.Build.DenseOfArray`, as `ComplexMatrixConverter` (moved from `ProjectJson.fs:92-123` in step 21) reads its cells. A malformed value throws `JsonException` inside the converter, and the callers already map that to `MalformedJsonErr` (as `ProjectJson.fs` `ProjectJsonText.parseProject` does). The options' doc names the two. No other option changes. The project, groups and environment formats gain the same form for a complex scalar. No schema constrains it (the `$defs` of `schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json` hold no complex object), so their facts stay green.", "acceptance": "After the converters are added, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts`, `a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows` and `an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options`, which step 22 left red; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 24, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [20], "how_to": "The identities, the provenance and the name rule of the library-entry files, in Domain (001 §A; 001 §B 'Every entry file carries'; .spec-md §3.11, §5). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `module LibraryEntryFiles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ElementId.fs` (one `<Compile>` line right after `ElementId.fs`'s in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`) and with no new comment. It opens `MaterialLibrary`, `Library`, `Placement` and `Softellect.Sys.Primitives` (`FileName`, `FileExtension`). Every type follows `AGENTS.md`: single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool` appears, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050. (1) `LibraryEntryKind`: `MaterialEntryKind`, `SampleEntryKind`, `SourceEntryKind`, `PolarizerEntryKind`, `DetectorEntryKind` and `CategoryEntryKind` (S7.1 adds the item-model kind). `member value : int` answers 1 to 6 in that order, and `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : LibraryEntryKind option` answers `None` for any other tag. `member extension : FileExtension` answers `.material-json`, `.sample-json`, `.source-json`, `.polarizer-json`, `.detector-json` and `.category-json` (001 §A). `member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` answers 1 for every kind. `static member all : LibraryEntryKind list` lists the six in tag order. (2) `FileSchemaVersion of int` is the schema version a stored file declares, and `EntrySchema = { kind : LibraryEntryKind; version : FileSchemaVersion }`. (3) `LibraryEntryId of Guid` is an entry's frozen GUID, whatever its kind (001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'). Type extensions after it: `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId`, `SampleId.toLibraryEntryId` and `CategoryId.toLibraryEntryId` keep the GUID. `ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId option` parses a preset's id and answers `None` for any other text; since step 20, every seeded and minted preset id is the canonical string of a GUID. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006): step 25's decoders build a kind's id at the file seam. (4) `CatalogueId of Guid`, `CatalogueName of string` and `KitId of Guid`. `KitId` is the GUID a kit's `.kit-json` carries (001 §E). The provenance needs it now, so it is born here, and S4.1's `Kit` module MUST reuse this type rather than declare a second one (ELEV014). (5) Provenance (001 §B): `MaterialSourceName`, `MaterialSourceRecordId`, `MaterialSourceVersion`, `EntryLicence` (an SPDX identifier, e.g. `CC0-1.0` or `CC-BY-4.0`) and `EntryCitation`, each `of string`; `SourcePullInfo = { source : MaterialSourceName; record : MaterialSourceRecordId; sourceVersion : MaterialSourceVersion; licence : EntryLicence; citation : EntryCitation }`; and `EntryProvenance` = `BuiltInProvenance of CatalogueId` | `UserProvenance` | `KitImportProvenance of KitId` | `SourcePullProvenance of SourcePullInfo`. A built-in's protection derives from its provenance: `member protection : EntryProtection` answers `ProtectedBuiltIn` for `BuiltInProvenance` and `UserManaged` for the rest, and `member categoryOrigin : CategoryOrigin` answers `BuiltInCategory` or `UserCategory` by the same rule. (6) `ContentHash of string` is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of an entry's canonical content. Storage computes it (step 27). (7) The name rule (001 §A; .spec-md §3.11) is `FileStem of string`. `static member ofText (text : string) : FileStem` replaces each of `: * ? \" < > |` and the separators `/` and `\\` with `_` and keeps every other character. `member withExtension (extension : FileExtension) : FileName` answers the stem followed by the extension. `EntryName.fileStem : FileStem` is a type extension. No reserved-name, length or trimming rule is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs` (`module LibraryEntryFilesTests`), appended to the compile list after `CanonicalJsonTests.fs`. (a) `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`: the six tags in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 7, the six extensions exactly as above, version 1 and `all` in tag order. (b) `a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids`: `Ti:sapphire laser, tunable 700–1000 nm` becomes `Ti_sapphire laser, tunable 700–1000 nm`; `a/b\\c*d?e\"f<g>h|i:j` becomes `a_b_c_d_e_f_g_h_i_j`; `Langasite (La3Ga5SiO14)` and `CO₂ laser 10.6 µm` are unchanged; and `(EntryName \"Silicon\").fileStem.withExtension MaterialEntryKind.extension` is `FileName \"Silicon.material-json\"`. (c) `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed`: `protection` and `categoryOrigin` of each of the four provenance cases. (d) `a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id`: `MaterialIds.silicon`, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` and `CategoryIds.glass` keep their GUIDs; `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer.tryToLibraryEntryId` is the GUID its text spells; and a test-local non-GUID `ElementValueId` answers `None`.", "acceptance": "After `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`, `a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids`, `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` and `a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 25, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [24], "how_to": "The entry content, its payload and the envelope, with the builders and decoders that join them to the domain values (001 §B; .spec-md §5). In `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, after step 24's types: (1) The payload holds what the envelope does not, because an entry's id, name, category and description belong to the envelope: `SamplePayloadData = { structure : SampleStructure; substrate : SubstrateKind; supportedEmission : Emission }`, `SourcePayloadData = { waveLength : WaveLength; tuning : SourceTuning }`, `PolarizerPayloadData = { behavior : PolarizerBehavior; category : PolarizerCategory }`, and `LibraryEntryPayload` = `MaterialPayload of MaterialComplexity` | `SamplePayload of SamplePayloadData` | `SourcePayload of SourcePayloadData` | `PolarizerPayload of PolarizerPayloadData` | `DetectorPayload of DetectorKind` | `CategoryPayload of CategoryVisibility`, with `member kind : LibraryEntryKind`. A preset's `protection` and a category's `origin` are not stored, because they derive from the provenance (step 24). (2) `LibraryEntryContent = { schema : EntrySchema; id : LibraryEntryId; version : VersionNumber; name : EntryName; categoryOpt : CategoryId option; descriptionOpt : EntryDescription option; payload : LibraryEntryPayload; provenance : EntryProvenance }` is the entry file without its hash. Its `member fileName : FileName` is `this.name.fileStem.withExtension this.schema.kind.extension`. `categoryOpt` holds a material's category and is `None` for every other kind. Facets are derived from the payload (`LibraryFacets`) and never stored. `VersionNumber` is `MaterialLibrary.fs:VersionNumber`, reused. `LibraryEntryEnvelope = { content : LibraryEntryContent; contentHash : ContentHash }`. The hash covers exactly the content, so the record keeps the two apart while the file stays flat: step 30 writes the content's keys and `contentHash` side by side. (3) `LibraryEntryError` is an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the entry: `EntryKindMismatchErr` (a decoder was given another kind), `EntryIdNotGuidErr` (a preset id that is not a GUID), `ProvenanceMismatchErr` (a preset's protection or a category's origin disagrees with the provenance it is filed under) and `MissingEntryFieldErr` (a material without a category, or a sample without a description). (4) The builders are static members of `LibraryEntryContent`. Each takes `(version : VersionNumber) (provenance : EntryProvenance)` and then the value, and sets `schema = { kind = payload.kind; version = kind.currentSchemaVersion }`. `ofMaterialEntry` and `ofSample` answer the content. `ofSourcePreset`, `ofDetectorPreset`, `ofPolarizerPreset` and `ofMaterialCategory` answer `Result<LibraryEntryContent, LibraryEntryError>`: they refuse an id that is not a GUID, and a protection or origin that disagrees with `provenance.protection` or `provenance.categoryOrigin`. A category is filed under its `CategoryName` as the entry name through `CategoryName.toEntryName`, a type extension declared here, so no builder re-wraps a `.value` (ELEV001). (5) The decoders are members of `LibraryEntryContent`: `toMaterialEntry`, `toSample`, `toSourcePreset`, `toDetectorPreset`, `toPolarizerPreset` and `toMaterialCategory`, each answering `Result<_, LibraryEntryError>`. Each builds the kind's own id from `this.id` (`MaterialId`, `SampleId`, `CategoryId`, or a preset's `ElementValueId` as the GUID's string) and a category's `CategoryName` from the entry name, takes the protection or origin from the provenance, and answers `EntryKindMismatchErr` for another kind's payload. Each decoder is marked `[<Softellect.Sys.ElevationBoundary(nameof Softellect.Sys.StorageBoundary, \"the library-entry file contract (001 §B): the file's kind-neutral entry GUID becomes the kind's own id\")>]`. This is the one place where an entry GUID becomes a kind's id, and it is the file seam, so the boundary licenses the re-wrap that ELEV001 would otherwise report. A builder followed by its decoder answers the value it was given. Tests, in `LibraryEntryFilesTests`: (a) `every kind's builder and decoder are inverse`: one value of each kind (the `builtInEntries` Langasite, `SeedSamples.multilayerQw`, a `SeedSources.tunables` source and the intensity detector under `BuiltInProvenance`, a test-local `ConstantMueller` polarizer under `UserProvenance`, and the `standardCategories` Glass under `BuiltInProvenance`). Each content's `schema` is its payload's kind at version 1, and its decoder answers the value. (b) `a decoder refuses another kind's content`: `toSample` of a material's content answers `EntryKindMismatchErr`. (c) `a preset or category filed under a provenance that disagrees is refused`: a `ProtectedBuiltIn` source under `UserProvenance` and a `UserCategory` under `BuiltInProvenance` answer `ProvenanceMismatchErr`, and a preset whose id is a test-local non-GUID text answers `EntryIdNotGuidErr`. (d) `a material without a category or a sample without a description does not decode`: a material content with `categoryOpt = None` and a sample content with `descriptionOpt = None` answer `MissingEntryFieldErr`. (e) `an entry's file name is its name made safe plus its kind's extension`: the content of a source named `Ti:sapphire laser 800 nm` has the file name `Ti_sapphire laser 800 nm.source-json`, and Langasite's has `Langasite (La3Ga5SiO14).material-json`.", "acceptance": "After the content model lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every kind's builder and decoder are inverse`, `a decoder refuses another kind's content`, `a preset or category filed under a provenance that disagrees is refused`, `a material without a category or a sample without a description does not decode` and `an entry's file name is its name made safe plus its kind's extension`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.every kind's builder and decoder are inverse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a decoder refuses another kind's content", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a preset or category filed under a provenance that disagrees is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a material without a category or a sample without a description does not decode", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.an entry's file name is its name made safe plus its kind's extension", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 26, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [25], "how_to": "The catalogue manifest (001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout': `.catalogue-json` holds the name, the catalogue id, the version and the entry hashes; .spec-md §5). In `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: (1) `CatalogueManifestRow = { kind : LibraryEntryKind; id : LibraryEntryId; version : VersionNumber; fileName : FileName; contentHash : ContentHash }`, and `LibraryEntryEnvelope.manifestRow : CatalogueManifestRow`, built from `content.schema.kind`, `content.id`, `content.version`, `content.fileName` and `contentHash`. (2) `CatalogueManifest = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; id : CatalogueId; name : CatalogueName; version : VersionNumber; entries : CatalogueManifestRow list }`, with three static members. `currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` is 1. `extension : FileExtension` is `.catalogue-json`, the one place that text is written, and `fileName : FileName` is `(FileStem.ofText \"\").withExtension extension`, because a file that exists once per folder is named by its extension alone (001 §A). `tryCreate (id : CatalogueId) (name : CatalogueName) (version : VersionNumber) (envelopes : LibraryEntryEnvelope list) : Result<CatalogueManifest, LibraryEntryError>` is the pure per-kind uniqueness check that export uses (001 §A). Two envelopes of one kind whose file names are equal ignoring case (the Windows file system's rule, `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`) are `DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`, naming both entries. Two envelopes with the same id and version are `DuplicateEntryVersionErr`. Both cases join `LibraryEntryError`. Equal names of different kinds are allowed, because their extensions differ. The rows are sorted by kind tag and then ordinally by file name, so a manifest's text does not depend on the order its entries arrived in. The manifest's own hash is not stored in it: Storage computes it (step 31), and S3's start-up import records it. Tests, in `LibraryEntryFilesTests`, over envelopes whose `contentHash` is a test-local 64-character hex literal (Domain does not hash): (a) `a manifest lists one row per envelope, sorted by kind and file name`: a source, a material and a sample, given in that order, become three rows in kind order, each equal to its envelope's `manifestRow`, and `schemaVersion` is 1. (b) `a manifest refuses two entries of one kind with one file name`: two materials named `Silicon` and `silicon`, and two named `Si:O` and `Si_O`, each answer `DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`, while a material and a sample both named `Glass` are accepted. (c) `a manifest refuses one entry version twice`: two envelopes with one id and one version answer `DuplicateEntryVersionErr`.", "acceptance": "After the manifest model lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a manifest lists one row per envelope, sorted by kind and file name`, `a manifest refuses two entries of one kind with one file name` and `a manifest refuses one entry version twice`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a manifest lists one row per envelope, sorted by kind and file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-MANIFEST-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a manifest refuses two entries of one kind with one file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-MANIFEST-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a manifest refuses one entry version twice", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-MANIFEST-MODEL"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 27, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [23, 24], "how_to": "The canonical form and the content hash (001 §B: `contentHash` is SHA-256 over canonical JSON, with sorted keys and invariant-culture numbers; .spec-md §5). In `CanonicalJson.fs`: (1) `nodeOf<'Value> (value : 'Value) : Result<JsonNode, StorageError>` serializes through `options` into a `JsonNode`. A serializer failure (a non-finite double, an unsupported type) is `MalformedJsonErr` carrying the message, never a throw. (2) The canonical rendering of a `JsonNode` lives in extension members on `JsonNode`, because members may speak primitives while no free function may take or return a bare `string` or `byte[]` (ELEV003). Every object's properties are written in ordinal order of their names (`StringComparer.Ordinal`). Arrays keep their order. Numbers keep the serializer's invariant shortest round-trip text. Strings are escaped by `JavaScriptEncoder.UnsafeRelaxedJsonEscaping`, so names such as `CO₂ laser 10.6 µm` stay readable. No BOM is written. There are two renderings: indented, with two-space indents and `\\n` line ends (`JsonWriterOptions.NewLine`), which is the file form; and compact, with no whitespace, which is the hashed form. (3) `contentHashOf<'Value> (value : 'Value) : Result<ContentHash, StorageError>` is the lowercase hex (`Convert.ToHexStringLower`) SHA-256 (`SHA256.HashData`) of the UTF-8 bytes of the compact canonical rendering of `nodeOf value`. So the hash depends on neither whitespace, key order nor the current culture. Doubles round-trip bit-exactly, because System.Text.Json writes the shortest round-trip text and reads it back with correct IEEE rounding. Tests, in `CanonicalJsonTests`: (a) `canonical text orders every object's keys and ignores the order they came in`: for the node of a test-local tunable `SourcePreset` and a copy with every object's properties reversed recursively, both renderings of the two are equal, and the keys come out in ordinal order. (b) `every double round-trips bit-exactly through canonical text whatever the culture`: the list `0.1; 1.0/3.0; 5e-324; 2.2250738585072014e-308; 1.7976931348623157e308; -0.0; 6.02214076e23; 1e-300` written canonically and read back keeps every value's `BitConverter.DoubleToInt64Bits`, under `CultureInfo(\"de-DE\")` set as the current culture and restored in a `finally`, and the text uses `.` as its decimal point. (c) `the content hash is the lowercase SHA-256 of the compact canonical text`: `contentHashOf` equals the test's own `SHA256.HashData` over the compact rendering's UTF-8, in 64 lowercase hex characters; equal values hash equal, and a changed number hashes differently. (d) `the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen`: for a test-local `MaterialCategory` with a fixed GUID literal and the name `Glass — CO₂ µm`, the indented rendering equals a text literal (LF line ends, two-space indents, the non-ASCII characters unescaped) and `contentHashOf` equals a hash literal. Both literals are the implemented writer's output, captured once while implementing this step and frozen from then on, so any later change to the canonical form fails here before it can change a committed catalogue file's hash (S1.5). (e) `a non-finite number is a typed serialization error`: `nodeOf nan` answers `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After the canonical writer and the hash land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `canonical text orders every object's keys and ignores the order they came in`, `every double round-trips bit-exactly through canonical text whatever the culture`, `the content hash is the lowercase SHA-256 of the compact canonical text`, `the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen` and `a non-finite number is a typed serialization error`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.canonical text orders every object's keys and ignores the order they came in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every double round-trips bit-exactly through canonical text whatever the culture", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.the content hash is the lowercase SHA-256 of the compact canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.a non-finite number is a typed serialization error", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 28, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [27], "how_to": "A closed set's disk tag is its int (`AGENTS.md`: 'A closed set's wire/disk tag is an integer'; .spec-md §4 'Shapes'). `CanonicalJson.options` gains four converters, written as step 23's are and registered before the `JsonFSharpConverter`. They cover `LibraryEntryKind` (step 24); S1.1's `TabulatedInterpolation` (step 2) and `PublishedIndexLaw` (step 8); and S1.2's `PublishedGyrationLaw` (step 10). The last three are in `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`. Each converter writes the case's `value` and reads through `tryOfWire`. An unknown tag throws `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. No other union changes its form. The fieldless unions without an int tag (`SubstrateKind`, `DetectorKind`, `CategoryVisibility` and the rest) keep the serializer's case-name form, which the project, groups and environment formats already store. Giving them int tags is out of scope. Tests, in `CanonicalJsonTests`: (a) `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back`: every case of the four sets serializes as its `value` (for example `1`) and reads back equal. (b) `an unknown disk tag is refused`: reading `9` as a `LibraryEntryKind` and `4` as a `PublishedIndexLaw` throws `JsonException`.", "acceptance": "After the tag converters land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-WIRE-TAGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-WIRE-TAGS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 29, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui"], "depends_on": [21], "how_to": "`SchemaValidation` is generalised from the one project schema to any build-copied schema (001 §B: 'JSON Schema per kind … REUSED'; .spec-md §6 'JSON + schema'), so one evaluation body serves every format. In `SchemaValidation.fs`, `validateWith (schema : Lazy<Result<JsonSchema, StorageError>>) (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` holds the evaluation body of today's `validate` (`:64-76`): `EvaluationOptions(OutputFormat = OutputFormat.List)`, `collectMessages` (`:45-59`) and the fallback message `schema validation failed`. `validate` answers `validateWith` over the project schema (`:31-36`), so `ProjectJson` is unchanged. The two copies of that body are deleted and call it: `GroupsLibrary.validateGroupsLibrary` (`GroupsLibrary.fs:49-59`) over its groups schema, and `UserEnvironment.validateUserEnvironment` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs:331-344`) over its environment schema. Both keep their names, their lazies and their `$id`s, and their docs say they reuse `validateWith`. The environment validator's messages now keep their nested instance locations, as the groups validator's already do. `EnvironmentRoundTripTests` asserts only that messages are present, and `GroupsRoundTripTests` that the groups-specific fallback text is absent, so both stay green unchanged. The per-kind schemas arrive with their files in step 30.", "acceptance": "After the generalisation, the project, groups and environment validators MUST share `validateWith`, and `RoundTripTests`, `GroupsRoundTripTests` and `EnvironmentRoundTripTests` MUST pass unchanged; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, the selected ui-tests classes and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/GroupsLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 30, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [26, 28, 29], "how_to": "One file per entry: write it, then read it back through schema, version and hash checks (001 §B: 'One entry per file', 'Every entry file carries', 'JSON Schema per kind', 'No up-converters'; .spec-md §5). (1) `Errors.fs`: `StorageError` (`:21-27`) gains `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr of SchemaVersionMismatchInfo` and `ContentHashMismatchErr of ContentHashMismatchInfo`. The two records are declared above it: `SchemaVersionMismatchInfo = { fileExtension : FileExtension; found : FileSchemaVersion; expected : FileSchemaVersion }`, where the extension names the file's kind (001 §A) so that S4's kit files can reuse the case, and `ContentHashMismatchInfo = { entryId : LibraryEntryId; recorded : ContentHash; computed : ContentHash }`. Records carry the two same-typed fields, because a case holding them as a tuple is ELEV011. The doc list (`:11-20`) names both cases. No existing match on `StorageError` is exhaustive, so no consumer changes. (2) Schemas, in draft 2020-12 like `schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json`, each with its own `$id` (`https://berreman/schema/library-<kind>.json`). `schema/library-common.schema.json` holds, once, the definitions that every entry and the catalogue share: the GUID string, a positive version, the content hash `^[0-9a-f]{64}$` and the four provenance shapes. The others reference it by its `$id`. `schema/library-material.schema.json`, `library-sample`, `library-source`, `library-polarizer`, `library-detector` and `library-category` each describe exactly what this step's writer emits for their kind. Each checks unconditionally that `schema` is `{ kind: <the kind's tag>, version: <a positive integer> }`. Everything else is checked only under `if` `schema.version` is 1 (`then`): every key present and no other (`additionalProperties: false`); `id` a GUID; `name` a non-empty string; `categoryOpt` a GUID for a material and `null` otherwise; `descriptionOpt` a string for a sample, a string or `null` for a material, and `null` otherwise; `payload` the kind's case tag with its record's required keys; `provenance` one of the four shapes; and `contentHash` the hash pattern. The physics inside a payload (`MaterialComplexity`, `SampleStructure`, `PolarizerBehavior`, `SourceTuning`) is bound by the serializer, which reports a malformed one as `MalformedJsonErr`. A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. Each file is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest`, beside the existing `schema/optical-constructor-*.schema.json` items of `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no new comment. (3) `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `type LibraryEntryKind with member schemaFile : FileName` (`schema/library-<kind>.schema.json`); the common schema and one lazy per kind, each loaded once (`JsonSchema.FromText` registers an `$id` only once, `:17-21`), with the common schema loaded before any entry schema evaluates; and `validateEntry (kind : LibraryEntryKind) (element : JsonElement)` over step 29's `validateWith`. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs`, `module EntryFileJson`, compiled directly after `CanonicalJson.fs`. `LibraryFileText of string` is a library file's text, UTF-8 without a BOM; S2's database payload and S4's kit snapshot hold it byte for byte. `LibraryEntryContent.sealed : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` is the content with `contentHashOf content` (step 27). `LibraryEntryEnvelope.fileText : Result<LibraryFileText, StorageError>` is the content's canonical node with `contentHash` added beside its keys, rendered indented and ending with one `\\n`; `ProjectJson.serializeProject` adds `schemaVersion` the same way. `LibraryFileText.parseEntry (kind : LibraryEntryKind) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` works in this order. It parses the text (`MalformedJsonErr`). It validates the document against the kind's schema (`SchemaValidationErr`), so a file of another kind fails here. It compares `schema.version` with `kind.currentSchemaVersion` before anything binds (`UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`). It binds the content from the document without `contentHash` (`MalformedJsonErr`). Finally it compares `contentHashOf content` with the recorded hash (`ContentHashMismatchErr`). There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Every .NET call that throws is caught here and mapped; nothing above handles an exception. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs` (`module EntryFileJsonTests`), appended to the compile list after `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs`. Each round trip goes content → `sealed` → `fileText` → `parseEntry` and answers an equal envelope, whose decoder answers the original value. (a) `a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape`: one constant complexity for each `ConstantEpsValue` case; dispersive complexities over `IsotropicDispersive`, `UniaxialDispersive` and `BiaxialDispersive` whose segments together carry every `EpsAxisDispersion` case: `RealNK` (through `DispersionModel.toEpsAxis` of a Cauchy model) and `ComplexEps` (of a Sellmeier model), `TabulatedNK` (through `TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate`), `TaucLorentzAxis`, `GaussianOscillatorAxis`, `ForouhiBloomerAxis` and `BrendelBormannAxis` (through `toEpsAxis` of coefficient sets written in the fixture), and `PublishedLawAxis` of each `PublishedIndexLaw`; one complexity with a constant and one with a dispersive `magnetic` aspect; and one with each `active` case, `RhoWithoutDispValue`, `RhoWithDispValue` and `PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw`. (b) `a multilayer sample entry file round-trips`: `SeedSamples.multilayerQw` (a `Repeated` period group) and `SeedSamples.langasiteSilicon`. (c) `a tunable source entry file round-trips`: a `SeedSources.tunables` source under `BuiltInProvenance` and a user source under `UserProvenance`. (d) `a constant-Mueller polarizer entry file round-trips`: a two-component `ConstantMueller` polarizer in the `CustomMueller` category. (e) `a detector and a category entry file round-trip`: the ellipsometer detector and the `standardCategories` Vacuum category. (f) `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`: one material under each of the four provenance cases. (g) `an entry file is indented canonical JSON whose hash survives a write and a read`: the text is the indented canonical rendering, ends with one `\\n` and holds no `\\r`; writing the parsed envelope again gives the same text; and the hash equals `contentHashOf` of the content. (h) `an entry file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: a material file with `schema.version` set to 2 answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = MaterialEntryKind.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`, both with its body intact and with `payload` replaced by `{}`. (i) `a tampered entry file is ContentHashMismatchErr`: a number inside the payload changed in the text, with the recorded hash kept, answers `ContentHashMismatchErr` whose `recorded` is the file's hash and whose `computed` is the changed content's. (j) `a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr`: the file without `name`, and a sample's file parsed as a material, answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; a text that is not JSON answers `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After the entry files land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the ten EntryFileJsonTests facts from `a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape` to `a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-material.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-sample.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-source.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-polarizer.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-detector.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-category.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a multilayer sample entry file round-trips", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a tunable source entry file round-trips", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a constant-Mueller polarizer entry file round-trips", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a detector and a category entry file round-trip", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.every provenance round-trips through an entry file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.an entry file is indented canonical JSON whose hash survives a write and a read", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.an entry file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a tampered entry file is ContentHashMismatchErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 31, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [30], "how_to": "The catalogue manifest's file, and the proof that every built-in has a file form (001 §A; 001 §B; .spec-md §5). (1) `schema/library-catalogue.schema.json` has its own `$id` and references `library-common.schema.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Under `if` it is 1: `id` a GUID, `name` a non-empty string, `version` positive, `entries` an array of rows `{ kind: 1 to 6, id, version, fileName: a non-empty string, contentHash }`, and no other key. It is a `Content` item like step 30's. `SchemaValidation.validateCatalogueManifest (element : JsonElement)` runs over `validateWith`, with its schema loaded once. (2) `EntryFileJson.fs` gains three members. `CatalogueManifest.fileText : Result<LibraryFileText, StorageError>` is indented canonical text ending with one `\\n`. `CatalogueManifest.manifestHash : Result<ContentHash, StorageError>` is `contentHashOf` the manifest, the hash S3's start-up import compares (001 §B 'Import on every start'). `LibraryFileText.parseCatalogueManifest : Result<CatalogueManifest, StorageError>` parses (`MalformedJsonErr`), validates (`SchemaValidationErr`), compares `schemaVersion` with `CatalogueManifest.currentSchemaVersion` (`UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = CatalogueManifest.extension`, step 26), and binds (`MalformedJsonErr`). (3) The built-ins: the code seeds are still present (`builtInEntries`, `standardCategories` and `seedEntries`, which S1.7 deletes). Every one of them is sealed at version 1 under `BuiltInProvenance` of a test catalogue id, written, parsed and decoded. Tests, in `EntryFileJsonTests`: (a) `a catalogue manifest round-trips and its hash is stable`: a manifest from `CatalogueManifest.tryCreate` over sealed envelopes of three kinds, written and parsed, is equal; its `manifestHash` is equal before and after and equals `contentHashOf` of the manifest; and changing one row's hash changes it. (b) `a catalogue manifest of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: with `schemaVersion` set to 2, it answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `CatalogueManifest.extension`, found 2 and expected 1. (c) `a schema-invalid catalogue manifest is SchemaValidationErr`: a row without `contentHash` answers `SchemaValidationErr`. (d) `every built-in seals, writes, reads and decodes equal to its seed`: every `builtInEntries` material, every `standardCategories` category and every `seedEntries` sample, source, detector and polarizer round-trips through its entry file, and its decoder answers a value equal to the seed. (e) `the built-ins form one catalogue with unique file names per kind`: `CatalogueManifest.tryCreate` over all of their envelopes is `Ok`, so the built-ins' file names are unique per kind and no id and version repeats; it has one row per built-in, and the manifest round-trips.", "acceptance": "After the catalogue file lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a catalogue manifest round-trips and its hash is stable`, `a catalogue manifest of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid catalogue manifest is SchemaValidationErr`, `every built-in seals, writes, reads and decodes equal to its seed` and `the built-ins form one catalogue with unique file names per kind`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-catalogue.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a catalogue manifest round-trips and its hash is stable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a catalogue manifest of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid catalogue manifest is SchemaValidationErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.every built-in seals, writes, reads and decodes equal to its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.the built-ins form one catalogue with unique file names per kind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 32, "anchor": "ADD_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S1.5a", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0001", "name": "CatalogueProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [26], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests"], "how_to": "The catalogue-folder seam in Domain (001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout', §B 'Shipped catalogue'; .spec-md §3.4, §3.5, §4 'Errors and IO', §5 `CatalogueProxy`): its data, its errors, its record, its in-memory double and the shipped catalogue's identity. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs`: `module CatalogueFiles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (step 24): one `<Compile Include=\"CatalogueFiles.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no new comment. It opens `MaterialLibrary` (`VersionNumber`) and `LibraryEntryFiles`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050, and every type follows `AGENTS.md` (two-word case names, no `bool`). (1) `module CatalogueIds` holds `builtInCatalogue : CatalogueId = Guid.Parse \"499ae2ca-4f4c-4d4f-b53e-62ef2627130a\" |> CatalogueId`, shaped like `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:50-62`): the frozen identity of the shipped Built-in catalogue and the one place it is written (.spec-md §3.3). (2) `CatalogueError` is an `*Error` union. Every case but the last is `of reason : string` naming the catalogue or the file: `CatalogueIoErr` (a folder or a file could not be read or written, or the in-memory store holds no catalogue), `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` (the manifest or an entry file failed its parse), `MissingEntryFileErr` (a manifest row names a file the folder lacks), `UnlistedEntryFileErr` (the folder holds an entry file no manifest row names) and `ManifestMismatchErr` (the manifest is not the one its entries make). `InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr of LibraryEntryError` carries step 26's refusal (`DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`, `DuplicateEntryVersionErr`). (3) `CatalogueData = { manifest : CatalogueManifest; envelopes : LibraryEntryEnvelope list }` is one catalogue: its manifest and every entry, in the manifest's row order. `static member tryCreate (id : CatalogueId) (name : CatalogueName) (version : VersionNumber) (envelopes : LibraryEntryEnvelope list) : Result<CatalogueData, CatalogueError>` builds the manifest through `CatalogueManifest.tryCreate` (step 26; its refusal is `InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr`) and orders the envelopes by its rows, so the sort rule stays step 26's alone. `member this.validate : Result<unit, CatalogueError>` is the one consistency rule both stores call: `CatalogueManifest.tryCreate` over `this.manifest`'s id, name and version and `this.envelopes` MUST answer exactly `this.manifest`, and the envelopes' `manifestRow`s MUST be its `entries` in order; otherwise it answers `ManifestMismatchErr` naming the catalogue, or `InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr`. (4) `[<ReferenceEquality>] CatalogueProxy = { readCatalogue : unit -> Result<CatalogueData, CatalogueError>; writeCatalogue : CatalogueData -> Result<unit, CatalogueError> }`, the functional-proxy convention of `ElementId.fs:SourceProxy`: one proxy per catalogue folder, built once where it is composed. Its doc states the contract. Read answers the catalogue with every file validated and hash-checked, or a typed error. Write refuses a catalogue that fails `validate` and then writes nothing; otherwise it writes every file atomically, so that read answers an equal catalogue. Storage's `create` (step 33) is the folder implementation. (5) `static member createInMemory () : CatalogueProxy` is the in-memory double (.spec-md §4: every proxy has one). It holds at most one `CatalogueData` in a closure-local `ref`, so mutation stays inside the closure as in `Library.createInMemoryEmpty` (`ElementId.fs:createInMemoryEmpty`). Write runs `validate`, then replaces what it holds; read answers what it holds, or `CatalogueIoErr` while nothing has been written. No caching, retry or other field is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs` (`module CatalogueProxyTests`), appended to `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list after `EntryFileJsonTests.fs` (step 30), with no new comment. Its envelopes are built with step 25's builders at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, each with a distinct test-local 64-character lowercase hex `ContentHash` literal, because Domain does not hash (as in step 26's facts). (a) `the in-memory catalogue reads back what it was written`: a `tryCreate` over a source, a material and a sample, given in that order, written and read, is equal, and its envelopes are in its manifest's row order. (b) `the in-memory catalogue holds nothing until it is written`: read answers `CatalogueIoErr`. (c) `a catalogue whose manifest its entries do not make is refused and not written`: the `tryCreate` result with one manifest row's `contentHash` replaced, and the same result with its envelopes reversed, each answer `ManifestMismatchErr` on write, and read still answers `CatalogueIoErr`. (d) `entries that cannot form a manifest are InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr`: `tryCreate` over two envelopes with one id and one version answers `InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr` holding `DuplicateEntryVersionErr`.", "acceptance": "After the contract lands, `CatalogueFiles.fs` MUST declare `CatalogueProxy` with exactly the fields `readCatalogue` and `writeCatalogue`, and constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the in-memory catalogue reads back what it was written`, `the in-memory catalogue holds nothing until it is written`, `a catalogue whose manifest its entries do not make is refused and not written` and `entries that cannot form a manifest are InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr`; and build, elevation and the six s05 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests.the in-memory catalogue reads back what it was written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests.the in-memory catalogue holds nothing until it is written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests.a catalogue whose manifest its entries do not make is refused and not written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests.entries that cannot form a manifest are InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-PROXY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueFiles.CatalogueProxy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-PROXY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.5 -- The built-in catalogue generated once from the code seeds"}
{"number": 33, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S1.5b", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0001", "name": "CatalogueProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [31, 32], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests"], "how_to": "The folder implementation of `CatalogueProxy` (001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout'; .spec-md §3.5, §4 'Stored formats', §5). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs`: `StorageError` gains `member this.describe : string`, one line per case: the text of `MalformedJsonErr`; the joined messages of `SchemaValidationErr`; a fixed text for `SchemaMissingErr`; the exception message of `FileIoExn` and `BinzExn`; the file of `SidecarMissingErr`; the extension with the found and expected versions of `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`; and the entry id with the recorded and computed hashes of `ContentHashMismatchErr` (step 30). It is the honest render a Domain error's reason carries, so no caller formats a `StorageError` with `%A` (ELEV002). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs`, `module CatalogueFolderStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `EntryFileJson.fs` (step 30): one `<Compile>` line and no new comment. (a) `type LibraryFileText with member this.writeAtomically (file : FileName) : Result<unit, StorageError>` writes the text as UTF-8 without a BOM to `<file>.tmp` beside the file, then moves it over the file (`File.Move(tmp, file, true)`). On a failure it deletes the `.tmp` and answers `FileIoExn`. (b) `type CatalogueProxy with static member create (folder : FolderName) : CatalogueProxy` (.spec-md §5: the Domain record, the real `create` in Storage). `readCatalogue` works in this order. The folder and its `.catalogue-json` (`CatalogueManifest.fileName`, step 26) are read: a missing folder, a missing manifest or any IO failure is `CatalogueIoErr`. `LibraryFileText.parseCatalogueManifest` (step 31) parses the manifest; its error is `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` naming `.catalogue-json` and the error's `describe`. The folder's top-level files whose extension is one of `LibraryEntryKind.all`'s `extension`s are its entry files; every other file (the manifest, a `.tmp`, a README) is not read. A row whose `fileName` the folder lacks is `MissingEntryFileErr`. Then an entry file that no row names is `UnlistedEntryFileErr`; names are compared with `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`, the Windows rule step 26 uses. Each row's file is parsed with `LibraryFileText.parseEntry row.kind` (step 30), so its schema, its version and its hash are checked; a refusal is `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` naming the file. Finally the result, envelopes in row order, MUST pass `CatalogueData.validate` (step 32). `writeCatalogue` runs `validate` first. It then refuses a folder that holds an entry file the catalogue does not name (`UnlistedEntryFileErr`), so a write never deletes a file and a written folder reads back equal. Otherwise it creates the folder when missing and writes each entry's `fileText` (step 30) to its `content.fileName`, and the manifest's `fileText` (step 31) to `.catalogue-json` last, each through `writeAtomically`, so a reader never meets a manifest naming a file that is not yet whole (.spec-md §4: write `*.tmp`, then replace). An IO failure is `CatalogueIoErr`, and a serialization failure is `CatalogueFileRejectedErr`. Every .NET IO call is caught here and mapped (.spec-md §4 'Errors and IO'). A declaration whose signature carries a bare primitive for that IO is marked on itself with `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof IoBoundary, ...)>]`. The write validates no schema, because it writes typed values, so it also runs where no `schema/` folder sits beside the assembly (step 35's script). Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs` (`module CatalogueFolderTests`), appended to the compile list after `CatalogueProxyTests.fs`. Every folder is a fresh one under `AppContext.BaseDirectory` (the `ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs:25` precedent), never `%TEMP%`. The catalogue is the `CatalogueData.tryCreate` of envelopes sealed with step 30's `sealed` from the code seeds (the `builtInEntries` Langasite, `SeedSamples.multilayerQw`, a `SeedSources.tunables` source, the ellipsometer detector and the `standardCategories` Glass) under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. (a) `a catalogue folder written and read back is equal`: after the write, the folder holds exactly `.catalogue-json` and one file per entry named by its `content.fileName`, and no `.tmp`; read answers an equal `CatalogueData`. Writing a second catalogue, in which the source's content changed (a new hash under the same file name), replaces the files, and read answers the second. (b) `a manifest row with no file is MissingEntryFileErr`: one entry file deleted. (c) `an entry file the manifest does not name is UnlistedEntryFileErr, and other files are ignored`: a copy of an entry file under another name with the same extension makes read answer `UnlistedEntryFileErr`, and write answer `UnlistedEntryFileErr` with every file's text unchanged; a `README.md` and a `stale.tmp` beside the entries leave read `Ok` and equal. (d) `a tampered entry file is CatalogueFileRejectedErr`: a number inside one entry file's payload changed, with its recorded hash kept, answers `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` whose reason names that file. (e) `a manifest that disagrees with its entry files is ManifestMismatchErr`: one entry file replaced by the sealed file of a changed content under the same file name is a valid file, but not the hash its row records. (f) `a missing folder or manifest is CatalogueIoErr`: a folder that does not exist, and a written folder whose `.catalogue-json` was deleted.", "acceptance": "After the folder implementation lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the six CatalogueFolderTests facts from `a catalogue folder written and read back is equal` to `a missing folder or manifest is CatalogueIoErr`, which instantiate the real `CatalogueProxy.create` over folders under the test output; and build, elevation and the six s05 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.a catalogue folder written and read back is equal", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.a manifest row with no file is MissingEntryFileErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.an entry file the manifest does not name is UnlistedEntryFileErr, and other files are ignored", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.a tampered entry file is CatalogueFileRejectedErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.a manifest that disagrees with its entry files is ManifestMismatchErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.a missing folder or manifest is CatalogueIoErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-CATALOGUE-FOLDER"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.5 -- The built-in catalogue generated once from the code seeds"}
{"number": 34, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.5c", "red": "RED_0006", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [33], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests"], "how_to": "Red first for 001 §B 'Shipped catalogue' ('tests load the same files') and .spec-md §3.5-§3.6: the catalogue the build copies into the test output equals the code seeds. Facts only; no production file changes. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs` (`module BuiltInCatalogueParityTests`), appended to the compile list after `CatalogueFolderTests.fs`. A private `readBuiltIn ()` reads `(CatalogueProxy.create (FolderName (Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"Catalogue\", \"Builtin\")))).readCatalogue ()` and fails the fact on an error. So every fact here is red today: the build copies no `Catalogue/Builtin/` yet, and the read answers `CatalogueIoErr`. The entries of one kind are decoded with that kind's decoder (step 25). The expected catalogue is computed independently of the export (step 35). Each seed is sealed at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, and `CatalogueData.tryCreate CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue (CatalogueName \"Built-in\") VersionNumber.first` builds the catalogue over them. The seeds are every `MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries` material, every `standardCategories` category, every `Library.SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` sample, every `SeedSources.allSeedSources` source, and the `DetectorItem` and `PolarizerItem` entries of `Library.seedEntries`. (a) `the built-in catalogue is the Built-in catalogue at version 1`: the manifest's id is `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, its name `CatalogueName \"Built-in\"` and its version `VersionNumber.first`; every envelope is version 1 under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`; there is one row per seed, counted from the seed lists; and the rows name `Silicon.material-json`, `Langasite (La3Ga5SiO14).material-json` and `Transparent glass (n = 1.52).material-json` (001 §A). (b) `every built-in material and category in the catalogue equals its seed`: the decoded materials equal `builtInEntries`, compared by id (the same ids, each equal in complexity and metadata), and the decoded categories equal `standardCategories`. (c) `every built-in sample in the catalogue equals its seed`: against `allSeedSamples`, compared by id. (d) `every built-in source, detector and polarizer in the catalogue equals its seed`: against `allSeedSources` and `seedEntries`' detectors and polarizers, compared by id. (e) `the built-in catalogue is exactly what the seeds seal to, and its manifest hash is stable`: the read `CatalogueData` equals the expected one, every content hash included; `manifestHash` (step 31) of the read manifest equals that of the expected one; and a second read gives the same hash. S1.7 deletes this class together with the seeds.", "acceptance": "After the facts land, constructor-unit-tests (BuiltInCatalogueParityTests) MUST fail with exactly `the built-in catalogue is the Built-in catalogue at version 1`, `every built-in material and category in the catalogue equals its seed`, `every built-in sample in the catalogue equals its seed`, `every built-in source, detector and polarizer in the catalogue equals its seed` and `the built-in catalogue is exactly what the seeds seal to, and its manifest hash is stable`, the class's only facts; and build, elevation and the six s05 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.the built-in catalogue is the Built-in catalogue at version 1", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-BUILTIN-PARITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.every built-in material and category in the catalogue equals its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-BUILTIN-PARITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.every built-in sample in the catalogue equals its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-BUILTIN-PARITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.every built-in source, detector and polarizer in the catalogue equals its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-BUILTIN-PARITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.the built-in catalogue is exactly what the seeds seal to, and its manifest hash is stable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S15-BUILTIN-PARITY"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.5 -- The built-in catalogue generated once from the code seeds"}
{"number": 35, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.5c", "closes": "RED_0006", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage"], "depends_on": [34], "how_to": "The code seeds are exported once into the shipped catalogue (001 §B 'Shipped catalogue': GUIDs and values byte-for-byte; .spec-md §3.5, §3.6, §7 'Code seeds → catalogue files'). (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx`, the throw-away tool. It `#I`s `../OpticalConstructor.Tests/bin/x64/Release/net10.0/`, the Release x64 output that holds the built Domain and Storage assemblies beside every assembly they load. From there it `#r`s `Softellect.Berreman.OpticalConstructor.Domain.dll`, `Softellect.Berreman.OpticalConstructor.Storage.dll` and the assemblies they load, each from that folder (among them Softellect.Sys, the Berreman core, MathNet.Numerics, FSharp.SystemTextJson, and JsonSchema.Net with Json.More and JsonPointer.Net). It uses no `#r \"nuget:\"`, so no network is needed. It seals every seed step 34 names at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, through step 25's builders and step 30's `sealed`. It builds `CatalogueData.tryCreate CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue (CatalogueName \"Built-in\") VersionNumber.first` and writes it with `(CatalogueProxy.create (FolderName (Path.Combine(__SOURCE_DIRECTORY__, \"Builtin\")))).writeCatalogue` (step 33). So the committed files are exactly what the product writer writes, and no second writer exists. Any `Error` prints its case and exits with 1. (2) Build the solution, run `dotnet fsi Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx` once from the repository root, and commit `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/`. It holds `.catalogue-json` and one file per seed, named by the entry's name made safe (step 24's `FileStem`) plus its kind's extension, with no category folders (001 §A): `Silicon.material-json`, `Nd_YAG ×2 532 nm.source-json` and the rest, exactly the files this step's effects list. Every file is LF-only and ends with one LF (step 30). `git check-ignore` MUST report none of them: `[Bb]in/` (`.gitignore:23`) does not match `Builtin/`, and only `*.tmp` (`.gitignore:78`) would match, which is intended, since no `.tmp` is committed. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` gains, beside its `schema` `Content` items, `<Content Include=\"..\\Catalogue\\Builtin\\**\" Link=\"Catalogue\\Builtin\\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)\">` with `<CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>`, and no new comment. So every output that references Storage carries the same files, as it carries `schema/` today: the App (`<install>\\Catalogue\\Builtin\\`), the TestWindows heads and both constructor test suites. No product code reads them yet (S1.6 does), and the seeds stay until S1.7.", "acceptance": "After the catalogue is exported and copied, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the built-in catalogue is the Built-in catalogue at version 1`, `every built-in material and category in the catalogue equals its seed`, `every built-in sample in the catalogue equals its seed`, `every built-in source, detector and polarizer in the catalogue equals its seed` and `the built-in catalogue is exactly what the seeds seal to, and its manifest hash is stable`, which step 34 left red; `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/` MUST hold exactly `.catalogue-json` and the entry files this step's effects list, none of them git-ignored; and build, elevation and the six s05 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/.catalogue-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Silicon.material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Langasite (La3Ga5SiO14).material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Transparent glass (n = 1.52).material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Transparent glass (n = 1.50).material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Transparent glass (n = 1.75).material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Transparent glass (n = 2.00).material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Uniaxial crystal.material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Biaxial crystal.material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Vacuum.material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Molybdenum (Mo, EUV).material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Silicon (Si, EUV).material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Active (gyrotropic) crystal.material-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Glass.category-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Metal.category-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Semiconductor.category-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Crystal.category-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Vacuum.category-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Glass plate (n=1.52, 1 mm).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Glass plate (n=1.52, 2 mm).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Glass thin film (n=1.75, 600 nm).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Glass _ vacuum interface (n=1.50).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Glass thin film (n=1.52, 200 nm).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Quarter-wave glass_vacuum multilayer (41 layers).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/EUV Mo_Si multilayer (100 pairs).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Uniaxial crystal film (1 µm).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Biaxial crystal film (1 µm).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Active gyrotropic crystal plate (1 cm).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Langasite film on silicon (10 µm, dispersive).sample-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Monochromatic 600 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/HeNe laser 632.8 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/HeNe laser 543.5 nm (green).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Argon-ion laser 488 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Argon-ion laser 514.5 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/HeCd laser 441.6 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/HeCd laser 325 nm (UV).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/GaN diode laser 405 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ruby laser 694.3 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ti_sapphire laser 800 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Nd_YAG laser 1064 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Nd_YAG ×2 532 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Nd_YAG ×3 355 nm (UV).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Nd_YAG ×4 266 nm (DUV).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Erbium fibre laser 1550 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/CO₂ laser 10.6 µm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Mercury g-line 435.8 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Mercury h-line 404.7 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Mercury i-line 365 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/KrF excimer 248 nm (DUV).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/ArF excimer 193 nm (DUV, dry _ immersion).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/F₂ excimer 157 nm (VUV).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/EUV 13.5 nm (Sn plasma).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/BEUV 6.7 nm (beyond EUV).source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Xenon lamp + monochromator, 190–1000 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ti_sapphire laser, tunable 700–1000 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Supercontinuum source, 450–2400 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/EUV beamline (synchrotron), 5–20 nm.source-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Intensity detector.detector-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ellipsometer.detector-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ideal linear polarizer.polarizer-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ideal circular polarizer (left).polarizer-json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ideal circular polarizer (right).polarizer-json"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.5 -- The built-in catalogue generated once from the code seeds"}
{"number": 36, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.5d", "touches": [], "depends_on": [35], "how_to": "The export tool is thrown away now that the parity facts are green (001 §B: the code seeds are exported ONCE by a throw-away tool; .spec-md §3.6). Delete `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx`, so `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/` holds only `Builtin/`. No project compiles or links the script and no gate runs it, so nothing else changes. The committed catalogue is what the migration produced (.spec-md §7 'Code seeds → catalogue files'): no second export path, script or seed-to-file code remains or is added. The parity facts (step 34) keep proving that the committed files equal the seeds until S1.7 deletes both.", "acceptance": "After the deletion, `git ls-files -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue` MUST list only files under `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/`, and constructor-unit-tests (BuiltInCatalogueParityTests) MUST still pass; and build and the six s05 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.5 -- The built-in catalogue generated once from the code seeds"}
{"number": 37, "anchor": "RENAME_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S1.6a", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0008", "name": "CatalogueImportProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "former_name": "SeedingProxy", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Seeding", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [36, "STORE_XDUO_0008"], "actions": ["RENAME_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingProxyTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "RENAME_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingInMemoryTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests"], "how_to": "The import seam moves into Domain under its new name (001 §B '`SeedingProxy` / `seedAll` become `CatalogueImport`'; .spec-md §3.4, §6 'Import seam'). This step moves and renames only: every behaviour, every fact's assertions (read through the new names) and the seed-fed `seedAll` stay as they are, and step 40 re-sources the orchestrator. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `module CatalogueImport` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `SampleStore.fs` (one `<Compile Include=\"CatalogueImport.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no new comment). It holds the body of module `Seeding` (`OpticalConstructor.Seeding/Seeding.fs:30-130`) with these renames and no other change: `SeedingError` becomes `CatalogueImportError`, and its case `SeedRejectedErr` becomes `ImportRejectedErr`, still `of reason : string`; `SeedingProxy` becomes `CatalogueImportProxy`, still `[<ReferenceEquality>]`, with the four fields `saveCategory`, `saveMaterial`, `saveSample` and `saveLibraryEntry`, each answering `Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>`; and `InMemorySeedStores` becomes `InMemoryCatalogueStores` with its five fields. `seedAll` and `createInMemory` keep their names and bodies, and the file opens what `Seeding.fs` opens, except the namespace it now lives in. The module doc says in one to three lines that this is the library-import seam (spec 0050 §3.4). The 'DECLARED lifecycle' and 'later IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT' paragraphs (`Seeding.fs:10-29`) are dropped, not moved, because the lifecycle they describe has ended, and each member doc names the renamed types. (2) The `OpticalConstructor.Seeding` project is deleted: `Seeding.fs`, `OpticalConstructor.Seeding.fsproj` and the folder with its build output; its `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` entry (`:23-25`); and its one `ProjectReference`, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, with the comment above that reference. `git grep -n \"OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.slnx\"` lists no other. (3) Tests. `SeedingProxyTests.fs` becomes `CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs` (`module CatalogueImportProxyTests`) and `SeedingInMemoryTests.fs` becomes `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` (`module CatalogueImportInMemoryTests`), at the same compile positions. Each opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport` in place of `OpticalConstructor.Seeding.Seeding` and names the renamed types and case, and its module doc names `CatalogueImportProxy`. The two project-file comments above their old entries describe the retired seam and are deleted; none is added. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, except that `a SeedingProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)` becomes `a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)`. (4) The doc comments that name the seam say `CatalogueImportProxy` and 'the catalogue import' instead, in no more words: `CategoryProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` in `MaterialLibrary.fs`, `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` in `MaterialStore.fs`, `SampleProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` in `SampleStore.fs` (`:189-191`), and `LibraryEntryStore` / `createInMemoryEmpty` in `ElementId.fs`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `CatalogueImport.fs` MUST declare `CatalogueImportProxy` with exactly the fields `saveCategory`, `saveMaterial`, `saveSample` and `saveLibraryEntry`; the `OpticalConstructor.Seeding` folder and its `Berreman.slnx` entry MUST NOT exist; `git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|OpticalConstructor.Seeding|SeedingError|SeedRejectedErr|InMemorySeedStores\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged, including the six renamed CatalogueImportProxyTests and CatalogueImportInMemoryTests facts; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SampleStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Seeding/Seeding.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Seeding/OpticalConstructor.Seeding.fsproj", "Berreman/Berreman.slnx", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SeedingProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SeedingInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingProxyTests.seedAll pushes every seed value exactly once, in category-material-sample-entry order through the exact signatures", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.seedAll pushes every seed value exactly once, in category-material-sample-entry order through the exact signatures", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingProxyTests.seedAll stops at the first rejected seed and returns that SeedRejected", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.seedAll stops at the first rejected seed and returns that SeedRejected", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingProxyTests.a SeedingProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingInMemoryTests.seedAll over empty in-memory stores reproduces the seeded catalogue counts", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.seedAll over empty in-memory stores reproduces the seeded catalogue counts", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingInMemoryTests.the fixed seed ids resolve to the same seed instances through the seeded in-memory stores", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the fixed seed ids resolve to the same seed instances through the seeded in-memory stores", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingInMemoryTests.re-seeding the already-seeded in-memory stores is rejected (the store is genuinely stateful)", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.re-seeding the already-seeded in-memory stores is rejected (the store is genuinely stateful)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Seeding.Seeding.SeedingProxy", "op": "rename", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Seeding.Seeding.SeedingError", "op": "rename", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Seeding.Seeding.InMemorySeedStores", "op": "rename", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.InMemoryCatalogueStores", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S16-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 38, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.6b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [33, 34], "how_to": "One name for the shipped catalogue's folder, so the composition roots and the tests read the same files (001 §B 'Shipped catalogue': `<install>\\Catalogue\\Builtin\\`, 'tests load the same files'; .spec-md §3.5). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs` (step 33) gains, beside `create` on the same `type CatalogueProxy with` extension, `static member createBuiltIn () : CatalogueProxy`. It answers `CatalogueProxy.create` over `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"Catalogue\", \"Builtin\")`, the folder that Storage's Content item (step 35) copies into every output referencing Storage. `System.AppContext` is written in full because the Ui's `AppContext` type shares the name. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 §3.5. This is the one place that path is written: `BuiltInCatalogueParityTests`' private `readBuiltIn` (step 34) reads `(CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ()).readCatalogue ()`, and its own `Path.Combine` is deleted. No parameter, cache or fallback folder is added. (2) `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `the Built-in catalogue proxy reads the catalogue the build copies beside the assembly`: `(CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ()).readCatalogue ()` is `Ok`, its manifest's id is `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` and its name `CatalogueName \"Built-in\"`, and it equals the read of `CatalogueProxy.create` over `Catalogue/Builtin` under `AppContext.BaseDirectory`, spelled out in the fact, so the fact states the location independently.", "acceptance": "After the member lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the Built-in catalogue proxy reads the catalogue the build copies beside the assembly` and the five BuiltInCatalogueParityTests facts, now reading through `createBuiltIn`; `BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs` MUST NOT contain `Path.Combine`; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.the Built-in catalogue proxy reads the catalogue the build copies beside the assembly", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-BUILTIN-FOLDER"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 39, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.6c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [32], "how_to": "The two Domain error unions a catalogue import meets gain their honest render, so a composition root logs them without `%A` (ELEV002; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO'), as `StorageError.describe` (step 33) does for Storage. (1) `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `LibraryEntryError` (steps 25-26) gains `member this.describe : string`, one line per case: a fixed phrase naming the case's condition, a colon, and the case's reason; for example `MissingEntryFieldErr reason` renders `an entry field is missing: <reason>`. (2) `CatalogueFiles.fs`: `CatalogueError` (step 32) gains `member this.describe : string` in the same form, and `InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr e` renders its phrase followed by `e.describe`. Each match is complete (FS0025 is an error), and no case, field or other member is added. Tests: `LibraryEntryFilesTests` gains `every library entry error renders its condition and its reason`: each of the six cases, over a distinct test-local reason, renders a distinct text that contains its reason. `CatalogueProxyTests` gains `every catalogue error renders its condition and its reason`: likewise for the six cases, and `InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr (DuplicateEntryVersionErr r)` renders a text containing `(DuplicateEntryVersionErr r).describe`.", "acceptance": "After the renders land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every library entry error renders its condition and its reason` and `every catalogue error renders its condition and its reason`; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.every library entry error renders its condition and its reason", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-ERROR-RENDERS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests.every catalogue error renders its condition and its reason", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-ERROR-RENDERS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 40, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S1.6d", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0008", "name": "CatalogueImportProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [37, 38, 39, "STORE_XDUO_0008"], "how_to": "`seedAll` becomes the import of a parsed catalogue (001 §B: 'the same seam shape, fed from parsed files; the in-memory implementation stays as the test double'; .spec-md §3.4, §5 `CatalogueImport`). In `CatalogueImport.fs` (step 37), which now also opens `LibraryEntryFiles` and `CatalogueFiles`: (1) `CatalogueImportError` keeps `ImportRejectedErr of reason : string` (a store refused an entry) and gains `UndecodableEntryErr of LibraryEntryError` (an entry did not decode into its kind's value) and `CatalogueUnreadableErr of CatalogueError` (the catalogue could not be read), with `member this.describe : string` in step 39's form, rendering a payload through its own `describe`. (2) `seedAll` is deleted, and `member this.importCatalogue (catalogue : CatalogueData) : Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` takes its place. It decodes each envelope of `catalogue.envelopes` with its kind's decoder (step 25: `toMaterialCategory`, `toMaterialEntry`, `toSample`, and `toSourcePreset`, `toPolarizerPreset` and `toDetectorPreset`, wrapped as `SourceItem`, `PolarizerItem` and `DetectorItem`) and pushes it through the matching field: every category, then every material, then every sample, then every preset (source, polarizer and detector), each group in the catalogue's row order. The first decode failure (`UndecodableEntryErr`) or store refusal (`ImportRejectedErr`) stops the import and is answered; the entries pushed before it stay. A sample is pushed through `saveSample` only, because `Library.liveLibrary` (`ElementId.fs:liveLibrary`) serves samples from the samples store. (3) `member this.importFrom (catalogue : CatalogueProxy) : Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` reads the catalogue (`readCatalogue`, step 32), maps a read failure to `CatalogueUnreadableErr`, and imports it. It is the one read-then-import that the composition roots and the test fixture call. (4) `createInMemory` keeps its body: the four empty `createInMemoryEmpty` stores and the four save adapters. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050. No retry, cache, ordering option or other field is added. Tests. (a) `CatalogueImportProxyTests` drives the record through its recording proxy (`recordingProxy`) over the Built-in catalogue read with `CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ()` (step 38), whose envelopes the facts decode for their expectations. `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures`: the tape is every category row, then every material row, then every sample row, then every source, polarizer and detector row, and each channel received exactly the decoded values in row order. `importCatalogue stops at the first rejected entry and answers its ImportRejectedErr`: a proxy refusing every material leaves every category pushed and no sample or preset. `an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr`: over `CatalogueData.tryCreate` (step 32) of the catalogue's first category envelope, a material envelope whose content's `categoryOpt` is `None`, and a sample envelope, the import answers `UndecodableEntryErr (MissingEntryFieldErr _)` after pushing only the category. `every import error renders its condition and its payload`: each case's `describe` contains its reason, or its payload's `describe`. The two seed-fed facts are deleted, and `a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)` keeps its name over the new recording proxy. (b) `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` instantiates the real in-memory stores through `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`. `importFrom fills empty in-memory stores with the whole Built-in catalogue`: after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, `listCategories`, `listMaterials IncludeInactive` and `listSamples IncludeInactive` hold one entry per row of their kind, and `entriesForKind` over `LightSource`, `Detector`, `LinearPolarizer` and `CircularPolarizer`, distinct by `entryId`, holds one entry per preset row. `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value`: each row's decoded value is what `listCategories`, `tryGetMaterial`, `tryGetSample` or `tryGetEntry` answers for its id, compared with `=`. `importing a catalogue the stores already hold is refused`: a second `importCatalogue` of the same catalogue answers `ImportRejectedErr`. `importFrom an unreadable catalogue imports nothing and answers CatalogueUnreadableErr`: over `CatalogueProxy.createInMemory ()` with nothing written, the answer is `CatalogueUnreadableErr (CatalogueIoErr _)` and every store is empty. The three seed-fed facts are deleted.", "acceptance": "After the import lands, `git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing, and constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures`, `importCatalogue stops at the first rejected entry and answers its ImportRejectedErr`, `an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr`, `every import error renders its condition and its payload`, `a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)`, `importFrom fills empty in-memory stores with the whole Built-in catalogue`, `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value`, `importing a catalogue the stores already hold is refused` and `importFrom an unreadable catalogue imports nothing and answers CatalogueUnreadableErr`, which instantiate the real in-memory stores; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.seedAll pushes every seed value exactly once, in category-material-sample-entry order through the exact signatures", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.seedAll stops at the first rejected seed and returns that SeedRejected", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.seedAll over empty in-memory stores reproduces the seeded catalogue counts", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the fixed seed ids resolve to the same seed instances through the seeded in-memory stores", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.re-seeding the already-seeded in-memory stores is rejected (the store is genuinely stateful)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.importCatalogue stops at the first rejected entry and answers its ImportRejectedErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every import error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importFrom fills empty in-memory stores with the whole Built-in catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importing a catalogue the stores already hold is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importFrom an unreadable catalogue imports nothing and answers CatalogueUnreadableErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S16-IMPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 41, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.6e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [40], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests"], "how_to": "The tests' one door to the shipped catalogue (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; .spec-md §3.5): one fixture file compiled into both constructor suites by a link (AGENTS.md: share sources by file-linking). (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs`: `module BuiltinCatalogue` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, the FIRST `<Compile>` item of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, so every test file can open it. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` links it as its first `<Compile>` item, `<Compile Include=\"..\\OpticalConstructor.Tests\\BuiltinCatalogue.fs\" Link=\"BuiltinCatalogue.fs\" />`. No comment is added to either project file. (2) It loads the catalogue once per test process: a private `Lazy<CatalogueData>` over `(CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ()).readCatalogue ()` (step 38) that fails with the error's `describe` (step 39) on first use when the read fails, so no fact runs against a partial catalogue and a test run's start never throws. It exposes, each with a one-line doc: `catalogueData () : CatalogueData`; `freshStores () : InMemoryCatalogueStores`, new in-memory stores (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory`, step 40) filled by `importCatalogue` of the loaded catalogue and failing with the error's `describe` when the import is refused, isolated per call; the decoded entries of each kind in row order, `materials () : MaterialEntry list`, `categories () : MaterialCategory list`, `samples () : Sample list` and `presets () : LibraryEntry list` (sources, polarizers and detectors), which take the seed lists' place for the tests; and the lookups by well-known id, `material (id : MaterialId) : MaterialEntry`, `category (id : CategoryId) : MaterialCategory`, `sample (id : SampleId) : Sample` and `preset (id : ElementValueId) : LibraryEntry`, each failing with the id when the catalogue holds no such entry. Decoding uses step 25's decoders, and a decode failure fails with its `describe`. Nothing else is added: no write, no cache beyond the one load, no seed value. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.fs` (`module BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests`), appended to the compile list after `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs`. `the fixture's fresh stores hold the whole Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call`: the stores of one call list as many categories, materials, samples and presets as the fixture's lists, and removing `SampleIds.glassFilm600Id` from one call's samples leaves a second call's samples holding it. `the fixture resolves the built-ins by their well-known ids`: `material MaterialIds.silicon` is named `Silicon`, `category CategoryIds.vacuumCategory` is `HiddenOnCreate`, `sample SampleIds.multilayerQwId` is named `Quarter-wave glass/vacuum multilayer (41 layers)`, `preset PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer` is the `Ellipsometer` detector, and every entry of the four lists resolves through its own lookup to itself.", "acceptance": "After the fixture lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the fixture's fresh stores hold the whole Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call` and `the fixture resolves the built-ins by their well-known ids`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` MUST compile `BuiltinCatalogue.fs` through its link, and ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.the fixture's fresh stores hold the whole Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-FIXTURE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.the fixture resolves the built-ins by their well-known ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S16-FIXTURE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 42, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.6f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [41], "how_to": "The test-scene default composes from the shipped files (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; .spec-md §3.4, §3.5). It is the composition the TestWindows heads and every `initMain ()` / `initTableAndElementRotation ()` fact run on. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, `module private DefaultStores`: `create ()` builds `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` (step 40) and runs `stores.proxy.importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` (steps 38, 40). On `Error e` it calls `Logger.logError` (`Softellect.Sys.Logging`, as `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs:155` does) with a one-line message carrying `e.describe`, and the scene starts with what was imported; nothing throws. `DefaultStoreSet` keeps its five fields: `materials`, `samples` and `categories` are the import's stores, `sources` is `SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`, and `library` is `liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples sources`. The `Lifecycle`, `MaterialStore` and `SampleStore` opens go if nothing else needs them, and the module's doc says in at most three lines that it composes the scene's stores from the Built-in catalogue. (2) `CatalogueImport.fs`, `createInMemory`: the bundle's `libraryEntries` proxy answers the existing `By kind` grouping for `libraryTrees`, `(Library.createInMemory ()).libraryTrees` (`ElementId.fs:createInMemory`), whose leaves name the built-ins' frozen ids, so the Select bay's rows (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, `libraryState` over `model.library.libraryTrees ()`) are unchanged; its `entriesForKind` and `tryGetEntry` stay the import's. One doc line says so, and no other grouping is built here. Preset order now follows the catalogue's rows; the Select bay (tree order) and the Library window (`LibraryWindowView.fs:sortNodesByLabel`) do not show it, and no ordering is added. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs` gains `the default test scene composes its stores from the Built-in catalogue`: over `initMain ()`, `samples.listSamples IncludeInactive` holds exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()` by id, `materials.listMaterials IncludeInactive` exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`, `categories.listCategories ()` exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`, and `library.tryGetEntry` resolves every `BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()` entry to itself.", "acceptance": "After the switch, constructor-unit-tests and ui-smoke MUST pass, and ui-tests MUST pass over every class that composes the default test scene, including `the default test scene composes its stores from the Built-in catalogue` and LibraryControlsTests' Select-bay facts; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests.the default test scene composes its stores from the Built-in catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S16-TEST-SCENES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S16-TEST-SCENES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.DefaultStores.create", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S16-TEST-SCENES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 43, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.6g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [42], "how_to": "`MainWorkbenchTests` composes its fresh stores the way the App does (`MainWorkbenchTests.fs:68-85`), so they come from the shipped catalogue too (.spec-md §3.4, §3.5). `freshStores ()` answers `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 41) in place of the two self-seeding stores. `mainWith` takes that bundle and calls `initMainWith (liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples (SourceProxy.createInMemory ())) (Experiments.createInMemoryExperiments ()) stores.materials stores.samples stores.categories`, the composition `DefaultStores.create` performs (step 42). The create-picker fact (`:143-146`) reads the bundle's `materials` and `categories` in place of building a category store. The two helpers' docs say they compose from the Built-in catalogue as the App does, and the `Lifecycle`, `MaterialStore` and `SampleStore` opens go if nothing else needs them. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, and `sampleBandsState collapses a period group to x-N bands (the Details-bay shape)` keeps reading `SeedSamples.multilayerQw`.", "acceptance": "After the re-point, `MainWorkbenchTests.fs` MUST NOT call `MaterialProxy.createInMemory`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` or `Library.createInMemory`; ui-tests (MainWorkbenchTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 44, "anchor": "WIRE", "ac": "AC-S1.6h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [43], "how_to": "The product composition root imports the shipped catalogue before any window opens (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`, §3.4). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`, `AppContext.create (settings)`: it builds `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` and runs `stores.proxy.importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. An `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe`, and the app starts with what was imported; nothing throws, as in `DefaultStores.create` (step 42). `materials`, `samples` and `categories` are the import's stores, `sources` is `Library.SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`, and `library` is `Library.liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples sources`. Every other field and the signature are unchanged, so `Program.fs:59` (`Startup.context`, evaluated before `LauncherWindow` opens at `:216`) and every test composition keep their code. The `Lifecycle`, `MaterialStore` and `SampleStore` opens go. (2) The comments the switch makes false say what is true, in no more words: `create`'s doc (`AppContext.fs:69-77`, 'every app start re-seeds') says the stores start empty and are filled from the Built-in catalogue (spec 0050 §3.4); the `VersionsInUse` paragraph (`:79-87`) goes with the store construction it explained; and the `library` field's doc (`:27-29`) says the presets are imported. The self-seeding store docs drop 'the app composition root keeps calling this unchanged': `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` in `MaterialLibrary.fs`, `MaterialProxy.createInMemory` in `MaterialStore.fs` and `SampleProxy.createInMemory` in `SampleStore.fs` (`:183-185`). `liveLibrary`'s doc in `ElementId.fs` says that `presets` is the preset store, which the composition roots fill from the Built-in catalogue. `WireUiCompositionTests`' module doc says that `AppContext.create` fills empty stores from the Built-in catalogue. (3) Tests. `AppContextTests` gains `create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores`: over `freshContext ()`, the samples, materials and categories list exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`, `materials ()` and `categories ()` by id (`IncludeInactive` where the store takes a scope), and `library.tryGetEntry` resolves every `BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()` entry to itself. `two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create re-seeds its own` (`AppContextTests.fs:117-126`) becomes `two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create imports its own`, with its body unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the wiring, `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT call `MaterialProxy.createInMemory`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` or `Library.createInMemory`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including the WireUiCompositionTests and WireUi0040CompositionTests acceptance facts over the real `AppContext.create`; ui-tests MUST pass over AppContextTests, LauncherTests, TableAndElementRotationTests and WireUiFinalCompositionTests, including `create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores` and `two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create imports its own`; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SampleStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S16-APP-ROOT"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create re-seeds its own", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create imports its own", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S16-APP-ROOT"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue"}
{"number": 45, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [44], "how_to": "The tests' fixture gains the store doubles that this section's re-point steps swap in, one for one, for the self-seeding stores S1.7 deletes (001 §B 'tests load the same files', 'the in-memory implementation stays as the test double'; .spec-md §3.3, §3.5). `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests) gains, each with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S1.7: (1) `materialStore (samplesReferencing : MaterialId -> Sample list) (versionsInUse : VersionsInUse) : MaterialProxy`, an empty `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty samplesReferencing versionsInUse` (`MaterialStore.fs`) holding every `materials ()` entry; (2) `sampleStore (versionsInUse : VersionsInUse) : SampleProxy`, an empty `SampleProxy.createInMemoryEmpty versionsInUse` (`SampleStore.fs`) holding every `samples ()` sample; (3) `categoryStore (materialsReferencingCategory : CategoryId -> MaterialEntry list) : CategoryProxy`, an empty `CategoryProxy.createInMemoryEmpty materialsReferencingCategory` (`MaterialLibrary.fs`) holding every `categories ()` category; (4) `library () : LibraryProxy`, the `proxy` of an empty `Library.createInMemoryEmpty ()` store (`ElementId.fs:createInMemoryEmpty`) holding every sample as a `SampleItem` and then every `presets ()` entry, which is what the self-seeding `Library.createInMemory` (`ElementId.fs:createInMemory`, over `seedEntries`) serves today; (5) `sources () : SourcePreset list`, the `SourceItem` presets of `presets ()` in row order, and `source (id : ElementValueId) : SourcePreset`, which fails with the id when no source has it. Each store is filled through its own write verb (`saveMaterial`, `saveSample`, `addCategory`, `addEntry`) in the fixture's row order, and a refusal fails the calling fact with the refused entry and the error, as `freshStores` (step 41) does. Every call builds new stores, so no two facts share state. No cache beyond the one catalogue load, no seed value and no product change is added. (6) `BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests` gains `the fixture's store doubles hold the Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call`: `materialStore (fun _ -> []) VersionsInUse.empty` lists exactly the ids of `materials ()` (`IncludeInactive`), `sampleStore VersionsInUse.empty` those of `samples ()` and `categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` those of `categories ()`; `library ()` resolves every sample's `entryId` and every preset to itself through `tryGetEntry`; `sources ()` holds exactly the `SourceItem` presets of `presets ()`, and `source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator` has tunable limits (`tunableLimitsOpt` matches `Some _`); and removing `SampleIds.glassFilm600Id` from one `sampleStore` leaves a second one holding it.", "acceptance": "After the doubles land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the fixture's store doubles hold the Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call`; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged, the linked fixture compiling in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.the fixture's store doubles hold the Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-FIXTURE-DOUBLES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 46, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [45], "how_to": "A category's name resolves through the categories its caller holds, never through the code seed (001 §B and §R: the code seed values go; the S1.7 brief: they 'resolve through a category list handed in instead (the CategoryProxy's listCategories)', and every caller passes the live store; .spec-md §0.1, `MaterialLibrary.fs` row). Resolution changes here; `standardCategories` itself stays until step 58. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `tryFindCategory (categories : MaterialCategory list) (id : CategoryId) : MaterialCategory option` and `tryFindCategoryByName (categories : MaterialCategory list) (name : CategoryName) : MaterialCategory option` search the list they are given, and `CategoryId.categoryName` becomes `member this.categoryName (categories : MaterialCategory list) : string`: the found category's name, or the id's GUID string for an id the list does not hold, as today. None of the three reads `standardCategories`; each doc is one to three lines saying the caller passes the live category store's `listCategories` (spec 0050 S1.7). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs`: the material category facet (`materialCategoryDef`) becomes a private function of the categories; `materialFacets (categories : MaterialCategory list) : AttributeDef<MaterialEntry> list` and `libraryFacets (categories : MaterialCategory list) (materials : MaterialEntry list) : AttributeDef<LibraryEntry> list` pass them on; the facet's doc says names resolve through the categories given. Every other facet is unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `liveCategoryName` answers `id.categoryName` over the store's `listCategories` (`[]` when the listing fails), and `CategoryProxy.liveMaterialFacets` answers `materialFacets` over the same live list. Its override of the category def's `extract` is deleted, because the shared def now resolves live: one resolution, not two. Their docs say so in no more words. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`: `LibraryWindowContext` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:153`) gains `categories : CategoryProxy` with a one-line doc, and `projectionInputs` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:502`) calls `libraryFacets` with the context's live categories (`[]` when the listing fails). `LibraryWindow.fs` puts its constructor's `categories` argument (`LibraryWindow.fs:34`) into the context. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs`: the view-only identity label resolves the name through `m.context.categories.listCategories ()` (`[]` when it fails). (6) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs`, module `MaterialLibrary`: `dtoToEntry` takes the categories first and resolves the name through `tryFindCategoryByName categories`; `FileName.importMaterials (categories : MaterialCategory list)` and `FileName.exportMaterials (categories : MaterialCategory list) (entries : MaterialEntry list)` pass them on; the DTO doc, the `dtoToEntry` comment and the export's category comment say the categories are the caller's. (7) The callers in the tests pass the fixture's categories (step 41): `materialFacets`, `libraryFacets`, `importMaterials` and `exportMaterials` take `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()` in `LibraryFacetsTests`, `PolarizerBehaviorTests` and `ExportImportTests`. Every `LibraryWindowContext` record that `LibraryWindowTests`, `LightSourceEditorTests` (`libraryContext`) and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` (`libraryContext`) build gets `categories = BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` (step 45), or the fact's own category store where the fact builds one. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions. (8) Facts. `CategoryProxyTests` gains `a category resolves by id and by name through the list it is given`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()` with Glass renamed to a test-local name, `tryFindCategory` answers the renamed record for `CategoryIds.glass`, `tryFindCategoryByName` finds it by the new name and answers `None` for `Glass`, and `CategoryIds.glass.categoryName` is the new name; over `[]`, `tryFindCategory` answers `None` and `categoryName` the id's GUID string. `LibraryFacetsTests` gains `the category facet names each material's category through the categories it is given`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`, the category facet of `materialFacets (BuiltinCatalogue.categories ())` keys Silicon (`MaterialIds.silicon`) by `Semiconductor`, and by the new name when Semiconductor (`CategoryIds.semiconductor`) is renamed in the list handed in. No cache, fallback catalogue or second resolution path is added.", "acceptance": "After the switch, `tryFindCategory`, `tryFindCategoryByName` and `CategoryId.categoryName` MUST NOT read `standardCategories`, and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` MUST NOT name it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a category resolves by id and by name through the list it is given` and `the category facet names each material's category through the categories it is given`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, every renamed-category fact included; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxyTests.a category resolves by id and by name through the list it is given", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests.the category facet names each material's category through the categories it is given", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.tryFindCategory", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.tryFindCategoryByName", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.CategoryId.categoryName", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.materialFacets", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.libraryFacets", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindowView.LibraryWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.MaterialLibrary.importMaterials", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.MaterialLibrary.exportMaterials", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-CATEGORY-LIST"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 47, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [45], "how_to": "The Library's 'By kind' grouping is derived from the entries it holds, so no grouping tree is seed data (the S1.7 brief: 'the By kind grouping is DERIVED by a pure function over the library's entries (kind, then category / facet, then leaf)'; .spec-md §3.3 'grouping trees' are deleted). `liveLibrary` and its one product consumer, the `model.library.libraryTrees ()` match in `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` (`libraryState`), keep their shapes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, type `LibraryTree`: `static member byKind (entries : LibraryEntry list) : LibraryTree`, pure, with a doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S1.7. Its name is `TreeName \"By kind\"` and its root `Group (TreeLabel \"Library\", groups)`. The groups are `Samples`, `Sources`, `Detectors` and `Polarizers`, in that order, and a kind with no entry has no group. Under `Samples`, one group per `SubstrateKind` present, in the order `Thin films` (`ThinFilm`), `Thick plates` (`ThickPlate`) and `Mirrors` (`Mirror`). Under `Sources`, `Fixed lines` (`FixedLine`) and then `Tunable` (`TunableBetween`). Under `Polarizers`, one group per `PolarizerCategory` present, in the union's case order, labelled by its `label`. Detectors carry no facet, so their leaves sit directly under `Detectors`. A leaf is `Leaf (entry.entryName.toTreeLabel, entry.entryId)`, and the leaves keep the order of the entries given. (2) `liveLibrary` (`ElementId.fs:liveLibrary`): `libraryTrees` answers `[ LibraryTree.byKind entries ]`, where the entries are those its own `entriesForKind` offers for `CatalogueKind.Sample`, `LightSource`, `Detector`, `LinearPolarizer` and `CircularPolarizer`, distinct by `entryId`; the first listing error passes through, as `entriesForKind`'s does. So a sample created in the samples store and a user source join the tree. Its doc's '`libraryTrees` stays the seeded grouping' says the tree is derived. (3) `createInMemoryEmpty` (`ElementId.fs:createInMemoryEmpty`): the store's `libraryTrees` answers `Ok [ LibraryTree.byKind held ]` over the entries it holds, in place of `Ok []`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, `createInMemory`: the bundle's `libraryEntries` is the store's own `proxy` again; step 42's override that answered the seeded tree (`(Library.createInMemory ()).libraryTrees`) and its doc line are deleted. The self-seeding `createInMemory` keeps `seedTrees` until step 58. No other grouping, ordering or option is added. (5) Facts, in `LibraryProxyTests`: `the By kind tree groups entries by kind, then facet, then leaf`: `LibraryTree.byKind` over a test-local list (the fixture's `SampleIds.glassFilm200Id` thin film and `SampleIds.euvMoSiId` mirror as `SampleItem`s, `PresetIds.heNe633` and `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator` from `BuiltinCatalogue.preset`, the ellipsometer, and the linear and left circular polarizers) equals the expected tree written out in the fact, and over `[]` it is the root with no group; `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds`: `Library.createInMemoryEmpty ()` answers the empty tree, and after `addEntry` of the intensity detector a tree with that one leaf under `Detectors`; `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`, with a user source saved under `newSourceId ()` and a sample saved under `newSampleId ()`, the leaf ids of `liveLibrary`'s tree are exactly the distinct entry ids `entriesForKind` offers for the five kinds, each once, both new entries included. In `LibraryControlsTests`: `the Select bay lists a sample created in the samples store under its geometry`: over `initMain ()`, a copy of `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.euvMoSiId` (a `Mirror`) under `newSampleId ()` and a test-local name, saved in the scene's `samples` store, appears with a Sample element selected as a leaf row of `libraryState` under the `Mirrors` group row.", "acceptance": "After the derivation, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs` MUST NOT call the self-seeding `Library.createInMemory`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the By kind tree groups entries by kind, then facet, then leaf`, `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds` and `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once`; ui-smoke MUST pass, the Select-bay re-render fact included; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Select bay lists a sample created in the samples store under its geometry` and LibraryControlsTests' Select-bay facts; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.the By kind tree groups entries by kind, then facet, then leaf", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-DERIVED-TREE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-DERIVED-TREE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-DERIVED-TREE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests.the Select bay lists a sample created in the samples store under its geometry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S17-DERIVED-TREE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Library.LibraryTree.byKind", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "obligations": ["S17-DERIVED-TREE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 48, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [45], "how_to": "The Details bay names a band's material through the scene's live materials store, not through the code seed (001 §R: the code seed values go; .spec-md §0.1 `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` row). The colour maps keep reading `MaterialIds` (the S1.7 brief: Schematic.fs and the colour map keep the well-known ids): `bandColors` and `Schematic.fs`'s curated colours are unchanged, except that the curated map's doc keys it by `MaterialIds` and no longer names `MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries`. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) the private `materialLibrary` (`= MaterialLibrary.standard`, the composition-root comment above it included) is deleted; (2) `MaterialId.bandDisplayName` becomes `member private materialId.bandDisplayName (materials : MaterialLibrary.MaterialProxy) : string`: the name of `materials.tryGetMaterial materialId`'s entry, or the id's GUID string when the store holds none or the lookup fails, so an unknown id still labels its band as today; (3) `Sample.bandsState` becomes `member s.bandsState (materials : MaterialLibrary.MaterialProxy) : LayerBandsControls.LayerBandsControlsState` and passes the store to each band; (4) `detailsState` passes `model.materials`. The docs say the names come from the materials store in no more words. No cache and no second lookup is added. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs`: `sampleBandsState collapses a period group to x-N bands (the Details-bay shape)` reads `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.multilayerQwId).bandsState (BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()).materials`, with its assertions unchanged, and the class gains `the band view names each band's material through the materials store it is given`: over the fixture's fresh materials store the quarter-wave stack's three band labels start with `Transparent glass (n = 1.52)`, `Vacuum` and `Transparent glass (n = 1.52)`, and over an empty `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty (fun _ -> []) VersionsInUse.empty` each label starts with its material's GUID string.", "acceptance": "After the switch, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs` MUST NOT name `MaterialLibrary.standard`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `sampleBandsState collapses a period group to x-N bands (the Details-bay shape)` and `the band view names each band's material through the materials store it is given`; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/Schematic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests.the band view names each band's material through the materials store it is given", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S17-BAND-NAMES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.bandsState", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S17-BAND-NAMES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 49, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [45], "how_to": "The Material editor window takes its category store from its caller, so no product code builds a self-seeding store (the S1.7 brief: the self-seeding `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` goes; .spec-md §3.3). The product's one opener already passes the shared store (`MaterialsWindow.fs:70`, `categories = categories`), and it keeps doing so, now to the mandatory parameter. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs`: the optional `?categories : CategoryProxy` constructor parameter becomes the mandatory third parameter `categories : CategoryProxy`, and the constructor's `defaultArg categories (CategoryProxy.createInMemory (fun _ -> []))` and the comment describing that default are deleted; the context takes `categories` directly. The class doc names the parameter in no more words. (2) Every test that opens the window without a store passes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` (step 45), which holds what the deleted default held: `EmbeddedChartTests`, `MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `MaterialsWindowTests`, `SampleEditorWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests` and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`; a test that already passes a store keeps it. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions.", "acceptance": "After the change, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs` MUST NOT name `createInMemory` or `defaultArg categories`; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/EmbeddedChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SampleEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 50, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [44], "how_to": "A seed list that holds no library value goes first: `Experiments.seedExperiments` (`Experiments.fs:seedExperiments`), the dark-line template that `createInMemoryExperiments` closes over (the S1.7 brief names it; .spec-md §3.3: every other seed value is deleted). It holds no library value, and no product code reads `listExperiments` or `tryGetExperiment`: the Experiments bay builds experiments against the scene. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `seedExperiments` and its doc are deleted; `createInMemoryExperiments ()` keeps its signature and answers `Ok []` from `listExperiments` and `Ok None` from `tryGetExperiment`; its doc says, in one to three lines, that the in-memory proxy holds no experiment (spec 0050 S1.7). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs`: `listExperiments returns at least one seed template` and `tryGetExperiment hits a known seed id and misses an unknown one` assert the deleted seed, so they are deleted, and `the in-memory experiments proxy lists no experiment` (`listExperiments ()` is `Ok []`) and `the in-memory experiments proxy resolves no experiment id` (`tryGetExperiment` of `ExperimentId 1` and of `ExperimentId 9999` is `Ok None`) take their place, so the class's count is unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`: the fact reading `seedExperiments |> List.head` builds its dark line as a test-local `Experiment` with the deleted seed's fields (`ExperimentId 1`, an empty setup, `varied = None`, `CaptureTransmitted`, `VariableRange.forVariable VaryR1`, no data file, no source wavelength), and its assertions are unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the deletion, `git grep -n -F \"seedExperiments\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged, including `the in-memory experiments proxy lists no experiment` and `the in-memory experiments proxy resolves no experiment id`; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.listExperiments returns at least one seed template", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S17-NO-SEED-EXPERIMENTS"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.tryGetExperiment hits a known seed id and misses an unknown one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S17-NO-SEED-EXPERIMENTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.the in-memory experiments proxy lists no experiment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-NO-SEED-EXPERIMENTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.the in-memory experiments proxy resolves no experiment id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-NO-SEED-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.seedExperiments", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S17-NO-SEED-EXPERIMENTS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S17-NO-SEED-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 51, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [45, 46], "how_to": "The constructor suite's material and category facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, a few files per step, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/`: `CategoryEditorTests.fs`, `CategoryProxyTests.fs`, `MaterialProxyTests.fs`, `MaterialComplexityTests.fs`, `MaterialPreviewTests.fs`, `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `StackEditTests.fs`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`, `ExportImportTests.fs`, `CanonicalJsonTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `MaterialPreviewTests`' `builtInEntries |> List.head` is Silicon, so it becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.material MaterialIds.silicon`; `DispersionModelsTests` and `StackEditTests` resolve against `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`, the fact that prepends an entry included; `CategoryEditorTests` opens the editor on `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()` and counts against it; `CategoryProxyTests` and `MaterialProxyTests` build their stores through `categoryStore` and `materialStore` with their own lookups and `VersionsInUse` values; `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`' Silicon is `BuiltinCatalogue.material MaterialIds.silicon`; `ExportImportTests` exports the fixture's described materials, filtered as before; `CanonicalJsonTests`' absorbing built-in is `BuiltinCatalogue.material MaterialIds.euvMolybdenum`.", "acceptance": "After the re-point, `git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory |[^A-Za-z]standard[^A-Za-z]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryEditorTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialPreviewTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StackEditTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialPreviewTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StackEditTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 52, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [45, 47], "how_to": "The constructor suite's sample, source and Library facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/`: `SampleProxyTests.fs`, `PropagationTests.fs`, `ExperimentProxyTests.fs`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs`, `ExperimentRunTests.fs`, `PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs`, `LibraryProxyTests.fs`, `SourceLibraryTests.fs`, `PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `LibraryProxyTests`' module proxy is `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, and its fact `libraryTrees returns at least one tree and every leaf entry id resolves` now runs over the derived tree (step 47) with its assertions unchanged; `SourceLibraryTests` builds every Library through `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()` and `sampleStore`, its unqualified `createInMemory ()` included, so it calls no `createInMemory` but `SourceProxy.createInMemory`; `the seeded tree lists every seeded source under Sources` collects the `Sources` group's leaves recursively, as its `leaves` already does, and compares them with the ids of `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()` order-independently, because the derived tree lists fixed lines before tunable sources; `PlacedSampleEmissionTests`' library is `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()` and its three ids are the `toElementValueId` of `SampleIds.euvMoSiId`, `glassFilm600Id` and `glassPlate1mmId`; `ExperimentRunTests` checks the four tunable `PresetIds` sources of the rules; `PropagationTests` builds its material store through `materialStore` and resolves `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`.", "acceptance": "After the re-point, `git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs MUST find nothing, and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs` MUST NOT contain `(createInMemory ())`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 53, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [45, 46], "how_to": "The constructor suite's facet and library-file facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/`: `LibraryFacetsTests.fs`, `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs`, `EntryFileJsonTests.fs`, `CatalogueFolderTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `LibraryFacetsTests`' corpora are the fixture's lists (`libraryDefs` is `libraryFacets (BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()) (BuiltinCatalogue.materials ())`), and its kind count reads `List.length (BuiltinCatalogue.sources ())`; `LibraryEntryFilesTests` and `CatalogueFolderTests` take their sample values by well-known id (Langasite `MaterialIds.langasite`, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`, the tunable `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`, the ellipsometer `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`, Glass `CategoryIds.glass`); `EntryFileJsonTests`' `a multilayer sample entry file round-trips`, `a tunable source entry file round-trips` and `a detector and a category entry file round-trip` take theirs the same way (`SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId`, `CategoryIds.vacuumCategory`), and `every built-in seals, writes, reads and decodes equal to its seed` and `the built-ins form one catalogue with unique file names per kind` run over every value of `materials ()`, `categories ()`, `samples ()` and `presets ()`, sealed at version 1 under the same test catalogue id.", "acceptance": "After the re-point, `git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 54, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [45, 49], "how_to": "The UI suite's material, category and sample-editor facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/`: `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `MaterialsWindowTests.fs`, `EmbeddedChartTests.fs`, `NkDispersionChartTests.fs`, `CategoryEditorWindowTests.fs`, `SampleEditorWindowTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `MaterialEditorWindowTests`' `builtIn` helper reads `BuiltinCatalogue.material`; `SampleEditorWindowTests`' stub material proxy answers from `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`, and every `initSampleEditor context builtInEntries` passes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `CategoryEditorWindowTests`' stub proxy starts from `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()` and counts against it; the stores of `MaterialsWindowTests`, `EmbeddedChartTests` and `NkDispersionChartTests` come from the doubles.", "acceptance": "After the re-point, `git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/EmbeddedChartTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/CategoryEditorWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SampleEditorWindowTests.fs MUST find nothing; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the touched classes with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/EmbeddedChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/CategoryEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SampleEditorWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 55, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [45, 46], "how_to": "The UI suite's Library-window and scene facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/`: `LibraryWindowTests.fs`, `InverseConstructorTests.fs`, `LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`, `ScrollExtentTests.fs`, `WindowLauncherTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `LibraryWindowTests`' `seededCorpus` counts `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()` plus `BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`, its kind counts read `List.length (BuiltinCatalogue.sources ())`, and its Library is `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; the scenes of `InverseConstructorTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `WindowLauncherTests` and `OutOfBandBadgeTests` compose over the doubles; `LightSourceEditorTests` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` build their `libraryContext` over them; `FsxAcceptanceTests` composes its scene's stores through `materialStore`, `sampleStore`, `categoryStore` and `library ()`, and saves its script materials into them as before, so every script comparison keeps its numbers.", "acceptance": "After the re-point, `git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WindowLauncherTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs MUST find nothing; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the touched classes with their counts unchanged, FsxAcceptanceTests' script comparisons included; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WindowLauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 56, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [45, 48], "how_to": "The UI suite's remaining seed readers, which bind or show a seeded sample, read the shipped catalogue instead (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/`: `AppContextTests.fs`, `ElementMenuTests.fs`, `ExperimentControlsTests.fs`, `LayerBandsControlsTests.fs`, `LibraryControlsTests.fs`, `SourceAndDetectorMoveTests.fs`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs`, `WireUiCompositionTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Each of these files names a seeded sample (`SeedSamples.<name>` or its `id`), which becomes its `SampleIds` member or `BuiltinCatalogue.sample`. After this step no constructor or UI test calls a self-seeding store, which step 58 relies on when it gives the empty stores the plain name.", "acceptance": "After the re-point, `git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` MUST find nothing, so neither test suite names a seed or calls a self-seeding store; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the touched classes with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementMenuTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SourceAndDetectorMoveTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 57, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [45], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests", "ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests"], "how_to": "The bridge between the code seeds and the shipped files goes, and a fact that needs no seed guards the files (the S1.7 brief: delete S1.5's parity class without a successor, because the bridge is gone, and add a catalogue-integrity fact in its place; .spec-md §7 'Code seeds → catalogue files': the parity test proved the migration once). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs` (steps 34 and 38) is deleted with its compile entry; its five facts, which compare the files with the seeds, go with it, and nothing replaces them. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.fs` (`module BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests`), compiled where the parity file was, with a module doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S1.7 and one fact, `the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present`: `(CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ()).readCatalogue ()` (step 38) is `Ok`, which means every entry file validated against its kind's schema, carried its schema version and matched its own content hash, and the manifest matched the entries (steps 30-33); the manifest's id is `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, its name `CatalogueName \"Built-in\"` and its version `VersionNumber.first`; every manifest row's `contentHash` equals both the `contentHash` of the envelope with its id and version and the `contentHashOf` of that envelope's content recomputed here (step 27); the envelopes' `LibraryEntryId`s are distinct across all kinds; and every kind of `LibraryEntryKind.all` has rows, 12 materials, 5 categories, 11 samples, 28 sources, 3 polarizers and 2 detectors. The counts are the committed catalogue's (step 35); a later section that adds a built-in kind or entry changes them in the step that adds it.", "acceptance": "After the swap, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs` MUST NOT exist and nothing under `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/` MUST name BuiltInCatalogueParityTests; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present`, its count falling by four (five parity facts deleted, one fact added); and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.the built-in catalogue is the Built-in catalogue at version 1", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S17-INTEGRITY"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.every built-in material and category in the catalogue equals its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S17-INTEGRITY"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.every built-in sample in the catalogue equals its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S17-INTEGRITY"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.every built-in source, detector and polarizer in the catalogue equals its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S17-INTEGRITY"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.the built-in catalogue is exactly what the seeds seal to, and its manifest hash is stable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S17-INTEGRITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S17-INTEGRITY"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 58, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.7j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [50, 51, 52, 53, 54, 55, 56, 57], "how_to": "The code seed values go, and with them the stores that seed themselves (001 §B: 'then the Domain seed values are deleted'; 001 §R 'The code seed values and seedAll's Domain source'; .spec-md §3.3). The well-known ids stay: `MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds` and `CatalogueIds`, read by the default-scene prebinds, the colour maps and the tests. Nothing reads a seed any more (steps 46-57). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `standardCategories`, `builtInEntries`, `standard`, the private complexities of the built-ins and every private helper only they use (the `ConstantEpsValue.constantComplexity` extension and any interval or index value left for them) are deleted, and so is the self-seeding `CategoryProxy.createInMemory`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `SeedSamples`, `SeedSources`, `seedEntries`, `sampleLeaf`, `seedTrees` and the self-seeding `createInMemory` are deleted, with the private builders only they use (`filmStructure`, `plateStructure`, `euvLayerThickness`); `qwGlassThickness` and `qwVacuumThickness` stay for `starterMultilayerStructure`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs` and `SampleStore.fs`: the self-seeding `MaterialProxy.createInMemory` and `SampleProxy.createInMemory` are deleted. (4) The plain names are free now, so each empty store takes it (the S1.7 brief; ELEV015 / ELEV019 hold, one member per receiver and one free `createInMemory`): `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty`, `SampleProxy.createInMemoryEmpty`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` and `Library.createInMemoryEmpty` become `createInMemory` with unchanged signatures and bodies, and every caller follows: `CatalogueImport.fs` (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory`), the fixture `BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 45) and `MainWorkbenchTests` (step 48); a doc naming `createInMemoryEmpty` (the Domain store docs, `CatalogueFiles.fs`' in-memory double) names `createInMemory`. Step 56 left no caller of a self-seeding store, and before the rename `git grep -n -E \"(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor` MUST list only the declarations and docs this step edits (S1.6 steps 42 and 44 and step 49 removed the product's calls), so every renamed call means what it meant; a call anywhere else is a missed re-point and stops the step with its question. (5) Docs and comments say what is true, in no more words: the `MaterialLibrary` and `Library` module docs; `MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `MaterialId`, `CategoryId`, `SampleId`, `SampleIds` and `PresetIds`, which become the identities of the Built-in catalogue's entries (spec 0050 §3.3); the category and store docs that described a seeded catalogue or a self-seeding store; `MaterialVersionId.firstOf` and `SampleVersionId.firstOf`; `LibraryEntryStore`; `liveLibrary`; the `open` comments in `CatalogueImport.fs`; and any `LibraryFacets.fs` doc naming a deleted value. (6) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE' (`AGENTS.md:574-578`): the presets are the preset store that `AppContext.create` fills from the Built-in catalogue (`Catalogue/Builtin/`, `CatalogueImportProxy.importFrom`), and the built-in lasers and UV / EUV lithography sources are protected presets named by `PresetIds`. No seed, no seeding helper and no compatibility alias is kept, and `open`s nothing needs go.", "acceptance": "After the deletion, `git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|allSeedSamples|allSeedSources\" -- Berreman/ AGENTS.md` MUST find nothing; `git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` (001 §T 'From section 1') MUST find nothing; `git grep -n -F \"createInMemoryEmpty\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; `MaterialLibrary.fs` MUST NOT declare `standard`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SampleStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted"}
{"number": 59, "anchor": "RETIRE_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S2.1a", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0007", "name": "TestDbContext", "kind": "component", "language": "csharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Database", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Database", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.App"], "depends_on": [58], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.TestDbMigrationTests"], "how_to": "The EF Core wiring proof goes with its only consumer and its MSSQL settings; the library model replaces it in the next step (001 §R 'The `Test` EF table and its initial migration'; 001 §C 'No migrations'; .spec-md §3.18 'One local database', §7 '`Test` EF table + migration → library model'). This step only deletes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Database/`: delete `Test.cs`, `TestDbContext.cs` and the `Migrations/` folder with its three files (`20260711000000_Initial.cs`, `20260711000000_Initial.Designer.cs`, `TestDbContextModelSnapshot.cs`). In `OpticalConstructor.Database.csproj`, delete the Spec 0038 Part M comment block above the first `PropertyGroup`: it says the project only proves EF wiring and that no product project references it, and both stop being true here and in the next step. Its properties, its NU1903 comment and its `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite` reference stay, so the project compiles with no source for this one step. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/`: delete `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` and `fixtures/database-appsettings.json`. In `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, delete the `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` compile item with its comment, the `fixtures\\database-appsettings.json` Content item with its comment, the `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite` PackageReference with its comment, and the `OpticalConstructor.App` and `OpticalConstructor.Database` ProjectReferences with their shared comment. `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` is the only test file that opens `OpticalConstructor.App`, `OpticalConstructor.Database` or EF Core, and the next step's tests reach the model and EF Core through Storage's reference. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`, module `ConfigKey`: delete `databaseProvider` (`:44-48`) and `mssqlConnectionString` (`:50-53`) with their docs, because their only reader was `TestDbMigrationTests` (.spec-md §3.18; 001 §W excludes cloud or shared databases). `sqliteConnectionString` (`:55-58`) stays; its doc becomes one line saying it is the library database's SQLite connection string, read through `AppSettingsProvider.tryGetConnectionString` (001 §C 'Settings'; spec 0050). The module doc (`:14-20`) drops '— and the Part M storage proof (step 040) —'. No other key, default or comment changes, and `OpticalConstructor.App/appsettings.json` is untouched, because it holds no database key. Nothing replaces the deleted facts: `TestDbMigrationTests`' seven cases (the four `DatabaseProvider.tryCreate` rows, the unknown-provider fact, the provider-choice fact and the migration fact) lower the constructor suite's count on purpose.", "acceptance": "After the retirement, `Test.cs`, `TestDbContext.cs`, the `Migrations/` folder, `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` and `fixtures/database-appsettings.json` MUST NOT exist; `git grep -n -i -E \"TestDbContext|TestDbMigrationTests|database-appsettings|DatabaseProvider|mssql|EFC-wiring\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with exactly `TestDbMigrationTests`' seven cases fewer; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/Test.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/TestDbContext.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/Migrations/20260711000000_Initial.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/Migrations/20260711000000_Initial.Designer.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/Migrations/TestDbContextModelSnapshot.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/OpticalConstructor.Database.csproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/fixtures/database-appsettings.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.TestDbMigrationTests.DatabaseProvider.tryCreate parses the enumerated choice", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs", "obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.TestDbMigrationTests.DatabaseProvider.tryCreate rejects an unknown provider", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs", "obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.TestDbMigrationTests.appsettings selects the SQLite provider through the step-5 ConfigKey", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs", "obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.TestDbMigrationTests.the initial migration creates and round-trips the Test table against SQLite", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs", "obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.ConfigKey.databaseProvider", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"], "preserves_obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.ConfigKey.mssqlConnectionString", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"], "preserves_obligations": ["S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.1 -- The library model in EF Core, created without migrations"}
{"number": 60, "anchor": "ADD_COMPONENT", "ac": "AC-S2.1b", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0002", "name": "LibraryDbContext", "kind": "component", "language": "csharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Database", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Database", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [59], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests"], "how_to": "The library model in EF Core, holding slow data only (001 §C 'What it holds', 'What it never holds', 'Hybrid shape'; .spec-md §5 '`LibraryDbContext` + entities'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Database/LibraryEntities.cs`, namespace `OpticalConstructor.Database`: seven sealed entity classes with public get/set properties, each with a `<summary>` of one to three lines citing 001 §C and spec 0050. Their names carry `Library`, so no F# type name collides with them (ELEV014). (a) `LibraryEntryVersionRow`, one immutable version of a library entry: `Guid EntryId`, `int Version`, `int Kind` (the `LibraryEntryKind` tag), `string Name`, `int Lifecycle`, `int Protection`, `int PinState`, `int ProvenanceKind`, `Guid? CatalogueId` (the catalogue a built-in ships in, else null), `string PayloadText` (the entry file's canonical text, byte for byte) and `string ContentHash`. (b) `LibraryLatestVersionRow`, the local 'latest' of one entry: `Guid EntryId`, `int Version`. (c) `LibraryEntryFacetRow`: `Guid EntryId`, `int Version`, `string FacetKey`, `string FacetValue`. (d) `LibrarySampleMaterialRow`: `Guid SampleId`, `int SampleVersion`, `Guid MaterialId`, `int MaterialVersion`. (e) `LibraryCatalogueImportRow`, the catalogue-import log: `Guid CatalogueId`, `string Folder`, `string ManifestHash`, `DateTime ImportedAtUtc`, `int EntryCount`. (f) `LibraryPulledSourceRow`, a record pulled from an online source and the version it minted (001 §D): `Guid EntryId`, `int Version`, `string Source`, `string RecordPath`, `string SourceVersion` (a snapshot date or a commit), `string Licence`, `string Citation`. (g) `LibrarySchemaStampRow`: `int Id`, `int SchemaVersion`. Every string property is initialised, so nullable reference types raise no warning. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Database/LibraryDbContext.cs`: `public class LibraryDbContext : DbContext` with the constructor `LibraryDbContext(DbContextOptions<LibraryDbContext> options)` and one `DbSet` per entity: `EntryVersions`, `LatestVersions`, `EntryFacets`, `SampleMaterials`, `CatalogueImports`, `PulledSources`, `SchemaStamps`. `OnModelCreating` pins with the fluent API: each table's name (`EntryVersion`, `LatestVersion`, `EntryFacet`, `SampleMaterial`, `CatalogueImport`, `PulledSource`, `SchemaStamp`); the keys, with every key property `ValueGeneratedNever()` so a key is always the caller's: `EntryVersion` (`EntryId`, `Version`), `LatestVersion` (`EntryId`), `EntryFacet` and `SampleMaterial` (all four columns), `CatalogueImport` (`CatalogueId`), `PulledSource` (`EntryId`, `Version`) and `SchemaStamp` (`Id`); every string column required; the foreign keys to `EntryVersion` (`EntryId`, `Version`): from `LatestVersion` with delete restricted, because a latest names a held version, and from `EntryFacet`, `PulledSource` and `SampleMaterial`'s (`SampleId`, `SampleVersion`) with delete cascading; and the indexes the queries read: `EntryVersion.Kind`, `EntryVersion.CatalogueId`, `EntryFacet` (`FacetKey`, `FacetValue`), `SampleMaterial` (`MaterialId`, `MaterialVersion`) and `PulledSource` (`Source`, `RecordPath`). A sample's material side is an indexed key, not a foreign key, so a sample version can be stored before the material versions it names. The model holds nothing a kit carries, no measured data and no preference (001 §C 'What it never holds'). The class doc says the database is created by `EnsureCreated` and stamped, never migrated (001 §C 'No migrations'). No migration, design-time factory, `HasData` seeding or second provider is added. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` gains `<ProjectReference Include=\"..\\OpticalConstructor.Database\\OpticalConstructor.Database.csproj\" />` beside its Domain reference, with no comment. Storage owns the F# side of the database (.spec-md §5), and every Storage consumer reaches the model through it. No F# product code uses it in this step. Through Storage, Ui, the App, the TestWindows heads and both constructor test suites now carry EF Core, and each MUST build with zero warnings from our code, `MSB3277` included (AGENTS.md). (4) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs` (`module LibraryDatabaseTests`), appended to the compile list with no comment. It reaches EF Core, `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite` and the model through Storage's reference, and its module doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S2.1. Fact `the library model creates exactly its seven tables and their columns`: over a `SqliteConnection` to `Data Source=:memory:` that the fact opens and disposes, `Database.EnsureCreated ()` of a `LibraryDbContext` built with `DbContextOptionsBuilder<LibraryDbContext>().UseSqlite(connection)` answers `true`. `sqlite_master` then lists exactly the tables `CatalogueImport`, `EntryFacet`, `EntryVersion`, `LatestVersion`, `PulledSource`, `SampleMaterial` and `SchemaStamp` (names starting `sqlite_` excluded), and each table's column names (`pragma_table_info`), compared as sets, are exactly those listed in (1). A second `EnsureCreated ()` answers `false`.", "acceptance": "After the model lands, `OpticalConstructor.Database` MUST hold `LibraryDbContext` and its seven entities and no migration, and `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` MUST reference `OpticalConstructor.Database.csproj`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the library model creates exactly its seven tables and their columns`; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/LibraryEntities.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/LibraryDbContext.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.the library model creates exactly its seven tables and their columns", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-LIBRARY-MODEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Database.LibraryDbContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/LibraryDbContext.cs", "obligations": ["S21-LIBRARY-MODEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.1 -- The library model in EF Core, created without migrations"}
{"number": 61, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.1c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [60], "how_to": "The closed sets a version row stores get their disk tags, and a sample's material references keep their versions (001 §C 'Hybrid shape': lifecycle, protection, pin and the sample-version → material-version keys are relational columns; AGENTS.md: a closed set's disk tag is a 1-based `int`, read back by `tryOfDb`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs`: `EntryLifecycle` (`:31-33`) gains `member this.value : int` (`ActiveEntry` 1, `InactiveEntry` 2) and `static member tryOfDb (v : int) : EntryLifecycle option`, which answers `None` for any other tag. Directly after it, new `PinState` = `VersionPinned` | `VersionUnpinned`, with `value` (1, 2) and `tryOfDb` the same way. Its doc is one to three lines: whether a library version is pinned; a pin is one-way, set when a kit first references the version or when it is exported, and a pinned version never mutates (001 §C 'Pinned replaces VersionsInUse'; spec 0050). This step adds the type only: `VersionsInUse` and every store are unchanged. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `EntryProtection` (`ElementId.fs:EntryProtection`) gains `value` (`ProtectedBuiltIn` 1, `UserManaged` 2) and `tryOfDb` the same way. `SampleStructure` gains `member this.referencedMaterialVersions : Set<MaterialVersionId>`: every material version the structure references (each film layer, a `Repeated` group's cell counted once; the substrate plate; the lower half-space), each kept at its own version. `referencedMaterials` (`ElementId.fs:SampleStructure.referencedMaterials`) becomes that set projected to `materialId`, so the structure is walked in one place; its doc says so in no more words. Each new member's doc is one line citing spec 0050. No other type, member or caller changes. (3) Tests. `LifecycleTests` gains `lifecycle, protection and pin states round-trip their database tags`: each of the six cases answers its tag above, `tryOfDb` of each tag answers its case, and `tryOfDb` of 0 and of 3 answers `None` for all three sets. `MaterialProxyTests` gains `referencedMaterialVersions keeps every referenced material version, a repeated cell once`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.multilayerQwId).structure.referencedMaterialVersions` is exactly `MaterialVersionId.firstOf` of `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial`; `SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId`'s is exactly `firstOf` of `MaterialIds.langasite` and `MaterialIds.silicon`; and a test-local structure whose one film layer names `{ materialId = MaterialIds.glass152; version = VersionNumber.first.next }` over a lower half-space at `MaterialVersionId.firstOf MaterialIds.glass152` answers both versions, while its `referencedMaterials` is `MaterialIds.glass152` alone. The fact `referencedMaterials covers films, repeated cells, the substrate plate, and the lower half-space` (`MaterialProxyTests.fs`) passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the tags land, `EntryLifecycle`, `EntryProtection` and `PinState` MUST each carry `value` and `tryOfDb`, and `referencedMaterials` MUST be the projection of `referencedMaterialVersions`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `lifecycle, protection and pin states round-trip their database tags`, `referencedMaterialVersions keeps every referenced material version, a repeated cell once` and the unchanged `referencedMaterials covers films, repeated cells, the substrate plate, and the lower half-space`; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LifecycleTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LifecycleTests.lifecycle, protection and pin states round-trip their database tags", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LifecycleTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LifecycleTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-DB-TAGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.referencedMaterialVersions keeps every referenced material version, a repeated cell once", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-DB-TAGS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Lifecycle.PinState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs", "obligations": ["S21-DB-TAGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Library.SampleStructure.referencedMaterialVersions", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "obligations": ["S21-DB-TAGS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.1 -- The library model in EF Core, created without migrations"}
{"number": 62, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.1d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [60], "how_to": "The one seam through which the app reaches the library database: open or create it, stamp it, and catch every EF Core call (001 §C 'No migrations', 'Settings': WAL mode, one writer; .spec-md §3.9, §4 'Errors and IO', 'Stored formats'; §7 '`Test` EF table + migration → library model'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs`, above `StorageError` (`Errors.fs:StorageError`): `LibrarySchemaVersion of int` with `.value` and `static member current : LibrarySchemaVersion`, which is 1. Its doc says it names `LibraryDbContext`'s model (step 60) and is raised, with the table listing of `the library model creates exactly its seven tables and their columns`, whenever that model changes. `LibrarySchemaMismatchInfo = { foundOpt : LibrarySchemaVersion option; expected : LibrarySchemaVersion }` is a record, because two same-typed positions in one case are ELEV011, as with `SchemaVersionMismatchInfo` (step 30). `StorageError` gains `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr of LibrarySchemaMismatchInfo` and `LibraryDatabaseExn of exn`; its doc list names both, and `describe` (step 33), like any other complete match on `StorageError`, gains their lines: the found version (or `no stamp`) beside the expected one, and the exception's message. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`, `module LibraryDatabaseStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `CatalogueFolderStore.fs` (step 33): one `<Compile>` line and no new comment. It opens `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite`, `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore`, `OpticalConstructor.Database` and `Softellect.Sys.Primitives` for `ConnectionString` (`Primitives.fs:713` in STL), the type `AppSettingsProvider.tryGetConnectionString` answers. `LibraryDatabase` is a sealed class implementing `IDisposable` that owns ONE open `SqliteConnection` for its lifetime, so a `:memory:` database lives exactly as long as its handle and the process has one writer. (a) `static member openOrCreate (connectionString : ConnectionString) : Result<LibraryDatabase, StorageError>` works in this order. It reads the string through `SqliteConnectionStringBuilder`, sets `Pooling` to false so that disposing the handle releases a database file, and opens the connection. It runs `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` on that connection itself, so the foreign keys are enforced whoever opens a context over it. For a file database (a `DataSource` other than `:memory:` and a `Mode` other than `Memory`) it runs `PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL` (001 §C: the file is local only). It calls `Database.EnsureCreated ()` on a context over the connection. When that created the schema, it writes the one `LibrarySchemaStampRow` (`Id` 1, `SchemaVersion` from `LibrarySchemaVersion.current`). Otherwise it reads the stamp. A database without the `SchemaStamp` table or its row (another application's file, or one whose creation was cut short) is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr { foundOpt = None; expected = LibrarySchemaVersion.current }`, and a stamp other than `current` is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr` carrying it. On a mismatch it disposes the connection and leaves the file as it was: no migration, no repair and no recreation, because the remedy is the caller's (001 §C; S2.4). (b) `member this.run<'Outcome> (work : LibraryDbContext -> 'Outcome) : Result<'Outcome, StorageError>` holds the handle's lock, builds a `LibraryDbContext` over the one connection (`UseSqlite(connection)`), runs `work`, disposes the context and answers the outcome. Every exception thrown inside, an EF Core one included, is caught here and answered as `LibraryDatabaseExn`; nothing above this seam handles an exception (.spec-md §4). (c) `Dispose` closes the connection, and a `run` after it answers `LibraryDatabaseExn`. `openOrCreate` and `run` carry `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the library database seam (001 §C): every EF Core and SQLite call is caught here and mapped to a typed error\")>]` on their declarations. No retry, cache, pool, second provider or configuration knob is added (.spec-md §8). (3) Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`. Every file database is `library.db` (001 §A) in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryDatabaseTests\")`, as `ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs:25` keeps its files, and never under `%TEMP%` or the user's folders (.spec-md §3.9). (a) `an in-memory library database is created, stamped and lives as long as its handle`: `openOrCreate (ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\")` is `Ok`; through `run`, `SchemaStamps` holds exactly one row, whose `SchemaVersion` is 1; and a `LibraryCatalogueImportRow` added and saved in one `run` is read back equal in a second `run`. (b) `a library database file runs in WAL mode and keeps its stamp and rows across opens`: a handle over a new file answers `wal` for `PRAGMA journal_mode`, and a `LibraryCatalogueImportRow` saved before that handle is disposed is read back by a second handle over the same file, whose stamp is still 1. (c) `a stamp other than the model's is LibrarySchemaMismatchErr and the file is left as it was`: after a file database is created, its stamp is set to 2 through `run` (`ExecuteSqlRaw`) and the handle is disposed; `openOrCreate` then answers `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr { foundOpt = Some (LibrarySchemaVersion 2); expected = LibrarySchemaVersion.current })` twice in a row, and the stamp, read through a plain `SqliteConnection` with pooling off, is still 2. A file holding only a test-local table written through such a plain connection answers `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr { foundOpt = None; expected = LibrarySchemaVersion.current }` and afterwards holds that table alone. Each error's `describe` names its found and expected versions. (d) `an EF Core failure inside run is LibraryDatabaseExn, never a throw`: saving a `LibraryEntryFacetRow` whose entry version no row holds answers `Error (LibraryDatabaseExn _)`, because the foreign key is enforced, and the next `run` on the same handle answers `Ok`.", "acceptance": "After the seam lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an in-memory library database is created, stamped and lives as long as its handle`, `a library database file runs in WAL mode and keeps its stamp and rows across opens`, `a stamp other than the model's is LibrarySchemaMismatchErr and the file is left as it was` and `an EF Core failure inside run is LibraryDatabaseExn, never a throw`; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.an in-memory library database is created, stamped and lives as long as its handle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-OPEN-STAMP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.a library database file runs in WAL mode and keeps its stamp and rows across opens", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-OPEN-STAMP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.a stamp other than the model's is LibrarySchemaMismatchErr and the file is left as it was", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-OPEN-STAMP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.an EF Core failure inside run is LibraryDatabaseExn, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-OPEN-STAMP"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryDatabaseStore.LibraryDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S21-OPEN-STAMP"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.1 -- The library model in EF Core, created without migrations"}
{"number": 63, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.1e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [61, 62], "how_to": "A library version and its database row map through the entry file, so the database payload IS the file (001 §C 'Hybrid shape': 'The library file, the database payload and a kit's snapshot of an entry are byte-identical, and the hash proves it'; .spec-md §5). In `LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (step 62): (1) `EntryVersionState = { lifecycle : EntryLifecycle; pin : PinState }` is what a version row holds beside its file, and `StoredEntryVersion = { envelope : LibraryEntryEnvelope; state : EntryVersionState }` is one stored version. Each doc is one line citing 001 §C. (2) `Errors.fs`: `StorageError` gains `LibraryRowInvalidErr of reason : string`, a row whose tags or columns its payload does not support, with its doc-list entry and a line (the reason) in `describe` and in any other complete match on `StorageError`. (3) Type extensions on `EntryProvenance` (step 24): `member this.kindValue : int` (`BuiltInProvenance` 1, `UserProvenance` 2, `KitImportProvenance` 3, `SourcePullProvenance` 4) is the provenance-kind column. It is written for queries and never read back, because the provenance itself lives in the payload. `member this.catalogueIdOpt : CatalogueId option` is `Some` for `BuiltInProvenance` alone. (4) `member this.versionRow : Result<LibraryEntryVersionRow, StorageError>` on `StoredEntryVersion` sets `EntryId`, `Version`, `Kind` and `Name` from the content's `id`, `version`, `schema.kind` and `name`; `Lifecycle` and `PinState` from the state; `Protection` from `provenance.protection`; `ProvenanceKind` and `CatalogueId` from (3); `PayloadText` from the envelope's `fileText` (step 30), the very text an entry file holds; and `ContentHash` from `contentHash`. A `fileText` failure passes through. (5) `type LibraryEntryVersionRow with member this.toStoredVersion : Result<StoredEntryVersion, StorageError>` works in this order. `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfWire` of `Kind`, `EntryLifecycle.tryOfDb` of `Lifecycle` and `PinState.tryOfDb` of `PinState` (step 61) come first, and an unknown tag is `LibraryRowInvalidErr` naming the entry, the version, the column and the tag. Then `LibraryFileText.parseEntry kind` (step 30) reads `PayloadText`, whose schema, version and hash checks answer their own `StorageError`s. Last, the row MUST equal, column for column, the `versionRow` of the parsed envelope under the read state; the first column that differs is `LibraryRowInvalidErr` naming it. Both mapping members carry step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark on their declarations, because they are the row's IO boundary. No cache, fallback reader or up-converter is added: a payload of another schema version is the parser's `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` (.spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). (6) Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`: (a) `every kind's entry round-trips through its database row byte for byte`: over `:memory:`, every envelope of `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()` is stored with the states `{ lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned }` and `{ lifecycle = InactiveEntry; pin = VersionPinned }` alternating in row order, each `versionRow` added and saved through `run`. Read back through a second `run`, every row's `toStoredVersion` is `Ok` and equals the version stored; every kind of `LibraryEntryKind.all` is present; and every row's `PayloadText`, in UTF-8, equals the bytes (`File.ReadAllBytes`) of its entry file, named by the content's `fileName`, in `Catalogue/Builtin` under `AppContext.BaseDirectory`. (b) `a row its payload does not support is refused`: taken from `MaterialIds.silicon`'s row, a changed `Name` and a `Kind` of 0 each answer `LibraryRowInvalidErr`, and a `PayloadText` whose entry name is changed inside the text answers `ContentHashMismatchErr`.", "acceptance": "After the mapping lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every kind's entry round-trips through its database row byte for byte` and `a row its payload does not support is refused`; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.every kind's entry round-trips through its database row byte for byte", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-ROW-MAPPING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.a row its payload does not support is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-ROW-MAPPING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryDatabaseStore.EntryVersionState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S21-ROW-MAPPING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryDatabaseStore.StoredEntryVersion", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S21-ROW-MAPPING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.1 -- The library model in EF Core, created without migrations"}
{"number": 64, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.1f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [63], "how_to": "The relational keys a library version is queried and constrained by, written beside its row (001 §C 'Hybrid shape': facet keys and sample-version → material-version keys). In `LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`, two members on `LibraryEntryEnvelope`, both keyed by the content's `id` and `version` and both carrying step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark: (1) `member this.facetRows : Result<LibraryEntryFacetRow list, StorageError>`. The rows are the distinct attribute-key and discrete-value pairs of the existing facet catalogue (`LibraryFacets.fs`): `FacetKey` is the `AttributeKey`'s text, `FacetValue` the `DiscreteKey`'s text, and only `DiscreteValue`s are stored. A material's rows come from every `LibraryFacets.materialFacets []` attribute that applies to its decoded `MaterialEntry` (`toMaterialEntry`, step 25). A sample's, source's, polarizer's or detector's come from every `LibraryFacets.libraryFacets [] []` attribute that applies to its decoded `LibraryEntry` (`SampleItem`, `SourceItem`, `PolarizerItem`, `DetectorItem`). A category has none. Both catalogues are read over empty lists (step 46's signatures), so a row depends on its own entry alone. The material-category row's value is therefore the category's GUID text, which is what `CategoryId.categoryName []` answers (step 46), so renaming a category never stales a row. The facets a sample reads through its materials extract nothing, because the sample-material rows below hold that relation, and the numeric film-thickness facet is not stored. A decoder refusal is `LibraryRowInvalidErr` carrying its `describe` (step 39). (2) `member this.sampleMaterialRows : Result<LibrarySampleMaterialRow list, StorageError>`: for a sample, one row per element of its structure's `referencedMaterialVersions` (step 61), with `SampleId` and `SampleVersion` from the content and `MaterialId` and `MaterialVersion` from the reference; every other kind has none. No other key, index or derived column is added. (3) Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`, over the envelopes of `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`: (a) `a material's facet rows hold its own discrete facets and key its category by id`: `MaterialIds.silicon`'s rows hold (`material-category`, the GUID text of `CategoryIds.semiconductor`), (`material-anisotropy`, `Isotropic`), (`material-dispersion`, `Dispersive`) and (`material-transparency`, `Absorbing`), and no `material-gyration-class`, `material-handedness` or `material-magnetic` row; `MaterialIds.langasite`'s hold (`material-anisotropy`, `Uniaxial`), (`material-gyration-class`, `Uniaxial 3 / 4 / 6 (g₁₁, g₃₃)`) and (`material-handedness`, `Right-handed`); and the `CategoryIds.glass` category entry has no row. (b) `an entry's facet rows are its kind and its own discrete facets`: `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` has exactly (`entry-kind`, `Sample`) and (`sample-has-thin-films`, `Has thin films`); `PresetIds.polarizerLp` exactly (`entry-kind`, `Polarizer`) and (`polarizer-category`, `Linear`); `PresetIds.source600` exactly (`entry-kind`, `Source`); and `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` exactly (`entry-kind`, `Detector`). (c) `a sample's material rows are every material version its structure references`: `SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId` has exactly the rows of `MaterialIds.langasite` and `MaterialIds.silicon` at version 1, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` exactly those of `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial` at version 1, and `MaterialIds.silicon`'s material entry has none. (d) `every built-in's facet and material rows are stored beside its version row`: over `:memory:`, every envelope's version row (step 63, state `{ lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned }`), facet rows and sample-material rows are added in one `run` and saved; a second `run` reads back exactly the facet rows and the sample-material rows written; and deleting `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s version row also removes its facet and material rows (step 60's cascade).", "acceptance": "After the keys land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a material's facet rows hold its own discrete facets and key its category by id`, `an entry's facet rows are its kind and its own discrete facets`, `a sample's material rows are every material version its structure references` and `every built-in's facet and material rows are stored beside its version row`; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.a material's facet rows hold its own discrete facets and key its category by id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-RELATIONAL-KEYS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.an entry's facet rows are its kind and its own discrete facets", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-RELATIONAL-KEYS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.a sample's material rows are every material version its structure references", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-RELATIONAL-KEYS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.every built-in's facet and material rows are stored beside its version row", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S21-RELATIONAL-KEYS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.1 -- The library model in EF Core, created without migrations"}
{"number": 65, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.2a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [64], "how_to": "Pinned replaces VersionsInUse (001 §C 'Versions are immutable', 'Pinned replaces VersionsInUse'; .spec-md §0.1 `Lifecycle.fs` row, §5 `PinState`, §6 'Version rule'). A pin is one-way and belongs to one version; it is set through a store verb, and nothing derives 'in use' from live experiments any more. This is one step because deleting the seam's type changes every caller at once. `PinState` (`VersionPinned` / `VersionUnpinned`, with `value` and `tryOfDb`) is step 61's and is reused, never declared again (ELEV014/016). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs`: `VersionsInUse` (`Lifecycle.fs:VersionsInUse`, with `empty`), `VersionUsage` (with `ofBool`) and `usageOf` are deleted. `decideVersioning`'s last parameter becomes `(pin : PinState)`, the stored latest version's pin, and its table reads: physics identical and metadata identical is `KeepCurrent`; physics identical and metadata changed is `MutateInPlace`, whatever the pin; physics changed is `MutateInPlace` when `VersionUnpinned` and `MintNextVersion` when `VersionPinned`. 001 §C binds 'edit latest' to this rule, so a pinned version's physics never changes in place, and a kit's snapshot hash is the second safeguard. Its doc table says pinned / unpinned. `VersionRef` stays, because an experiment still binds a sample by version (`Experiments.fs:ElementBinding`); its doc drops the in-use sentences. The module doc names the pin where it named the seam. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `MaterialProxy` gains `pinMaterialVersion : MaterialVersionId -> Result<unit, MaterialError>`, after `supersedeMaterial`. Its doc list gains the verb (a pin is one-way), `saveMaterial`'s entry says it decides with the latest version's pin, and `removeMaterial`'s says it refuses a material with any pinned version. `MaterialVersionInUseErr` becomes `MaterialVersionPinnedErr of reason : string`, and its doc says removal is refused while any version is pinned. The `VersionNumber` and `MaterialVersionId.firstOf` docs say pinned where they say used and drop their `VersionsInUse` and 'step 25' clauses. Directly after `MaterialVersionId`, `type MaterialError with static member unknownMaterialVersion (version : MaterialVersionId) : MaterialError` holds the one text for an unresolved material version, moved from `Propagation.fs:resolveMaterialVersion` (`unknown material version '<id>' v<n>`), which now calls it, so the pin verb below reuses it (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'); its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.2. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, the same for samples: `SampleProxy` gains `pinSampleVersion : SampleVersionId -> Result<unit, SampleError>`, after `supersedeSample`; `SampleVersionInUseErr` becomes `SampleVersionPinnedErr of reason : string`; and the `SampleError`, `SampleProxy`, `SampleVersionId.firstOf` and `samplesReferencing` docs, with the comment above `samplesReferencing` (`ElementId.fs:1044-1050`), say pinned and drop the seam. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs` and `SampleStore.fs`: each version record gains `pin : PinState`. A new id inserts version 1 `VersionUnpinned`, and a minted version starts `VersionUnpinned`; `MutateInPlace` and the three lifecycle verbs keep the version's pin. `saveMaterial` / `saveSample` pass the latest version's pin to `decideVersioning`, and `usageAt` is deleted. `pinMaterialVersion` / `pinSampleVersion` set `VersionPinned` on the named version and answer `Ok ()`, also when it is already pinned; an id the store does not hold, or a version its history does not hold, is `MaterialError.unknownMaterialVersion` / an `UnknownSampleIdErr` naming the id and the version as `v<n>`. No verb unpins. `removeMaterial` keeps its referenced-by-samples refusal first, then refuses a material with any pinned version as `MaterialVersionPinnedErr`, whose reason keeps today's shape (the name, the id, the count and the versions as `v1, v2`) with 'pinned' in place of 'bound by a live experiment'; `removeSample` refuses likewise with `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. `createInMemory` loses its `versionsInUse` parameter: `MaterialProxy.createInMemory (samplesReferencing : MaterialId -> Sample list)` and `SampleProxy.createInMemory ()`. The module and member docs say pinned. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `boundVersions` and `versionsInUseSeam` are deleted. `ElementBinding.versionRefOpt` and `Experiment.versionRefs` stay, because they say what an experiment binds; their docs name no seam, and the `Lifecycle` open's comment names `VersionRef` alone. `ExperimentCollectionStore.fs`'s module doc drops its clause about the app-scope `VersionsInUse` source. `CatalogueImport.fs` (step 37), `createInMemory`, builds `SampleProxy.createInMemory ()` and `MaterialProxy.createInMemory (samplesReferencing samples)`, and its material and sample reason matches name the renamed cases. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` the comments above the `Lifecycle.fs`, `Experiments.fs` and `SampleStore.fs` items lose the clauses naming `VersionsInUse`, `boundVersions` and `versionsInUseSeam`; nothing is added (AGENTS.md: no new comments in project files). (6) Ui. `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs` (`MaterialError.caption`, `SampleError.caption`) and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:runFailureCaption` name the renamed cases. The comments that describe a used version or the seam say pinned or drop the clause: `LibraryWindowView.fs:selectedVersionsOf`, `MaterialsWindowView.fs:selectedVersionsOf`, the `AddLayerClicked` and `SaveClicked` comments of `SampleEditorView.fs`, and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:descriptorBinding`. `AppContext.fs:AppContext.create` builds its stores through `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory` since step 44 and needs no change. (7) Every caller, with one rule. A call that passes a `VersionsInUse` value drops it, and so does the fixture: `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (samplesReferencing : MaterialId -> Sample list)` and `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()` (step 45); every caller of these and of the two `createInMemory`s follows. A fact that stubbed the seam with versions builds the plain store and pins those versions through the new verb. Every stub `MaterialProxy` record gains `pinMaterialVersion = fun _ -> Ok ()` and every stub `SampleProxy` record `pinSampleVersion = fun _ -> Ok ()`: in `MaterialProxyTests`, `SampleProxyTests`, `MaterialEditorWindowTests` (two), `MaterialsWindowTests`, `SampleEditorWindowTests` (three) and `LibraryWindowTests`. An `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Lifecycle` whose only use was the seam goes, with its comment; so does the `VersionsInUse` clause of the `LifecycleTests.fs` item comment in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, whose 'used/unused' becomes 'pinned/unpinned'. The callers at authoring time are the constructor suite's `CategoryProxyTests`, `MaterialProxyTests`, `SampleProxyTests`, `LifecycleTests`, `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`, `PropagationTests`, `SourceLibraryTests`, `BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests` and the fixture `BuiltinCatalogue.fs`, and the UI suite's `EmbeddedChartTests`, `FsxAcceptanceTests`, `InverseConstructorTests`, `LibraryWindowTests`, `LightSourceEditorTests`, `MainWorkbenchTests`, `MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `MaterialsWindowTests`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests`, `SampleEditorWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `WindowLauncherTests`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`. A caller the closing grep finds anywhere else is re-pointed by the same rule. (8) Facts. `LifecycleTests`: the helper `decide` takes a `PinState`, and the eight decision-table facts keep their expectations under their pinned names: `identical save keeps the current version — unused` becomes `identical save keeps the current version — unpinned`; `identical save keeps the current version — used` becomes `identical save keeps the current version — pinned`; `metadata-only edit never versions — unused mutates in place` becomes `metadata-only edit never versions — unpinned mutates in place`; `metadata-only edit never versions — used mutates in place, does NOT mint` becomes `metadata-only edit never versions — pinned mutates in place, does NOT mint`; `unused physics change mutates in place` becomes `unpinned physics change mutates in place`; `used physics change mints the next version` becomes `pinned physics change mints the next version`; `unused physics-and-metadata change mutates in place` becomes `unpinned physics-and-metadata change mutates in place`; `used physics-and-metadata change mints the next version (new metadata rides along)` becomes `pinned physics-and-metadata change mints the next version (new metadata rides along)`. `usageOf reports VersionUsed for a ref the seam contains and VersionUnused otherwise` and `a bound version unlocks the used-version rule through the seam` are deleted with their subject. The module doc and the section comment say pin. `MaterialProxyTests` and `SampleProxyTests`: `proxyWithUsed` becomes `proxyWithPinned`, a fresh store whose listed versions are pinned through the verb, and `v1Ref` goes. The facts that used it keep their expectations: `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a used version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged` becomes `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a USED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint` becomes `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a physics change of an UNUSED version updates version 1 in place` becomes `MutateInPlace — a physics change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a physics change of a USED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2` becomes `MintNextVersion — a physics change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `removeMaterial on a material with a used version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version` becomes `removeMaterial on a material with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor version-used` becomes `removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor pinned`; and in `SampleProxyTests`, `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a used version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged` becomes `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a USED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint` becomes `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNUSED version updates version 1 in place` becomes `MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a structure change of a USED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2` becomes `MintNextVersion — a structure change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `removeSample on a sample with a used version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version` becomes `removeSample on a sample with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeSample succeeds when no version is in use, then the id is unknown` becomes `removeSample succeeds when no version is pinned, then the id is unknown`. The STUB facts' refusals name `MaterialVersionPinnedErr` / `SampleVersionPinnedErr`, and `a sample layer keeps resolving its pinned material version after the material mints a newer one` pins `MaterialVersionId.firstOf MaterialIds.glass152` through `pinMaterialVersion` where it stubbed the seam. `MaterialProxyTests` gains `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`: pinning version 1 of `MaterialIds.glass152` twice answers `Ok ()` both times; a physics change (the `MaterialIds.glass200` complexity) then mints version 2; a second physics change, back to the original complexity, mutates version 2 in place, so no version 3 resolves and version 1 keeps the original physics; and pinning version 1 of a freshly minted id, and version 3 of `MaterialIds.glass152`, answer `UnknownMaterialIdErr` naming the id and the version. `SampleProxyTests` gains `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`, the same over `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and the `SampleIds.glassPlate2mmId` structure. `ExperimentProxyTests`: `boundVersions collects the versioned bindings of the setup (samples yes, presets no)` becomes `versionRefs collects the versioned bindings of the setup (samples yes, presets no)`; `a bound version appears in versionsInUse and BLOCKS removal of that sample` becomes `pinning an experiment's bound sample version BLOCKS removal of that sample`; `editing a USED sample version mints the next version instead of rewriting it` becomes `editing a PINNED sample version mints the next version instead of rewriting it`. The first asserts on `e1.versionRefs`; the other two pin each `SampleVersionRef` of `e1.versionRefs` through `pinSampleVersion` of `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()`, and the second still removes the sample freely from a store nothing pinned. `committing from a scene captures the ordered chain including the detector kind` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`' `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and DataFilePath attachments` read the experiment's `versionRefs` where they read `boundVersions`, with the same expected references.", "acceptance": "After the replacement, `git grep -n -E \"VersionsInUse|versionsInUse|VersionUsage|VersionUsed|VersionUnused|usageOf|boundVersions|versionsInUseSeam|VersionInUseErr\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged (the two deleted LifecycleTests facts out, the two pin facts in), including `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`, `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` and the renamed decision-table, removal and ExperimentProxyTests facts; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Propagation.fs", "Ber