resolvable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 97, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [96], "how_to": "The catalogue-import log (001 §B 'Import on every start': the hash 'recorded in the database'; 001 §C 'What it holds': 'the catalogue-import log'; .spec-md §3.8: a registered catalogue folder is an import-log row). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`. `CatalogueImportTime of DateTime` (UTC) and `CatalogueEntryCount of int` each carry `.value`. `CatalogueImportLogEntry = { catalogueId : CatalogueId; folder : FolderName; manifestHash : ContentHash; importedAt : CatalogueImportTime; entryCount : CatalogueEntryCount }` records which catalogue was absorbed, from which folder, under which manifest hash, when, and with how many entries. `FolderName` is `Softellect.Sys.Primitives.FolderName`, as `DataLocations` holds it (step 81). Each doc is one line. `CatalogueImportProxy` gains three fields. `loggedImports : unit -> Result<CatalogueImportLogEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers every row, ordered ordinally by folder. `logImport : CatalogueImportLogEntry -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` adds the catalogue's row, or replaces it. `forgetImport : CatalogueId -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` removes the row; an unlogged id changes nothing and answers `Ok ()`. The record's doc names the log. `createInMemory` keeps the log in a closure-local map keyed by catalogue id. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`. `type CatalogueImportLogEntry with member this.importRow : LibraryCatalogueImportRow` and `type LibraryCatalogueImportRow with member this.toLogEntry : CatalogueImportLogEntry` map step 60's columns `CatalogueId`, `Folder`, `ManifestHash`, `ImportedAtUtc` and `EntryCount`. Each carries step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark, as `versionRow` and `toStoredVersion` (step 63) do. `createInDatabase`'s three fields work over `CatalogueImports`: they list the rows, add or overwrite the tracked row, and remove it, each in one `run`. (3) Tests. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `recordingProxy` gains an empty log. `CatalogueImportContract` gains `the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id`: two entries are logged under folders `b` and `a` and listed `a` first. Logging the first again with another hash replaces its row. Forgetting it leaves the other, and forgetting it again answers `Ok ()`. Every listed entry equals the one logged, its time included.", "acceptance": "After the log lands, `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST declare `loggedImports`, `logImport` and `forgetImport` over both stores; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id` over both `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportLogEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 98, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [97], "how_to": "Import on every start, cheap by manifest hash (001 §B 'Import on every start': 'compare each catalogue's `.catalogue-json` hash with the one recorded in the database, and import only on change'; .spec-md §3.7, §3.8; the S3.1 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportContext` (step 94) gains three fields. `hashManifest : CatalogueManifest -> Result<ContentHash, CatalogueImportError>` hashes a manifest. `now : unit -> CatalogueImportTime` is the clock. `openCatalogue : FolderName -> CatalogueProxy` opens a catalogue folder. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`' `create` fills them with `CatalogueManifest.manifestHash` (step 31, a `StorageError` as `EntryHashingErr`), `CatalogueImportTime DateTime.UtcNow` and `CatalogueProxy.create` (step 33). Its signature is unchanged, and a fact replaces a field by record update. (2) The outcomes, each with a one-line doc. `PendingCatalogueImport = { entry : CatalogueImportLogEntry; decisions : ImportDecision list }` is a catalogue imported but not settled: the log row it will write, and the rows that wait. `FolderImportResult` = `CatalogueUnchanged of CatalogueImportLogEntry` | `CatalogueImported of CatalogueImportLogEntry` | `CatalogueAwaitsChoices of PendingCatalogueImport`. `FolderImportReport = { folder : FolderName; outcome : Result<FolderImportResult, CatalogueImportError> }`. `StartupImportReport = { folders : FolderImportReport list }` has `member this.pending : PendingCatalogueImport list`, its awaiting catalogues in order. (3) `member private this.importFolder (folder : FolderName) : Result<FolderImportResult, CatalogueImportError>` works in this order. It opens the folder through `openCatalogue`, reads its manifest (`readManifest`, step 92; `CatalogueUnreadableErr`), and hashes it. When `loggedImports` holds the manifest's catalogue under that hash, the answer is `CatalogueUnchanged` of the logged row: no entry file is read and nothing is written. Otherwise it reads the catalogue and runs `importCatalogue` (step 94). The row is `{ catalogueId = manifest.id; folder = folder; manifestHash = hash; importedAt = now (); entryCount = … }`, with one count per manifest row. With no awaiting row it is logged (`logImport`) and answered as `CatalogueImported`. With awaiting rows the answer is `CatalogueAwaitsChoices` and the log is left as it was, so the next start decides those rows again; the rows applied unasked are then reused. (4) `member this.importOnStart (shippedFolder : FolderName) : Result<StartupImportReport, CatalogueImportError>` imports the shipped folder first. It then reads `loggedImports`, whose failure is the answer. It then imports every logged folder whose `catalogueId` is not `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` (that row is the shipped catalogue's), in the log's order. A folder's failure is its own report's outcome, and the other folders still run. No retry, cache beyond the manifest-hash skip, or option is added (.spec-md §8). (5) Tests, new `[<Fact>]` members of `CatalogueImportContract`. Their folders are fresh, each with a GUID name under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"CatalogueImportTests\")`, written through `CatalogueProxy.create` (step 33), and never under `%TEMP%`. Each fact replaces `now` with a test-local clock that advances one second per call. (a) `the start-up import logs the shipped catalogue and skips it, reading no entry file, while its manifest hash is unchanged`. The first start over a folder holding the Built-in catalogue answers `CatalogueImported`; its row names the folder, the catalogue's `manifestHash` and one count per entry. After one entry file is deleted from the folder, the second start answers `CatalogueUnchanged` with that same row: it read no entry file, and the log is unchanged. (b) `a changed built-in catalogue mints the new version and moves the latest on the next start`. The folder is rewritten with Silicon's version 2 under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. The next start answers `CatalogueImported` under the new hash, and Silicon is held at versions 1 and 2 with latest 2. (c) `a catalogue whose rows await a choice imports the rest and is not logged, so the next start decides again`. A user material named `Lab glass` is put. The shipped folder holds the Built-in catalogue, a new-id material named `Lab glass` and a new source. The start answers `CatalogueAwaitsChoices` with the one `NameCollision` row, the source is held, and the log holds no row. A second start answers the same row again. (d) `every logged folder is re-checked on start, and a failing one is reported without stopping the others`. Two `Lab` folders, each with its own test-local catalogue id, are logged through `logImport` under a test-local hash that is not theirs, and the second folder is then deleted. The start's report holds the shipped folder first and then both `Lab` folders, found by folder: the first is `CatalogueImported` with its entries held, and the second is `CatalogueUnreadableErr`, whose row stays in the log. (e) `a user entry is never touched by the start-up import`. A `Lab` folder holding two user materials is logged under a hash that is not its own, so a first start imports it. The first material's entry file is then deleted and the folder is rewritten with the second's version 2. The next start retires nothing, and the second material is held at versions 1 and 2 with its latest still 1.", "acceptance": "After the start-up import lands, `CatalogueImportContext.importOnStart` MUST skip a catalogue whose logged manifest hash is unchanged and log a catalogue only when no row awaits a choice; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the start-up import logs the shipped catalogue and skips it, reading no entry file, while its manifest hash is unchanged`, `a changed built-in catalogue mints the new version and moves the latest on the next start`, `a catalogue whose rows await a choice imports the rest and is not logged, so the next start decides again`, `every logged folder is re-checked on start, and a failing one is reported without stopping the others`, `a user entry is never touched by the start-up import` over both stores, the count rising by 10; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the start-up import logs the shipped catalogue and skips it, reading no entry file, while its manifest hash is unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.the start-up import logs the shipped catalogue and skips it, reading no entry file, while its manifest hash is unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a changed built-in catalogue mints the new version and moves the latest on the next start", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a changed built-in catalogue mints the new version and moves the latest on the next start", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue whose rows await a choice imports the rest and is not logged, so the next start decides again", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue whose rows await a choice imports the rest and is not logged, so the next start decides again", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.every logged folder is re-checked on start, and a failing one is reported without stopping the others", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.every logged folder is re-checked on start, and a failing one is reported without stopping the others", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a user entry is never touched by the start-up import", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a user entry is never touched by the start-up import", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.StartupImportReport", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 99, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [98], "how_to": "Extra read-only catalogue folders, and settling a catalogue whose rows waited (001 §B 'Extra catalogue folders: read-only folders on a share or a git checkout', 'nothing is overwritten silently'; .spec-md §3.8; the S3.1 brief: registering imports the folder and logs it; unregistering removes the log row and keeps its entries). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportError` gains `CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr of reason : string`, with its `describe` line. (2) `member this.registerFolder (folder : FolderName) : Result<FolderImportResult, CatalogueImportError>` on `CatalogueImportContext` reads the folder's manifest through `openCatalogue` and `readManifest`. A manifest whose catalogue is `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, or already in `loggedImports`, is `CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr` naming the folder, the catalogue and the folder it is logged under. Otherwise the answer is `importFolder folder` (step 98). The folder is only read, so its permissions stay its own. (3) `member this.settle (pending : PendingCatalogueImport) (choices : ImportChoice list) : Result<ImportOutcome, CatalogueImportError>` completes an awaiting import once its rows are chosen; the import dialog (S3.2) calls it. Every pending row MUST have exactly one choice, matched by `entryId`, and no choice may name a row the pending import does not hold; otherwise the answer is `InvalidImportChoiceErr`. It then runs `apply`, and on success logs `{ pending.entry with importedAt = now () }`, so the next start skips the catalogue. (4) `member this.registeredFolders () : Result<CatalogueImportLogEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` on `CatalogueImportProxy` is `loggedImports` without the `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` row. Unregistering a folder is `forgetImport` (step 97): its row goes, and every entry it brought stays, because user data never vanishes silently. Each doc is one to three lines. (5) Tests, new members of `CatalogueImportContract` over folders made as in step 98. (a) `registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder`: after the shipped start, registering a `Lab` folder answers `CatalogueImported`, its entries are held, and `registeredFolders` lists exactly its row. (b) `registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused`: a folder holding the Built-in catalogue, and the `Lab` folder a second time, each answer `CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr`, and nothing changes. (c) `unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it`: after `forgetImport`, the `Lab` entries are still held, and the next start's report has no `Lab` row. (d) `settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused`, over step 98 (c)'s setup. Settling with no choice answers `InvalidImportChoiceErr` and logs nothing. Settling with the collision's `byDefault` holds both `Lab glass` materials and logs the catalogue, and the next start answers `CatalogueUnchanged`. `every import error renders its condition and its payload` (`CatalogueImportProxyTests`) covers the new case.", "acceptance": "After registration lands, `CatalogueImportContext` MUST declare `registerFolder` and `settle` and `CatalogueImportProxy` `registeredFolders`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder`, `registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused`, `unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it`, `settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused` over both stores and `every import error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every import error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 100, "anchor": "WIRE", "ac": "AC-S3.1j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [99], "how_to": "The app imports its catalogues on every start (001 §B 'Import on every start'; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`: it imports the catalogues on start; §3.7, §3.8; the S3.1 brief: the rows that need a choice are held in the AppContext for S3.2's dialog). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the record gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` is the library's import seam over the database, through which the Library window registers folders. `pendingImports : PendingCatalogueImport list` holds the start-up imports whose rows wait for a choice. `compose` (step 89) builds `catalogueImports = CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase database)` (steps 95, 98). It runs `catalogueImports.importOnStart (CatalogueProxy.builtInFolderUnder locations.shippedCatalogueFolder)` (step 92) on every start, created or opened, so step 88's `CreatedLibraryDatabase` branch and its import are deleted. An `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe` and leaves `pendingImports` empty. For an `Ok report`, every folder report whose outcome is an `Error e` is logged naming the folder and `e.describe`, and `pendingImports` is `report.pending`. The app starts with what was imported, as step 88 does, and nothing throws. `create`'s and `recreateLibrary`'s docs say, in no more words, that every start imports the shipped catalogue and the registered folders by manifest hash. `LibraryDatabase.origin` (step 84) keeps its members, because the facts in `LibraryDatabaseTests` and the backup suites still read it. (2) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE': the parenthesis naming `CatalogueImportProxy.importFrom` (step 58) names `CatalogueImportContext.importOnStart`, which imports `Catalogue/Builtin/` and every registered catalogue folder on every start. (3) Tests, in `AppContextTests`. Each uses `TestAppScope.fileLocations` (step 88) of the module, with `shippedCatalogueFolder` set to a fresh folder under the test output. That folder's `Builtin` subfolder is written through `CatalogueProxy.create` (step 33) from `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`. `create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one`: the first create lists Silicon with its description. The `Builtin` folder is rewritten with Silicon's version 2, whose description differs and whose name, and so file name, is unchanged. The second create's `materials.tryGetMaterial MaterialIds.silicon` answers the new description, and `resolveVersion` of version 1 answers the old one. A third create over the unchanged folder leaves the Built-in row of `catalogueImports.proxy.loggedImports ()` exactly as the second create logged it. `create holds the shipped rows that need a choice as pending imports and imports the rest`. After the first create, a user material named `Lab glass` is saved through its `materials`. The `Builtin` folder is rewritten with a new-id material named `Lab glass` and a new source added, both under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. The second create's `pendingImports` holds one catalogue whose one row is that material's `NameCollision`, the material is not held, and `library.tryGetEntry` resolves the source. The step-88 facts `create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again` and `create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores` keep their assertions, because an unchanged manifest is skipped.", "acceptance": "After the wiring, `AppContext.create` MUST run `importOnStart` over the shipped catalogue on every start and hold its awaiting rows in `pendingImports`, and `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT read `LibraryDatabase.origin`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one` and `create holds the shipped rows that need a choice as pending imports and imports the rest`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-APP-IMPORTS-ON-START"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create holds the shipped rows that need a choice as pending imports and imports the rest", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-APP-IMPORTS-ON-START"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 101, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.1k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [100], "how_to": "'Register catalogue folder…' in the Library window (001 §B 'Extra catalogue folders'; .spec-md §3.8; §10: discoverability ('Register catalogue folder…' is in the Library window) and action buttons; the S3.1 brief). Unregister has no undo and needs none: it keeps every entry, and registering the folder again restores the row. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowContext` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:153`) gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `libraryBackups` (step 90), with a one-line doc. (b) `LibraryWindowError` gains `CatalogueImportRefusedErr of CatalogueImportError`, and its `caption` renders it through `CatalogueImportError.caption`. (c) `LibraryWindowModel` (`:229`) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `importStatus : ControlCaption option` opens as `None`. `pendingImports : PendingCatalogueImport list` opens as `[]`; it holds the registrations whose rows wait for the import dialog. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains `RegisterCatalogueFolder of FolderName` and `UnregisterCatalogueFolder of CatalogueId`, each documented. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `RegisterCatalogueFolder folder` calls `context.catalogueImports.registerFolder folder` (step 99), and each outcome clears `lastError`. `Ok (CatalogueImported entry)` sets `importStatus` to `Registered catalogue folder <folder> (<n> entries).`. `Ok (CatalogueAwaitsChoices pending)` appends `pending` to `pendingImports` and sets `importStatus` to `Imported <folder>; <k> entries wait for a decision, so the folder is not registered yet.`. `Ok (CatalogueUnchanged entry)` sets it to `Catalogue folder <folder> is unchanged.`. `Error e` sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr e` and clears `importStatus`. `UnregisterCatalogueFolder id` calls `context.catalogueImports.proxy.forgetImport id`. `Ok ()` sets `importStatus` to `Unregistered <folder>. Its entries stay in the library.`, naming the folder its `registeredFolders` row had, and `Error e` sets `lastError`. Neither message arms or disarms a gate. (f) The view. `verbButton` (`:1020`) becomes `verbButtonOn (id : ConstructorUiId) (label : ControlCaption) (onPressed : PointerPressedEventArgs -> unit)`, and `verbButton id label onClick` is `verbButtonOn id label (fun _ -> onClick ())`, so the look keeps one body. A private `pickCatalogueFolder (owner : Window) (onPicked : FolderName -> unit) : unit` opens `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync` with `FolderPickerOpenOptions(Title = \"Register catalogue folder\", AllowMultiple = false)`. On a confirmed pick it passes the first folder's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FolderName`, posted on the UI thread. It is wrapped so that a host without a provider changes nothing, in the shape of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`. In the verbs row (`verbsRow`, `:1104`), after the entry verbs and in Browse and Select mode alike, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton (ControlCaption \"Register catalogue folder…\")` resolves the owner window from the press, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton` does, and dispatches `RegisterCatalogueFolder` on a confirmed pick. When `context.catalogueImports.proxy.registeredFolders ()` answers at least one row, a block carrying `libraryCatalogueFoldersPanel`, titled `Catalogue folders`, follows the verbs. It holds one row per folder carrying `libraryCatalogueFolderRow entry.catalogueId.uiKey`: the folder, `imported <yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm> UTC`, `<n> entries`, and `verbButton (ConstructorUiId.libraryUnregisterCatalogueButton entry.catalogueId.uiKey) (ControlCaption \"Unregister\")`. `importStatus`, when `Some`, shows in a `TextBlock` carrying `libraryImportStatusText`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type CatalogueId with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (its GUID's text, as `CategoryId.uiKey` is) and `type CatalogueImportError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`), each with a one-line doc. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group (`UiIds.fs:498-523`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.1: `libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton` (`\"LibraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton\"`), `libraryCatalogueFoldersPanel` (`\"LibraryCatalogueFoldersPanel\"`), `libraryCatalogueFolderRow (catalogue : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"LibraryCatalogueFolderRow_{catalogue.value}\"`), `libraryUnregisterCatalogueButton (catalogue : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"LibraryUnregisterCatalogueButton_{catalogue.value}\"`) and `libraryImportStatusText` (`\"LibraryImportStatusText\"`). (4) Threading, along step 90's `libraryBackups` path, so that every Library window has the app scope's import seam. `LibraryWindow` (`LibraryWindow.fs:34`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `libraryBackups` and sets the context field. `EditorLaunchers.openLibraryWindow` and `openLibrarySelectWindow` take it after the `LibraryBackupProxy`, and `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext`. `initWith` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:475`) sets it to `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `DefaultStores.DefaultStoreSet` (`:430`) gains `catalogueImports`, the context its stores were imported through (step 94), and `initTableAndElementRotation` and `initMain` set it by record update beside `sources`. The strip's `OpenLibraryWindow` and the Select open pass `model.catalogueImports`. `Program.fs`' `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` thread `catalogueImports = context.catalogueImports` beside `libraryBackups`, and the launcher's Library button passes it. Every test construction passes one. `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` and its two `LibraryWindow(...)`, `LightSourceEditorTests`' `libraryContext`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' `libraryContext` and `ScrollExtentTests`' `LibraryWindow(...)` pass `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` passes `ctx.catalogueImports`. `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording launchers and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' Select-open stub take the extra argument. A doc that lists the window's or the launchers' stores names the import seam in no more words. (5) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`. The pure facts run over `stubContext` with an in-memory import context and a catalogue folder written through `CatalogueProxy.create` into a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryWindowTests\")`, holding one user source. `the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the five ids' texts. `RegisterCatalogueFolder imports and registers the folder and names it in the status`: afterwards the context's `registeredFolders` lists the folder, `tryHeldEntry` holds the source, and `importStatus` names the folder. `a folder whose rows await a choice is imported but held for the import dialog, not registered`: a source with the folder's source name is put first under another id; `pendingImports` holds the one collision, `registeredFolders` is empty, and `importStatus` counts one entry waiting. `a refused registration shows its reason as the window message`: registering the same folder twice sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr (CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr _)`. `UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries`: `registeredFolders` is empty, the source is still held, and `importStatus` names the folder. `acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries` (trait `ui-smoke`) runs over `AppContext.create` of `TestAppScope.fileLocations`. The folder is registered through `ctx.catalogueImports.registerFolder`, and a `LibraryWindow` is composed from the context's stores, `libraryBackups` and `catalogueImports`. The window shows `libraryCatalogueFolderRow` for the folder. A press on its Unregister verb, made as the file's other acceptance facts press a verb, removes the row, `libraryImportStatusText` names the folder, and `ctx.sources.tryGetSource` still resolves the folder's source.", "acceptance": "After the Library window is wired, every Library window, opened from the launcher, the strip or a Select session, MUST carry the app scope's `CatalogueImportContext` and offer `libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `RegisterCatalogueFolder imports and registers the folder and names it in the status`, `a folder whose rows await a choice is imported but held for the import dialog, not registered`, `a refused registration shows its reason as the window message`, `UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.RegisterCatalogueFolder imports and registers the folder and names it in the status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a folder whose rows await a choice is imported but held for the import dialog, not registered", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a refused registration shows its reason as the window message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindowView.LibraryWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.EditorLaunchers", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 102, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [101], "how_to": "A dropped entry file is an import origin of its own, and one entry is decided on its own (001 §H 'A library entry: its `-json` file, dropped onto the Library or Materials window (§B decision table)'; 001 §B 'one table for catalogues, kit snapshots and single dropped files'; the S3.2 brief). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `ImportOrigin` (step 93) gains `DroppedFileOrigin of file : FileName`, documented as an entry file dropped onto the Library or Materials window, held by its leaf name (`FileName.leafName`). (2) `member this.describe : string` on `ImportOrigin` is its honest render (ELEV002): the catalogue's name for `CatalogueImportOrigin` and the file's text for `DroppedFileOrigin`. `ImportDecision.rowName` (step 93) reads it, so a name collision from a dropped file is `<name> — from <file>`, and one from a catalogue stays `<name> — from <catalogue name>`. (3) `ImportDecision.decide` keeps its rules. Its latest-move condition names `CatalogueImportOrigin (c, _)`, so an entry from a dropped file never moves the latest: a version not held is `AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion`. Its doc says so in one line. (4) On `CatalogueImportProxy`, `member this.decideEntry (origin : ImportOrigin) (incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope) : Result<ImportDecision, CatalogueImportError>` holds the per-envelope body of `decideCatalogue` (step 94 (5)): `tryHeldEntry`, then `heldEntriesNamed` for the envelope's kind and name when nothing is held, then `ImportDecision.decide`. `decideCatalogue` calls it for every envelope in row order and keeps its unlisted rows, so one body decides catalogue rows, dropped files (step 104) and S4.2's kit snapshots. No store is read or written beyond that body, and no other member changes. (5) Tests: `ImportDecisionTests` gains `a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision`. Under `DroppedFileOrigin (FileName \"Silicon.material-json\")`, Silicon's built-in version 2 against its held version 1 is `VersionNotHeld` defaulting to `AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion`. A user material named `Silicon` under `DroppedFileOrigin (FileName \"lab-silicon.material-json\")` against the held Silicon is `NameCollision` whose `rowName` is `Silicon — from lab-silicon.material-json`. `describe` answers `Built-in` for the class's catalogue origin and `lab-silicon.material-json` for that file's. The facts over `decideCatalogue` keep their assertions.", "acceptance": "After the origin lands, `ImportOrigin` MUST hold `DroppedFileOrigin`, and `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST declare `decideEntry`, which `decideCatalogue` calls for every envelope; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROP-ORIGIN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.ImportDecision", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S32-DROP-ORIGIN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-DROP-ORIGIN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 103, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [102], "how_to": "One library entry file is read on its own (001 §H: a single entry file is dropped in; 001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout'; the S3.2 brief: dropped files are parsed by S1.4's reader). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: on `LibraryEntryKind` (step 24), `static member tryOfFileName (file : FileName) : LibraryEntryKind option` answers the kind whose `extension` equals the file's extension (`FileName.tryGetExtension`), compared with `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` (the Windows rule of step 26), and `None` otherwise, a `.catalogue-json` included. Its doc is one line citing 001 §A. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs` (steps 33, 92): `type LibraryFileText with static member readEntryFile (kind : LibraryEntryKind) (file : FileName) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` reads the file's text as UTF-8 (a missing or unreadable file is `FileIoExn`; every .NET IO exception is caught here) and answers `LibraryFileText.parseEntry kind` of it (step 30), so the file's schema, version and hash are checked. It is the per-row read of `CatalogueProxy.create`'s `readCatalogue` (step 33), moved: `readCatalogue` calls `readEntryFile row.kind` for each manifest row and maps its error to `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` naming the file, as before, and the folder's entry files are the top-level files for which `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName` answers a kind. One body reads an entry file, and one rule names its kind. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.2. (3) Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` gains `a file's extension names its entry kind, ignoring case`: `Silicon.material-json` is `MaterialEntryKind`, `C:/lab/Glass.CATEGORY-JSON` is `CategoryEntryKind`, a stem followed by each of the six kinds' `extension` answers that kind, and `.catalogue-json`, `notes.txt` and `Silicon` answer `None`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `readEntryFile reads one entry file through its schema, version and hash checks`, over a folder written as the class's other facts write one: each entry file read with its row's kind answers the catalogue's envelope; a file name that does not exist answers `FileIoExn`; the sample's file read as `MaterialEntryKind` answers `SchemaValidationErr`; and the source's file with a number changed inside its payload, its hash kept, answers `ContentHashMismatchErr`. The class's facts over `readCatalogue` keep their assertions.", "acceptance": "After the read is shared, `LibraryFileText.readEntryFile` MUST be the one read of an entry file, which `readCatalogue` calls, and `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName` the one rule naming a file's kind; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a file's extension names its entry kind, ignoring case` and `readEntryFile reads one entry file through its schema, version and hash checks`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a file's extension names its entry kind, ignoring case", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-FILE-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.readEntryFile reads one entry file through its schema, version and hash checks", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-FILE-READ"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CatalogueFolderStore.LibraryFileText.readEntryFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-FILE-READ"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 104, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [103], "how_to": "Dropped entry files are decided against the library, and nothing is written (001 §H; 001 §B 'nothing is overwritten silently'; .spec-md §3.7: a dropped file always opens the dialog; the S3.2 brief: dropping one or more entry files of any kind parses them and opens the dialog). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `CatalogueImportError` gains `DroppedFileRefusedErr of reason : string` (a dropped file is not a library entry file, does not read, or contradicts another dropped file) and `UnresolvedReferenceErr of reason : string` (a dropped entry names an entry neither held nor dropped), each with a `describe` line in step 39's form. (2) `CatalogueImportContext` (steps 94, 98) gains `readEntryFile : LibraryEntryKind -> FileName -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, CatalogueImportError>`, documented as reading one entry file. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`' `create` fills it with `LibraryFileText.readEntryFile` (step 103), a `StorageError` becoming `DroppedFileRefusedErr` that names the file with the error's `describe`. `create`'s signature is unchanged, and a fact replaces the field by record update. (3) `member this.decideDroppedFiles (files : FileName list) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` on `CatalogueImportContext` works in this order. (a) A file's kind is `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName` (step 103). A file without one is refused as `<file>: not a library entry file`, and every other file is read through `readEntryFile`, a refusal keeping its reason. When any file is refused, the answer is one `DroppedFileRefusedErr` whose reason lists every refused file with its reason, one line each in drop order, so every bad file is named at once. (b) Two files holding one id and version are one entry when their hashes agree, the first file kept, and `DroppedFileRefusedErr` naming both files when they differ. (c) Every id in an entry's `content.referencedEntryIds` (step 93) MUST be the id of a dropped entry or be held (`proxy.tryHeldEntry` answers `Some`). Otherwise the answer is `UnresolvedReferenceErr` naming the entry, its file and the missing id, so an applied drop never leaves a reference dangling. (d) Each remaining entry, in drop order, is `proxy.decideEntry (DroppedFileOrigin file.leafName) envelope` (step 102). An empty list answers `Ok []`, and the first read error of the proxy is the answer. Nothing is written: the import dialog applies the rows (steps 107, 108). No retry, cache or option is added. (4) Tests: new `[<Fact>]` members of `CatalogueImportContract`, so each runs over the in-memory seam and SQLite `:memory:`. Each fact first runs `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` through `freshImport ()`'s context, whose `readEntryFile` is the real reader. Its files are written into a fresh folder, a GUID name under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"CatalogueImportTests\")`, through each envelope's `fileText` (step 30) and `writeAtomically` (step 33), named by `content.fileName`, from envelopes sealed with `LibraryEntryContent.sealed`. `dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name`: a new user material's file and Silicon's built-in file, dropped in that order, answer an `EntryIdNotHeld` row whose origin is `DroppedFileOrigin` of the first file's leaf name and a `SameContentHash` row, and `tryHeldEntry` of the new material still answers `None`. `a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file`: `notes.txt`, a `missing.material-json` that does not exist and the user material's file answer one `DroppedFileRefusedErr` whose reason names `notes.txt` and `missing.material-json` and not the material's file. `two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ`: the material's file and a copy of it under another name answer one row; the material's file and the file of a changed content at the same id and version answer `DroppedFileRefusedErr` naming both files. `a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr`: a test-local user sample whose structure names a new user material, dropped alone, answers `UnresolvedReferenceErr` naming the material's id; dropped after the material's file, the two answer two `EntryIdNotHeld` rows in drop order. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `every import error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After dropped files are decided, `CatalogueImportContext` MUST declare `readEntryFile` and `decideDroppedFiles`, which writes nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name`, `a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file`, `two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ`, `a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr` over both stores and `every import error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every import error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 105, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [104], "how_to": "The import seam answers a held version's envelope, so the import dialog can show what an incoming entry would change (001 §B: 'with an explicit \"use my Si instead\" re-binding and a diff preview'; the S3.2 brief: the override picker carries a diff preview of the two payloads). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportProxy` gains `tryHeldEnvelope : LibraryEntryId -> VersionNumber -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope option, CatalogueImportError>`, documented as the envelope of one held version, whatever its lifecycle, and `None` when that version is not held. The in-memory double answers it from its map (step 94 (4)), and `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `recordingProxy` (step 94) answers `None`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `createInDatabase` (step 95) answers it in one `database.run` through `tryStoredVersion id version` (step 67), `Some stored` answering `stored.envelope` and every `StorageError` `ImportStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`, as its other fields do. No other field, cache or query is added. (3) Tests: `CatalogueImportContract` gains `tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held`. After `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` and a put of Silicon's version 2 (a changed description, sealed) with `KeepLatestVersion`, `tryHeldEnvelope MaterialIds.silicon.toLibraryEntryId` answers the catalogue's envelope at version 1 and the put's at version 2, and `None` at version 3; a test-local GUID answers `None`.", "acceptance": "After the read lands, both implementations of `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST answer `tryHeldEnvelope`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held` over both stores, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-HELD-ENVELOPE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-HELD-ENVELOPE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-HELD-ENVELOPE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 106, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [105], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests"], "how_to": "The line diff of two entry files, which the import dialog's preview shows (001 §B 'a diff preview'; the S3.2 brief). An entry file is canonical text (step 27: sorted keys, two-space indents), so a line diff of two files compares their payloads field by field. No diff package is added. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/EntryTextDiff.fs`, `module EntryTextDiff` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `CatalogueFiles.fs` (step 32), with one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `EntryTextLine of string`, with `.value`, is one line of an entry file. `EntryDiffLine` = `SameEntryLine of EntryTextLine` | `RemovedEntryLine of EntryTextLine` | `AddedEntryLine of EntryTextLine` is one line of a comparison: the held side's lines are removed and the incoming side's added. `static member diffLines (held : EntryTextLine list) (incoming : EntryTextLine list) : EntryDiffLine list` on `EntryDiffLine` keeps the common leading and trailing lines as `SameEntryLine`. It compares the lines between them by their longest common subsequence, a dynamic-programming table over that middle alone, so a small edit to a long tabulated file stays cheap. Between two kept lines, the held side's other lines come first as `RemovedEntryLine` and then the incoming side's as `AddedEntryLine`, each in its own order. So the `SameEntryLine` and `RemovedEntryLine` lines, in order, are the held text, and the `SameEntryLine` and `AddedEntryLine` lines are the incoming text. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.2. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs` (step 30): `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.diffFrom (held : LibraryEntryEnvelope) : Result<EntryDiffLine list, StorageError>` renders both envelopes' `fileText` and splits each at `\\n`, dropping the empty segment after the final line end. It answers `EntryDiffLine.diffLines` of the held lines and this envelope's lines, and a `fileText` failure passes through. Its doc is one line. (3) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs` (`module EntryTextDiffTests`), appended to the compile list after `ImportDecisionTests.fs` (step 93) with no comment. `equal texts diff as unchanged lines only`: two equal three-line lists answer three `SameEntryLine`s in order, and two empty lists answer `[]`. `a changed line is removed and then added between the unchanged lines`: `a b c d` against `a x c d` answers `SameEntryLine a`, `RemovedEntryLine b`, `AddedEntryLine x`, `SameEntryLine c`, `SameEntryLine d`; and `a b c` against `a c` answers `SameEntryLine a`, `RemovedEntryLine b`, `SameEntryLine c`. `lines added or removed at either end leave the rest unchanged`: `x a b` against `a b` answers `RemovedEntryLine x` and then two `SameEntryLine`s; `a b` against `a b y` answers two `SameEntryLine`s and then `AddedEntryLine y`; and `a b` against `c d` answers `RemovedEntryLine a`, `RemovedEntryLine b`, `AddedEntryLine c`, `AddedEntryLine d`. In every case of the three facts, the held and the incoming texts are recovered from the answer as (1) says. `EntryFileJsonTests` gains `two versions of an entry diff by the lines of their files`: Silicon's built-in envelope and a sealed copy whose description differs answer exactly two `RemovedEntryLine`s, the held file's `contentHash` and `descriptionOpt` lines, and two `AddedEntryLine`s, the copy's; every other line of the file is a `SameEntryLine`.", "acceptance": "After the diff lands, `EntryDiffLine.diffLines` MUST answer the lines of its rule and `LibraryEntryEnvelope.diffFrom` MUST diff two entry files; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal texts diff as unchanged lines only`, `a changed line is removed and then added between the unchanged lines`, `lines added or removed at either end leave the rest unchanged`, `two versions of an entry diff by the lines of their files`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/EntryTextDiff.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests.equal texts diff as unchanged lines only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests.a changed line is removed and then added between the unchanged lines", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests.lines added or removed at either end leave the rest unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.two versions of an entry diff by the lines of their files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.EntryTextDiff.EntryDiffLine", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/EntryTextDiff.fs", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.EntryFileJson.LibraryEntryEnvelope.diffFrom", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 107, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [106], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests"], "how_to": "The import dialog's pure MVU (001 §B 'The decisions show as one dialog with a row per entry, and nothing is overwritten silently'; 001 §O 'Import dialog: one row per entry, its status, the default action and an override'; .spec-md §3.7, §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 the Apply / Cancel pair; the S3.2 brief). It reaches the import seam only on Apply. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `brush`, `messageColor`, `positiveBackground`, `negativeBackground`, `verbButton` and `actionButton` (the view section, `MaterialsWindowView.fs:877-924`) lose `private`. Their docs say, in no more words, that the import dialog uses the same look: one declaration serves both, the spec 0048 R2 rule `LibraryWindowView.fs` follows for `LifecycleAction`. No body changes, and no other view's copy is touched. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView`, compiled directly after `MaterialsWindowView.fs` and before `MaterialsWindow.fs` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment. The module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §B and spec 0050 S3.2, and every type, case and field has a one-line doc. (a) `ImportDialogRequest` = `SettlePendingCatalogue of PendingCatalogueImport` (a catalogue whose rows wait, step 98) | `ApplyDroppedEntries of decisions : ImportDecision list` (dropped entry files, step 104): what the dialog decides. S4.2 adds a kit snapshot's case. `member this.decisions : ImportDecision list` is the pending import's `decisions` or the dropped ones. `member this.heading : ControlCaption` is `Import from <folder>: <k> entries need a decision.` (`entry.folder` of the pending import) or `Import <n> dropped entry files.`. (b) `ImportDialogApplied = { request : ImportDialogRequest; choices : ImportChoice list; outcome : ImportOutcome }` is what an Apply did. `member this.summary : ControlCaption` is `Imported <folder> (decisions applied: <n>).` or `Imported the dropped entry files (decisions applied: <n>).`, `n` counting the choices. Every opener shows it as its status, so the text is written once. (c) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ImportDialogContext = { imports : CatalogueImportContext; request : ImportDialogRequest; onApplied : ImportDialogApplied -> unit; requestClose : unit -> unit }`, in the shape of `MaterialsWindowContext` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:154`): the composition root bakes the seam, the opener's callback and the window's close, and tests substitute recording stubs. (d) `ImportDiffState` = `NoImportDiffShown` | `ImportDiffShown of LibraryEntryId`: at most one row shows its diff. (e) `ImportDialogModel = { context : ImportDialogContext; choices : ImportChoice list; diff : ImportDiffState; lastError : CatalogueImportError option }`. `initImportDialog (context : ImportDialogContext) : ImportDialogModel` opens with the `byDefault` (step 93) of every decision of `context.request.decisions`, in order, no diff shown and no error. Rows are told apart by their decision's `entryId`, the key `settle` matches choices by (step 99). (f) `ImportDialogMsg`, each case documented: `DecideImportRow of LibraryEntryId` (the row takes its default action), `OverrideImportRow of LibraryEntryId * ImportAction` (the row takes one of its `alternatives`), `ToggleImportDiff of LibraryEntryId`, `ApplyImportChoices` and `CancelImportDialog`. (g) `updateImportDialog (msg : ImportDialogMsg) (m : ImportDialogModel) : ImportDialogModel`. `DecideImportRow id` sets the row's action to its `defaultAction`. `OverrideImportRow (id, action)` sets it when `action` is one of the row's `alternatives` and is inert otherwise, including for a row the dialog does not hold. Both clear `lastError`. `ToggleImportDiff id` shows that row's diff, or hides it when it is the one shown. `ApplyImportChoices` is the only message that reaches the seam: for `SettlePendingCatalogue p` it calls `context.imports.settle p m.choices` (step 99), and for `ApplyDroppedEntries _` it calls `context.imports.apply m.choices` (step 94). `Ok outcome` calls `context.onApplied { request = context.request; choices = m.choices; outcome = outcome }`, then `context.requestClose ()`, and clears `lastError`. `Error e` sets `lastError` to `Some e`, and the dialog stays open with its choices. `CancelImportDialog` calls `context.requestClose ()` and nothing else. (h) `importDialogView (m : ImportDialogModel) (dispatch : ImportDialogMsg -> unit) : IView` is a `DockPanel`. Docked at the bottom is one horizontal row of `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importApplyButton (ControlCaption \"Apply\") positiveBackground` and `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importCancelButton (ControlCaption \"Cancel\") negativeBackground`: one row, the boxes' margin as the gap, distinct colours, the look of the Select / Close pair. Above it, when `lastError` is `Some e`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importDialogMessage` shows `e.caption` (step 101) in `messageColor`. Docked at the top, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importDialogHeading` shows `request.heading` and the line `Nothing is imported until you press Apply.`. A `ScrollViewer` fills the rest; its vertical `StackPanel` carries `importDecisionList` and holds one block per choice. A row's block carries `importDecisionRow entryId.uiKey` and holds, in order: a line with the decision's `rowName`, its `kind.caption`, `version <v>` (the incoming content's version, or the held latest for `EntryUnlisted`) and `status.caption`; the line `Default: <decision.actionCaption decision.defaultAction>`; a `WrapPanel` holding one box per offered action, the default first and then the `alternatives` in order, each carrying `importActionOption entryId.uiKey action.uiKey` with `decision.actionCaption action` as its label. The chosen one is an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others are `verbButton`s. Pressing the default dispatches `DecideImportRow`, and an alternative `OverrideImportRow`. The `WrapPanel` sits in the vertical block, so it wraps at the window's width (AGENTS.md: never in a horizontal `StackPanel`). When the row has a diff base, a `verbButton` carrying `importDiffToggle entryId.uiKey`, labelled `Show diff` or `Hide diff` while shown, dispatches `ToggleImportDiff`. While shown, a block carrying `importDiffPreview entryId.uiKey` lists the lines of `incoming.diffFrom held` (step 106), one `TextBlock` each, prefixed `  `, `- ` or `+ `, with removed lines in `messageColor` and added lines in `Color.FromRgb(0uy, 110uy, 0uy)`. The held envelope is read through `context.imports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope` (step 105) as the view renders, as the library windows' views re-query their stores. An error shows one line with its `describe`, and `None` the line `The held version is not in the library.`. The diff base is: for `DivergentContent (incoming, held)`, the held version equal to the incoming version when `held.versions` holds it, else `held.latest`; for `VersionNotHeld (incoming, held)`, `held.latest`; for `NameCollision (incoming, sameName)`, the entry the row's `RebindToHeldEntry` names when that is its action, else the first of `sameName`, at its latest. `EntryIdNotHeld`, `SameContentHash` and `EntryUnlisted` rows have none. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type LibraryEntryId with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`, its GUID's text, as `CategoryId.uiKey`; `type LibraryEntryKind with member this.caption : ControlCaption`: `Material`, `Sample`, `Source`, `Polarizer`, `Detector`, `Category`; `type ImportStatus with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, in step 93's order: `New entry`, `Already in the library`, `New version of a held entry`, `Differs from the held version`, `Same name as a held entry`, `No longer in its catalogue`; `type ImportAction with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`: `add`, `reuse`, `version-latest`, `version-kept`, `fork`, `rebind-<guid>`, `skip`, `retire`; `type ImportDecision with member this.actionCaption (action : ImportAction) : ControlCaption`: `Add` (`Side by side` on a `NameCollision`), `Reuse the held entry`, `Add version, made latest`, `Add version, latest kept`, `Fork as a new entry`, `Use my <name> instead` (001 §B; the name of the same-name entry it names, or `Use the held entry instead` on any other status), `Skip` and `Mark inactive`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a group after the Materials window's, under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.2: `importDialogWindow` (`\"ImportDialogWindow\"`), `importDialogHeading` (`\"ImportDialogHeading\"`), `importDecisionList` (`\"ImportDecisionList\"`), `importDecisionRow (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportDecisionRow_{entry.value}\"`), `importActionOption (entry : ConstructorUiKey) (action : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportActionOption_{entry.value}_{action.value}\"`), `importDiffToggle (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportDiffToggle_{entry.value}\"`), `importDiffPreview (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportDiffPreview_{entry.value}\"`), `importDialogMessage` (`\"ImportDialogMessage\"`), `importApplyButton` (`\"ImportApplyButton\"`) and `importCancelButton` (`\"ImportCancelButton\"`). (5) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs` (`module ImportDialogTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`), appended to the compile list after `LibraryWindowTests.fs` with no comment. Its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and its dialog context records `onApplied` and `requestClose`. Its rows come from `decideDroppedFiles` (step 104) over files written as step 104's facts write them, in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"ImportDialogTests\")`: a new user material, a user material named `Silicon` (a `NameCollision`) and Silicon's built-in version 2 with a changed description (a `VersionNotHeld`). `the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the ten ids' texts. `the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied`: three rows in drop order, each choice its `byDefault`, no diff shown, and `tryHeldEntry` of the new material answers `None`. `an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert`: `OverrideImportRow` of the collision with its `RebindToHeldEntry` takes it; of the new material with `ForkIncomingEntry`, which it does not offer, it is inert; and `DecideImportRow` restores the collision's default. `Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes`: with the collision overridden by `SkipIncomingEntry`, `ApplyImportChoices` leaves the new material held, Silicon held at versions 1 and 2 with latest 1, and no second `Silicon`; it records one `onApplied` whose `choices` are the model's and whose `summary` is `Imported the dropped entry files (decisions applied: 3).`, and one close. `Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue`: a test-local `PendingCatalogueImport`, whose entry names a test-local catalogue id and folder and whose one decision is the collision `decideEntry` gives under `CatalogueImportOrigin (that id, CatalogueName \"Lab\")`, applied through `ApplyImportChoices`, holds both `Silicon` materials, and `proxy.loggedImports ()` holds a row for that catalogue id. `a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open`: the rows of a dropped new material and a dropped sample that names it, with the material overridden by `SkipIncomingEntry`, answer `lastError = Some (DanglingReferenceErr _)` on Apply, with no `onApplied`, no close and nothing held. `Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing`: `CancelImportDialog` records one close, no `onApplied`, and nothing is held. `each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers`: `importDialogView` mounted headless, as `LibraryWindowTests` mounts a view, shows in the collision's row `Silicon — from <its file>`, `Material`, `version 1`, `Same name as a held entry` and `Default: Side by side`, and the options `Side by side`, `Use my Silicon instead` and `Skip` by their `importActionOption` ids; the new material's row has no `importDiffToggle`. `a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload`: pressing the version row's `importDiffToggle` shows `importDiffPreview` holding a `- ` line with the held description and a `+ ` line with the incoming one; pressing it again hides it.", "acceptance": "After the dialog's MVU lands, `ImportDialogView` MUST reach the import seam only on `ApplyImportChoices`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied`, `an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert`, `Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes`, `Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue`, `a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open`, `Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing`, `each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers`, `a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload`, the count rising by 9; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.ImportDialogRequest", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.ImportDialogContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.updateImportDialog", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 108, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [107], "how_to": "The import dialog's window, and the one drop seam of the library windows (the S3.2 brief: a new window with its own view and window files; 001 §H; .spec-md §4 'UI': every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `ImportDialogView.fs`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment. (a) `type ImportDialogWindow(imports : CatalogueImportContext, request : ImportDialogRequest, onApplied : ImportDialogApplied -> unit)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `MaterialsWindow` (`MaterialsWindow.fs:29`) does. Its title is `Import decisions`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.importDialogWindow`; it asks for 900 × 640 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`). It runs `Program.mkProgram` over `initImportDialog`, `updateImportDialog` and `importDialogView` (step 107) with the context `{ imports = imports; request = request; onApplied = onApplied; requestClose = this.Close }`. Closing it any other way than Apply applies nothing, because only `ApplyImportChoices` reaches the seam. Its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §B and spec 0050 S3.2. (b) `module EntryFileDrop` holds `acceptEntryFiles (window : Window) (onDropped : FileName list -> unit) : unit`, the one drop seam of the Library and Materials windows (001 §H). It calls `DragDrop.SetAllowDrop(window, true)` and adds two handlers through `DragDrop.AddDragOverHandler` and `DragDrop.AddDropHandler`. The drag-over handler sets `e.DragEffects` to `DragDropEffects.Copy` when `e.DataTransfer.Contains DataFormat.File`, and to `DragDropEffects.None` otherwise. The drop handler takes `e.DataTransfer.TryGetFiles ()` and calls `onDropped` with each item's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FileName`, in order, when there is at least one. It is an IO edge in the shape of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`: each handler body is wrapped so that a platform failure changes nothing, and headless facts send the windows' drop message directly (steps 110, 111). Its doc is one to three lines. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the import dialog leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"ImportDialog\"` over an `ImportDialogWindow` whose request is `ApplyDroppedEntries` of one `EntryIdNotHeld` row per envelope of `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`, each `ImportDecision.decide (DroppedFileOrigin <its file name>) envelope None []`, and one `NameCollision` row against two same-name held entries, so the list is longer than the screen and one row's options are wide. Its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`, and `onApplied` is `ignore`. (3) `ImportDialogTests` gains `acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it` (trait `ui-smoke`). Over the class's in-memory context and two dropped rows (step 107), an `ImportDialogWindow` with a recording `onApplied` is shown headless. It shows `importDialogHeading`, `importDecisionList` holding both rows, and `importApplyButton` and `importCancelButton` with equal tops, Cancel to the right of Apply with a gap between them. Pressing Apply's centre, as the file's other facts press a box, holds both entries, records one `onApplied`, and closes the window.", "acceptance": "After the window lands, `ImportDialogWindow` MUST call `WindowFit.keepOnScreen`, and `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles` MUST be the one drop seam; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import dialog leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the import dialog leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 109, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [108], "how_to": "Every Materials window carries the app's import seam, the one a Sample editor opens in Select state included, so a file dropped on it is decided against the app library (001 §H: dropped onto the Library or Materials window; the S3.2 brief). This step threads the seam and changes no behaviour; step 110 reads it. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `MaterialsWindowContext` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:154`) gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories`, documented as the import seam that dropped entry files are decided and applied through. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`: `MaterialsWindow` (`MaterialsWindow.fs:29`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories` and sets the context field. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SampleEditorWindow.fs`: `SampleEditorWindow` (`SampleEditorWindow.fs:30`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories` and passes it to the Select-state `MaterialsWindow` that its `openMaterialsSelect` builds (`SampleEditorWindow.fs:69`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs`: the Sample editor it opens (`LibraryWindow.fs:77`) gets the window's `catalogueImports` (step 101). (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `EditorLaunchers.openMaterialsWindow` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:150`) takes the `CatalogueImportContext` after the `CategoryProxy`; `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it to `MaterialsWindow` (`:193`); and the strip's `OpenMaterialsWindow` (`:1832`) passes `model.catalogueImports` (step 101). The field's doc names the import seam in no more words. (6) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: the launcher's Materials button passes `context.catalogueImports`. (7) Every test construction passes one. `MaterialsWindowTests`' `stubContext` (`MaterialsWindowTests.fs:180`) and its `MaterialsWindow(...)` mounts (`:702`, `:1044`), `SampleEditorWindowTests`' `SampleEditorWindow(...)` mounts, `EmbeddedChartTests`' `MaterialsWindow(...)` (`EmbeddedChartTests.fs:230`), `ScrollExtentTests`' `MaterialsWindow(...)` and `SampleEditorWindow(...)`, `WindowLauncherTests`' windows (`WindowLauncherTests.fs:453`, `:488`, `:545`) and `WireUi0040CompositionTests`' Sample editors (`WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:306`, `:352`) pass `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:47`, `:57`, `:149`) passes `ctx.catalogueImports`, and `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording `openMaterialsWindow` (`MainWorkbenchTests.fs:106`) takes the extra argument. `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' launchers, a record update of `EditorLaunchers.defaults` (`WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs:136`), keep their code. A doc that lists the window's stores names the import seam in no more words. No assertion changes: the facts whose constructions change keep what they assert, among them `Library and Materials windows: the facet rows wrap, nothing is clipped`, `Material, Sample, Category and Source editors leave everything reachable`, `the Materials and Library strip buttons reach their launchers as pure launches`, `the initial projection lists every stored material as a selectable entry leaf with the live count`.", "acceptance": "After the threading, every `MaterialsWindow` and `SampleEditorWindow` construction MUST pass a `CatalogueImportContext`, and no assertion MUST change; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SampleEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SampleEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/EmbeddedChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WindowLauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.Library and Materials windows: the facet rows wrap, nothing is clipped", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.Material, Sample, Category and Source editors leave everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests.the Materials and Library strip buttons reach their launchers as pure launches", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the initial projection lists every stored material as a selectable entry leaf with the live count", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.MaterialsWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SampleEditorWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.EditorLaunchers", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 110, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.2i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [109], "how_to": "Dropping entry files onto the Materials window opens the import dialog over them (001 §H; .spec-md §3.7: a dropped file always opens the dialog; §10.1 discoverability: the dialog opens on a dropped entry file; §10.4: the dialog's completion message updates the window's model, whose projections re-query the store, so no reload is needed; the S3.2 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) `MaterialsWindowContext` gains `openImportDialog : ImportDecision list -> unit`, documented as opening the import dialog over the rows of dropped entries (the composition root bakes the window; tests record). (b) `MaterialsWindowModel` gains `importStatus : ControlCaption option` and `importError : CatalogueImportError option`, each opening `None`, each with a one-line doc. (c) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `DropMaterialEntryFiles of FileName list` and `MaterialsImportApplied of summary : ControlCaption`. (d) `updateMaterialsWindow`. `DropMaterialEntryFiles files` calls `context.catalogueImports.decideDroppedFiles files` (step 104). `Ok []` leaves the model as it was. `Ok decisions` calls `context.openImportDialog decisions` and clears `importStatus` and `importError`. `Error e` sets `importError` to `Some e` and clears `importStatus`; no dialog opens. `MaterialsImportApplied summary` sets `importStatus` to `Some summary` and clears `importError`; the next render re-queries the store, so an added material is listed. Neither arms or disarms a gate or changes the mode. (e) The view: after `messageRow` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:messageRow`), when either is set, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialsImportStatusText` shows `importError`'s `caption` (step 101) in `messageColor`, or else `importStatus`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`. The context's `openImportDialog` is `fun decisions -> ImportDialogWindow(catalogueImports, ApplyDroppedEntries decisions, fun applied -> dispatch (MaterialsImportApplied applied.summary)).Show()` (step 108). `member _.DropEntryFiles (files : FileName list) : unit` dispatches `DropMaterialEntryFiles files`: the semantic seam that the drop and the tests share, as `Retarget` is the launcher's. After `Program.run`, `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles this (fun files -> dispatch (DropMaterialEntryFiles files))` (step 108). The class doc names the drop in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group: `materialsImportStatusText` (`\"MaterialsImportStatusText\"`) under a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S3.2. (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`. `stubContext` (step 109) passes a recording `openImportDialog`. Files are written as step 104's facts write them, into a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"MaterialsWindowTests\")`. `dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`: `DropMaterialEntryFiles` of a new user material's file records one `openImportDialog` holding one `EntryIdNotHeld` row, `importError` stays `None`, and the context's import seam does not hold the material. `a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog`: `DropMaterialEntryFiles [ notes.txt ]` sets `importError` to `Some (DroppedFileRefusedErr _)` and records no dialog. `an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status`: `MaterialsImportApplied` of a summary sets `importStatus` to it and clears `importError`. `the Materials window accepts dropped files`: a `MaterialsWindow` mounted as the class mounts one answers `DragDrop.GetAllowDrop` true. `acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations …)`, a `MaterialsWindow(ctx.materials, ctx.categories, ctx.catalogueImports)` is shown headless. After `window.DropEntryFiles` of a new user material's file, exactly one `ImportDialogWindow` opens, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent` as `LauncherTests.clickAndObserve` observes. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, `ctx.materials.tryGetMaterial` resolves the material, and `materialsImportStatusText` shows the summary.", "acceptance": "After the drop is wired, a file dropped on the Materials window MUST be decided through `decideDroppedFiles` and open `ImportDialogWindow`, applying nothing before Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`, `a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog`, `an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status`, `the Materials window accepts dropped files`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the Materials window accepts dropped files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.MaterialsWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 111, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.2j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [110], "how_to": "Dropping entry files onto the Library window opens the import dialog over them, and so does a registered folder whose rows wait (001 §H; 001 §B 'Extra catalogue folders'; .spec-md §3.7, §3.8, §10.1, §10.4; S3.1 step 101 holds such a registration in `pendingImports` for this dialog). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowContext` gains `openImportDialog : ImportDialogRequest -> unit`, documented as `MaterialsWindowContext`'s is. (b) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `DropLibraryEntryFiles of FileName list`, `ReviewPendingImports` and `LibraryImportApplied of ImportDialogApplied`. (c) `updateLibraryWindow`. `DropLibraryEntryFiles files` calls `context.catalogueImports.decideDroppedFiles files`: `Ok []` is inert; `Ok decisions` calls `context.openImportDialog (ApplyDroppedEntries decisions)` and clears `lastError` and `importStatus`; `Error e` sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr e` (step 101) and clears `importStatus`. The `RegisterCatalogueFolder` arm for `Ok (CatalogueAwaitsChoices pending)` (step 101) also calls `context.openImportDialog (SettlePendingCatalogue pending)`. `ReviewPendingImports` opens the dialog over the first of `pendingImports`, and is inert when there is none. `LibraryImportApplied applied` sets `importStatus` to `applied.summary` and clears `lastError`. For `SettlePendingCatalogue p` it also removes from `pendingImports` the import whose `entry.catalogueId` is `p.entry.catalogueId`, because `settle` logged it and `registeredFolders` now lists it. None of these arms or disarms a gate. (d) The view: while `pendingImports` is not empty, the verbs row (`LibraryWindowView.fs:verbsRow`), in Browse and Select mode alike and after step 101's `Register catalogue folder…`, holds `verbButton ConstructorUiId.libraryReviewImportsButton (ControlCaption \"Review imports…\")`, which dispatches `ReviewPendingImports`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs`. The context's `openImportDialog` is `fun request -> ImportDialogWindow(catalogueImports, request, fun applied -> dispatch (LibraryImportApplied applied)).Show()`. `member _.DropEntryFiles (files : FileName list) : unit` dispatches `DropLibraryEntryFiles files`, and after `Program.run`, `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles this (fun files -> dispatch (DropLibraryEntryFiles files))`. The class doc names the drop in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group: `libraryReviewImportsButton` (`\"LibraryReviewImportsButton\"`) under a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S3.2. (4) Every other construction of `LibraryWindowContext` passes `openImportDialog`: `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` a recording stub, and `LightSourceEditorTests`' and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' `libraryContext` `ignore`. (5) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`, over `stubContext` with step 101's in-memory import context; files and catalogue folders are written as step 101's facts write them. `dropping entry files on the Library window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`: `DropLibraryEntryFiles` of a new user source's file records one `ApplyDroppedEntries` request holding one `EntryIdNotHeld` row; `lastError` stays `None`, and the source is not held. `a refused drop on the Library window shows its reason as the window message`: `DropLibraryEntryFiles [ notes.txt ]` sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr (DroppedFileRefusedErr _)` and records no request. `a registration whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog, and Review imports reopens it`: over step 101's awaiting-folder setup, `RegisterCatalogueFolder` records one `SettlePendingCatalogue` request over the model's pending import, and `ReviewPendingImports` records it again. `a settled registration leaves the pending list and its summary is the status`: after that, the pending import settled through `context.catalogueImports.settle` with its `byDefault` choices, `LibraryImportApplied` of the result empties `pendingImports`, sets `importStatus` to its `summary`, and `registeredFolders` lists the folder. `the Library window accepts dropped files`: a `LibraryWindow` mounted as the class mounts one answers `DragDrop.GetAllowDrop` true. `acceptance: a source file dropped on the Library window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations …)`, a `LibraryWindow` composed from the context's stores, `libraryBackups` and `catalogueImports` is shown headless. After `window.DropEntryFiles` of a new user source's file, exactly one `ImportDialogWindow` opens, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent`. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, `ctx.sources.tryGetSource` resolves the source, and `libraryImportStatusText` (step 101) shows the summary.", "acceptance": "After the drop is wired, a file dropped on the Library window and a registration whose rows await MUST open `ImportDialogWindow`, applying nothing before Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a source file dropped on the Library window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `dropping entry files on the Library window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`, `a refused drop on the Library window shows its reason as the window message`, `a registration whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog, and Review imports reopens it`, `a settled registration leaves the pending list and its summary is the status`, `the Library window accepts dropped files`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.dropping entry files on the Library window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a refused drop on the Library window shows its reason as the window message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a registration whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog, and Review imports reopens it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a settled registration leaves the pending list and its summary is the status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the Library window accepts dropped files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.acceptance: a source file dropped on the Library window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindowView.LibraryWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 112, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.2k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [111], "how_to": "The start-up imports whose rows wait open the import dialog from the Launcher (001 §B; .spec-md §3.7: rows that need a choice wait in the one import dialog, their default pre-selected, and nothing in them applies unconfirmed; §10.1: the dialog opens at start when a catalogue row needs a choice; S3.1 step 100 holds them in `AppContext.pendingImports`). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow` (steps 88, 89): (1) For `Ok context`, the window keeps the imports still waiting in one local mutable list, started from `context.pendingImports`; the window is the IO edge (AGENTS.md: mutation only at the IO boundary). While the list is not empty, the content shows, between the title and the surface buttons, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherPendingImportsText` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, with the text `Library entries waiting for an import decision: <n>.` (`n` summing the `decisions` of the list), and a `Button` carrying `launcherReviewImportsButton` the same way, labelled `Review imports…`. Its click opens `ImportDialogWindow(context.catalogueImports, SettlePendingCatalogue head, onApplied)` (step 108) over the head of the list. `onApplied` removes from the list the import whose `entry.catalogueId` is the applied request's, and rebuilds the content through step 89's local content function, so the notice counts what still waits and goes when nothing does. Cancel leaves the list as it was. (2) The first time the launcher opens (`Opened`), when the list is not empty, it opens the dialog over its head, so the choice is asked at start; the launcher never applies a row itself. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `launcherPendingImportsText` (`\"LauncherPendingImportsText\"`) and `launcherReviewImportsButton` (`\"LauncherReviewImportsButton\"`), each with a one-line doc. (4) Tests, in `LauncherTests`. `a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice`: in `withLauncher` (a new library imports the Built-in catalogue, so nothing waits) neither id is present, and the buttons are still the four surfaces. `acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `TestAppScope.fileLocations`, a first `AppContext.create` saves a user material `Lab glass` through its `materials`; the `Builtin` folder under the locations' `shippedCatalogueFolder` is rewritten with a new-id material named `Lab glass` (step 100's `create holds the shipped rows that need a choice as pending imports and imports the rest` setup); and a second `AppContext.create` holds one pending import. `LauncherWindow(locations, WorkbenchSettings.defaults, Ok ctx)` shown headless opens exactly one `ImportDialogWindow`, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent`, and `launcherPendingImportsText` reads `Library entries waiting for an import decision: 1.`. Pressing the dialog's `importCancelButton` closes it and keeps the notice. Clicking `launcherReviewImportsButton` opens a dialog again. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, removes the notice and the button, and leaves both `Lab glass` materials held. A third `AppContext.create` over the same locations holds no pending import. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher, whose context holds no pending import, keeps its code.", "acceptance": "After the launcher is wired, a start-up import whose rows await MUST open `ImportDialogWindow` from the launcher and stay waiting until Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LAUNCHER-PENDING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-LAUNCHER-PENDING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S32-LAUNCHER-PENDING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 113, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [112], "how_to": "Licence attribution is a fact of an entry's provenance, decided once in Domain (001 §B 'Licence attribution: CC-BY entries show their attribution in the Library and Materials windows and in the Details view'; the S3.3 brief: an entry whose provenance licence requires attribution shows its citation, and CC0 shows the licence name only). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, after `EntryProvenance` and `EntryForkInfo` (steps 24, 91), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3: (1) `EntryAttribution` = `LicenceAndCitation of licence : EntryLicence * citation : EntryCitation` | `LicenceNameOnly of licence : EntryLicence` is what an entry shows about its licence. Its `member this.text : string` is the honest render (ELEV002): `Licence <licence> — cite: <citation>` and `Licence <licence>`. (2) `type EntryLicence with member this.attributionWith (citation : EntryCitation) : EntryAttribution` holds the one CC-BY rule. A licence whose SPDX identifier starts with `CC-BY` (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`: `CC-BY-4.0`, `CC-BY-SA-4.0`, `CC-BY-NC-4.0` …) obliges its user to credit the source, so it answers `LicenceAndCitation`. Every other licence, `CC0-1.0` included, answers `LicenceNameOnly`. No other licence family, table or option is added. (3) `type EntryProvenance with member this.attributionOpt : EntryAttribution option`. `SourcePullProvenance info` answers `Some (info.licence.attributionWith info.citation)`. `ForkProvenance fork` answers `fork.originalProvenance.attributionOpt`, so a fork of a pulled entry, and a fork of that fork, keep its credit (S3.1 interpretation 2). `BuiltInProvenance`, `UserProvenance` and `KitImportProvenance` answer `None`, because they carry no licence. (4) `EntryAttributionLine = { entryName : EntryName; attribution : EntryAttribution }` is one credited entry as a surface lists it, with `member this.text : string` = `<entry name>: <attribution text>`. (5) `type LibraryEntry with member this.attributedEntryIds : LibraryEntryId list` names the entries a surface showing the entry credits: the entry's own id (`entry.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24; none for a non-GUID id), then, for a `SampleItem`, every material its structure references (`ElementId.fs:188` `SampleStructure.referencedMaterials`) through `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId`, in that set's order. A sample's own provenance carries no licence, but the optical constants of its layers may. (6) The fixture `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains, each with a one-line doc, the builders both suites use for licensed and user entries, so no fact copies them. `licensedMaterialContent (id : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) (licence : EntryLicence) (citation : EntryCitation) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's Silicon (`MaterialIds.silicon`, decoded from `catalogueData ()`) under `id` and `name`, built with `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry VersionNumber.first` under `SourcePullProvenance { source = MaterialSourceName \"Test optical constants\"; record = MaterialSourceRecordId \"test/<name>\"; sourceVersion = MaterialSourceVersion \"2026-11-01\"; licence = licence; citation = citation }`. `userMaterialContent (id : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the same Silicon under `UserProvenance`. `userCategoryContent (id : CategoryId) (name : CategoryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's Glass category (`CategoryIds.glass`) under `id`, `name` and `UserCategory`, built with `ofMaterialCategory VersionNumber.first UserProvenance`. `sampleContentOver (id : SampleId) (material : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` sample under `id`, `name` and `UserProvenance`, its films replaced by one 100 nm `SingleLayer` of version 1 of `material`. `putSealedEntries (context : CatalogueImportContext) (contents : LibraryEntryContent list) : unit` seals each content through `context.sealEntry` and puts it through `context.proxy.putEntryVersion` with `MoveLatestVersion`, in order. A builder or seam error fails the calling fact with its `describe`. (7) Tests, in `LibraryEntryFilesTests`. `a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone`: `CC-BY-4.0`, `cc-by-sa-4.0` and `CC-BY-NC-4.0` answer `LicenceAndCitation`, `CC0-1.0` and `MIT` answer `LicenceNameOnly`, and the two texts are exactly `Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: <citation>` and `Licence CC0-1.0`. `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none`: a `SourcePullProvenance` under `CC-BY-4.0`, a fork of it and a fork of that fork answer the same `LicenceAndCitation`; a `SourcePullProvenance` under `CC0-1.0` answers `LicenceNameOnly`; `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, `UserProvenance` and a `KitImportProvenance` of a test-local `KitId` answer `None`; and an `EntryAttributionLine` named `PTB glass` renders `PTB glass: <its attribution's text>`. `an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials`: a source preset of the catalogue answers its own id alone, and the `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` sample answers its own id followed by `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial` in the order of its `referencedMaterials`.", "acceptance": "After the attribution lands, `EntryProvenance.attributionOpt` MUST answer a pulled entry's licence attribution, through any fork, and `None` for every other provenance; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone`, `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none`, `an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryAttribution", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryAttributionLine", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 114, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [113], "how_to": "The library answers the credit a list of entries owes, so the three surfaces that show it read one body (001 §B 'Licence attribution'; the S3.3 brief: the Library window, the Materials window and the Details view of a bound element). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, on `CatalogueImportProxy`: `member this.attributionLinesOf (ids : LibraryEntryId list) : Result<EntryAttributionLine list, CatalogueImportError>`. For each distinct id, in the order given, it calls `tryHeldEntry` (step 94). An id the library does not hold adds nothing. A held entry adds `{ entryName = held.name; attribution = a }` when `held.provenance.attributionOpt` (step 113) is `Some a`: the latest version's provenance is the entry's credit. The first read error is the answer. It writes nothing. Its doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. No cache, per-version lookup or other member is added. Tests: `CatalogueImportContract` gains `attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked`, so it runs over the in-memory seam and SQLite `:memory:`. After `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` through `freshImport ()`'s context, `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries` (step 113) puts `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` under `CC-BY-4.0` and the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`, `licensedMaterialContent` `RII glass` under `CC0-1.0`, a fork of `PTB glass` named `PTB glass (fork)` (its content under a test-local id and `ForkProvenance` of `PTB glass`'s id, version and provenance), and `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass`. `attributionLinesOf` of `Lab glass`, `MaterialIds.silicon`, `PTB glass`, `RII glass`, the fork, a test-local GUID and `PTB glass` again answers exactly three lines, in this order: `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`, `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0` and the fork's line, which carries `PTB glass`'s licence and citation.", "acceptance": "After the read lands, `CatalogueImportProxy.attributionLinesOf` MUST answer one line per held, licensed entry in the order asked; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked` over both stores, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION-READ"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 115, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [114], "how_to": "The import seam lists the user's entries and pins a version of any kind, which every export needs (001 §B 'Export: … Exporting pins the exported versions (§C)'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned — a one-way flag — when a kit first references it, or when it is exported'; the S3.3 brief: exporting pins every exported version through S2.2's pin verbs). S2.2's verbs (`pinMaterialVersion`, `pinSampleVersion`, step 65) cover two kinds, and the source, preset and category stores have none (S2.3 interpretation 4). So the kind-neutral pin lives on the envelope seam (step 94), and its database half shares one body with those verbs. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportProxy` gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `heldUserEntries : unit -> Result<HeldEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers every held entry whose latest provenance is not a built-in (`provenance.protection` is `UserManaged`: user, kit-import, pulled and forked entries), whatever its lifecycle, each as `tryHeldEntry` answers it. `pinEntryVersion : LibraryEntryId -> VersionNumber -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` pins one held version, one way. It answers `Ok ()` also when the version is already pinned, and `ImportRejectedErr` naming the id and the version when that version is not held. The record's doc names both in no more words. (2) The in-memory double (`createInMemory`, step 95). `heldUserEntries` answers the map's entries whose latest provenance is `UserManaged`, in the map's id order. `pinEntryVersion` answers `ImportRejectedErr` for a version the map does not hold. For a held material or sample version it decodes the envelope (step 25), as its put does, and calls the bundled store's `pinMaterialVersion` or `pinSampleVersion` (step 65); a refusal is `ImportRejectedErr` with the store's reason. For every other kind it answers `Ok ()`, because the in-memory category, source and preset stores hold no pin. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`: the operations' extension (step 67) gains `stagePin (id : LibraryEntryId) (version : VersionNumber) : Result<StoredEntryVersion option, StorageError>` under the same `StorageBoundary` mark. It calls `tryStoredVersion id version`; a held version is restaged through `stageVersion` with `pin = VersionPinned` and its lifecycle kept, and is answered as it was found; a version not held answers `None`. It stages and never saves. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs`' `pinMaterialVersion` (step 69) and `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs`' `pinSampleVersion` (step 74) call it in place of their own restage and keep their refusals, so one body pins a version row. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`' `createInDatabase` (step 95). `heldUserEntries` answers, in one `database.run` and as `heldEntriesOf` does, every entry whose latest row (`LatestVersion` joined to `EntryVersion`) has `Protection` = `UserManaged.value`, in no promised order. `pinEntryVersion id version` is one `run` of `stagePin` and one `SaveChanges ()`; `None` is `ImportRejectedErr` naming the id and the version. Every `StorageError` is `ImportStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`, as for its other fields. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs`: `recordingProxy` (step 94) answers `heldUserEntries` with `[]` and `pinEntryVersion` with `Ok ()`. No cache, retry, unpin verb or other field is added: a pin is one-way (001 §C). (6) Tests. `CatalogueImportContract` gains two facts, so each runs over both stores; their entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `putSealedEntries` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. `heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in`: before any put it answers `[]`. After `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass`, `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` and a fork of `PTB glass` (as step 114's fact builds it) are put, and `Lab glass` is retired through `retireEntry`, it answers exactly those three ids, compared as a set, each with its own name. `pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held`: `Lab glass`'s version 1 is pinned through `pinEntryVersion`, and a second pin of it answers `Ok ()`. The material, decoded and given the catalogue Langasite's complexity, saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial` then resolves at versions 1 and 2, and version 1 keeps Silicon's complexity. A put `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack`, its version 1 pinned the same way, makes `samples.removeSample` answer `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. Version 3 of `Lab glass` and version 1 of a test-local GUID answer `ImportRejectedErr`. `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` gains `pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle`. Over a database the fact opens as the class's `freshImport` does, after `importFrom` of the Built-in catalogue and `retireEntry` of one built-in source, `pinEntryVersion` of version 1 of one entry of each of the six kinds, that source included, leaves each of those rows `VersionPinned`, read through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`. The source stays `InactiveEntry`, and every other entry's version 1 stays `VersionUnpinned`. The inherited `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` and `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` (steps 66, 73) run unchanged over the shared `stagePin`.", "acceptance": "After the seam grows, both implementations of `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST answer `heldUserEntries` and `pinEntryVersion`, and the database pin verbs MUST share `stagePin`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in` and `pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held` over both stores and `pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 116, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [115], "how_to": "One library entry exports to its own `-json` file, and exporting pins the version it writes (001 §B 'Export: any entry → its `-json` file … Exporting pins the exported versions'; 001 §A: the file name is the entry's name made filesystem-safe plus its kind's extension; the S3.3 brief). Export lives on the import context, the library-exchange seam that every library window already carries (steps 101, 109), so no new context is threaded. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, before `CatalogueImportContext`: `LibraryExportError` is an `*Error` union, each case documented. `ExportedEntryNotHeldErr of reason : string` is an entry to export that the library does not hold, named by its id. `ExportLibraryRefusedErr of CatalogueImportError` is a seam failure while reading or pinning. `ExportFileWriteErr of reason : string` is an entry file that could not be written, naming the file. `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: a fixed phrase naming the condition, a colon, then the reason or the wrapped error's `describe`. (2) On `CatalogueImportProxy`: `member this.tryLatestEnvelope (id : LibraryEntryId) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope option, CatalogueImportError>` is `tryHeldEntry id` and then `tryHeldEnvelope id held.latest` (step 105); an id not held answers `None`. (3) `CatalogueImportContext` (steps 94, 98, 104) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `writeEntryFile : FileName -> LibraryEntryEnvelope -> Result<unit, LibraryExportError>` writes one entry's file. `exportFolderOpt : FolderName option` is the folder the export dialogs open in (001 §G 'Exports': the catalogue-export folder), `None` where no location is configured. `member this.exportEntry (id : LibraryEntryId) (file : FileName) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, LibraryExportError>` reads the latest envelope through `tryLatestEnvelope`: `None` is `ExportedEntryNotHeldErr` naming the id, and a read error is `ExportLibraryRefusedErr`. It then pins that version through `proxy.pinEntryVersion` (step 115) before anything is written, so the file always names a frozen version. It then writes the file through `writeEntryFile` and answers the envelope written. The member doc says so in one to three lines. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `create`, its signature unchanged, fills `writeEntryFile` with the envelope's `fileText` (step 30) written through `LibraryFileText.writeAtomically` (step 33). The file is therefore byte-identical to the catalogue's and the database's copy of the entry (001 §C 'Hybrid shape'). A `StorageError` is `ExportFileWriteErr` naming the file, with the error's `describe`. `create` sets `exportFolderOpt` to `None`; the composition root sets the configured folder (step 118). No overwrite check is added, because the save dialog's own prompt guards the chosen file (steps 119, 120). (5) Tests. Each file goes into a fresh folder, a GUID name under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryExportTests\")`. `CatalogueImportContract` gains two facts, so each runs over both stores. `exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse`: after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` and `putSealedEntries` of `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` (step 113), `exportEntry` of it to `<folder>/Lab glass.material-json` answers the held envelope. The context's `readEntryFile MaterialEntryKind` (step 104) reads that file back equal, and `decideDroppedFiles` of it answers one `SameContentHash` row. The material, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial`, then resolves at versions 1 and 2. `exportEntry` of `MaterialIds.silicon` to `<folder>/Silicon.material-json` writes a file whose text equals `Catalogue/Builtin/Silicon.material-json` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, byte for byte. `exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing`: a test-local GUID answers `ExportedEntryNotHeldErr` naming it, and the folder holds no file. `CatalogueImportProxyTests` gains `every export error renders its condition and its payload`: each of the three cases, over a distinct test-local reason or a wrapped `ImportRejectedErr`, renders a distinct text holding its reason or the wrapped error's `describe`.", "acceptance": "After single-entry export lands, `CatalogueImportContext.exportEntry` MUST pin the latest version before it writes that entry's file; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse` and `exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing` over both stores and `every export error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every export error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.LibraryExportError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 117, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [116], "how_to": "A selection, a category or the whole of the user's library exports to a catalogue folder: one `.catalogue-json` manifest and one file per entry (001 §B 'Export: … a selection or a category → a catalogue folder'; 001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout': uniqueness per kind within a catalogue is checked on export; 001 §C '\"Export my library\" writes the user entries to a catalogue folder, which the recreated database imports'; the S3.3 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`. (a) `CatalogueExportTarget = { folder : FolderName; name : CatalogueName }` is where a catalogue export goes and the name its manifest carries. (b) `LibraryExportError` (step 116) gains three cases, each documented and each with a `describe` line. `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr of CatalogueError`: the entries do not form a catalogue (`InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr` from `CatalogueData.tryCreate`), or the folder write failed. `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr of reason : string`: the target folder already holds a catalogue manifest, naming the folder. `EmptyLibraryExportErr of reason : string`: there is nothing to export. (c) `CatalogueImportContext` gains `newCatalogueId : unit -> CatalogueId`, documented as the id an exported catalogue is minted under and injected as `newEntryId` is. (d) `member this.exportEntries (ids : LibraryEntryId list) (target : CatalogueExportTarget) : Result<CatalogueData, LibraryExportError>` works in this order, and nothing is pinned or written before its last two steps. (i) An empty list is `EmptyLibraryExportErr` naming the folder. (ii) Each distinct id's latest envelope is read through `tryLatestEnvelope` (`ExportedEntryNotHeldErr`, `ExportLibraryRefusedErr`). (iii) The user entries they reference join them. Every id in an exported content's `referencedEntryIds` (step 93) that is not yet exported, and for which `tryHeldEntry` answers a `UserManaged` entry, joins at its latest version, and its own references are followed the same way. A referenced built-in does not join, because every library imports the shipped catalogue. So a sample over Silicon exports alone, and an export of user entries never meets a built-in's file name. (iv) The per-kind name check comes first among the refusals: `CatalogueData.tryCreate (this.newCatalogueId ()) target.name VersionNumber.first envelopes` (step 32). Its refusal is `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr`, so two exported entries of one kind and one file name are refused, naming both (step 26's `DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`). (v) `(this.openCatalogue target.folder).readManifest ()` (steps 92, 98). `Ok manifest` or `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` is `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr` naming the folder, so an export never overwrites a catalogue. Any other answer (no folder, no manifest) goes on; the writer creates a missing folder. (vi) Every envelope's version is pinned through `proxy.pinEntryVersion` (step 115). (vii) `writeCatalogue` writes the data (step 33: the entry files, then the manifest, each atomically; a folder holding an entry file the catalogue does not name is refused, and those pins stay, which only makes the next physics edit mint a version). The answer is the data written. (e) `member this.exportUserLibrary (target : CatalogueExportTarget) : Result<CatalogueData, LibraryExportError>` is `exportEntries` over every id `proxy.heldUserEntries ()` answers, inactive entries included, so a recreated library gets back everything the user owned (001 §C). A library holding no user entry is `EmptyLibraryExportErr`. A catalogue holds one version of each entry, its latest, because the folder names each entry's file by its name (001 §A). Each member doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `create`, its signature unchanged, fills `newCatalogueId` with a new GUID. `type CatalogueExportTarget with static member ofFolder (folder : FolderName) : CatalogueExportTarget` names the target by the folder's last segment (`Path.GetFileName` of the path without its trailing separator), so a chosen folder `…/Lab catalogue` exports as the catalogue `Lab catalogue`. The export dialogs call it (steps 119, 120). Its doc is one line. No merge into an existing catalogue, version bump of a re-export, progress report or option is added: each target folder becomes a new catalogue. (3) Tests. Each target is a fresh GUID folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryExportTests\")`, not created beforehand. Entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `putSealedEntries` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. `CatalogueImportContract` gains six facts, so each runs over both stores. `a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry`: `userCategoryContent` `Lab category`, `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` with its `categoryOpt` set to that category, and `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack` over `Lab glass`. `exportEntries [ Lab stack ]` answers data whose envelopes are exactly those three, each equal to its held latest envelope. `CatalogueProxy.create` over the folder reads it back equal, its manifest named `target.name`. `proxy.decideCatalogue` of it answers three `SameContentHash` rows, each defaulting to `ReuseHeldEntry`, and `importCatalogue` of it answers `Ok []` with `heldUserEntries` unchanged. `a catalogue export pins every exported version`: after (E1)'s export, `Lab glass`, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial`, resolves at versions 1 and 2, and `samples.removeSample` of `Lab stack` answers `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. `a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing`: two `userMaterialContent`s named `Lab glass` under two ids answer `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr (InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr (DuplicateEntryFileNameErr reason))`, whose reason names both entries (step 26). The target folder does not exist, and the first material, given Langasite's complexity and saved, still resolves at version 1 alone. `a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue`: after `Lab glass` is exported to the target, exporting `Lab stack` to it answers `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr` naming the folder, and every file's text in it is unchanged. `Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in`: over `Lab category`, `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and a `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` retired through `retireEntry`, `exportUserLibrary` answers data whose ids are exactly `heldUserEntries ()`'s four, none under `BuiltInProvenance`, and the folder reads back equal. `an export with nothing to write is refused`: `exportEntries []`, and `exportUserLibrary` over a library holding only the Built-in catalogue, each answer `EmptyLibraryExportErr`, and the target folder does not exist. `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` gains `a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind`: over a database the fact opens as the class's `freshImport` does, `Lab category`, `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and a user source (the catalogue's first source under a fresh GUID id and `UserManaged`, built with `ofSourcePreset` under `UserProvenance`) are put. `exportEntries` of those four and of one built-in polarizer and one built-in detector leaves each exported version row `VersionPinned`, read through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`, while an unexported built-in source stays `VersionUnpinned`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `a catalogue export target is named by its folder`: `ofFolder (FolderName \"D:/Exports/Lab catalogue\")` and `ofFolder (FolderName \"D:/Exports/Lab catalogue/\")` each answer the folder as given and `CatalogueName \"Lab catalogue\"`. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `every export error renders its condition and its payload` (step 116) covers the three new cases.", "acceptance": "After catalogue export lands, `exportEntries` and `exportUserLibrary` MUST check per-kind file-name uniqueness before they pin, pin before they write, and never overwrite a catalogue folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry`, `a catalogue export pins every exported version`, `a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing`, `a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue`, `Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in`, `an export with nothing to write is refused` over both stores, `a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind`, `a catalogue export target is named by its folder` and `every export error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 14; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export pins every exported version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export pins every exported version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.an export with nothing to write is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.an export with nothing to write is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.a catalogue export target is named by its folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every export error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.LibraryExportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueExportTarget", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 118, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [117], "how_to": "The two library windows share one verb box and one folder picker, and the app's import context suggests the configured catalogue-export folder (001 §G 'Exports' and 'Every path is overridable'; S2.4 interpretation 10: the catalogue-export location is carried in `DataLocations` until its reader arrives; spec 0048 R2 and S3.2 interpretation 6: the lower declaration serves both windows). Both windows behave as before. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) The body of `verbButton` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:889`, public since step 107) moves into the new public `verbButtonOn (id : ConstructorUiId) (label : ControlCaption) (onPressed : PointerPressedEventArgs -> unit) : IView`, which hands the press to `onPressed`, and `verbButton id label onClick` becomes `verbButtonOn id label (fun _ -> onClick ())`. (b) The public `pickLibraryFolder (owner : Window) (title : ControlCaption) (startOpt : FolderName option) (onPicked : FolderName -> unit) : unit` is step 101's `pickCatalogueFolder` body, moved, with the title and the start folder as parameters. It opens `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync` with `FolderPickerOpenOptions(Title = title.value, AllowMultiple = false)`. For `Some folder`, `SuggestedStartLocation` is resolved through `StorageProviderExtensions.TryGetFolderFromPathAsync`, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile` (`:3376`) resolves its folder. A confirmed pick passes the first folder's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FolderName`, posted on the UI thread, and a host without a provider changes nothing. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`: its private `verbButton` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1020`) and step 101's private `verbButtonOn` and `pickCatalogueFolder` are deleted. Every call uses `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` or `MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn`, and Register catalogue folder… calls `MaterialsWindowView.pickLibraryFolder owner (ControlCaption \"Register catalogue folder\") None`. The look, the ids and the messages are unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the compose that `create` and `recreateLibrary` share (steps 89, 100) builds `catalogueImports` as `CatalogueImportContext.create` with `exportFolderOpt` (step 116) set to `Some locations.cataloguesFolder` (`DataLocations.cataloguesFolder`, step 81) by record update, so every library window the app opens suggests it. Every other composition (`DefaultStores`, `initWith`, the tests) keeps `None`. (4) Tests. `AppContextTests` gains `the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports`: over an app context composed through `TestAppScope` (step 83: `testLocations`, `freshAppContext`), `catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` is `Some` of those locations' `cataloguesFolder`, and `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`'s `exportFolderOpt` is `None`. Every `LibraryWindowTests`, `MaterialsWindowTests` and `ImportDialogTests` fact passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the shared pieces land, `LibraryWindowView.fs` MUST declare no `verbButton`, `verbButtonOn` or `pickCatalogueFolder` of its own, and the app's `catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` MUST be the configured catalogues folder; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-SHARED-WINDOW-PIECES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-SHARED-WINDOW-PIECES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.pickLibraryFolder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-SHARED-WINDOW-PIECES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 119, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.3g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [118], "how_to": "The Materials window exports the selected material to its file and the shown materials to a catalogue folder, and credits a licensed material (001 §B 'Export', 'Licence attribution'; 001 §G 'Exports'; the S3.3 brief: the buttons go in the Library and Materials windows, with messages and ids; a single-entry export goes through a save dialog defaulting to the catalogues folder; a category exports to a catalogue folder; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each a one-line doc: `type LibraryExportError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`); `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.exportedCaption (file : FileName) : ControlCaption` = `Exported <name> version <n> to <file>; that version is now pinned.`; and `type CatalogueData with member this.exportedCaption (folder : FolderName) : ControlCaption` = `Exported <k> entries to the catalogue folder <folder>; their versions are now pinned.`, `k` counting its envelopes. Both windows render their export outcomes through these alone. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) The public `pickEntryExportFile (owner : Window) (startOpt : FolderName option) (envelope : LibraryEntryEnvelope) (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` is the save dialog, an IO edge in `pickLibraryFolder`'s shape (step 118): `owner.StorageProvider.SaveFilePickerAsync` with `Title = \"Export library entry\"`, `SuggestedFileName = envelope.content.fileName.value`, `DefaultExtension` the kind's extension without its leading dot, one `FilePickerFileType` whose pattern is `*` plus that extension, `ShowOverwritePrompt = true`, and `startOpt` resolved as `pickLibraryFolder` resolves it. A confirmed file's `Path.LocalPath` is passed as a `FileName`, posted on the UI thread. (b) The public `attributionPanel (id : ConstructorUiId) (lines : EntryAttributionLine list) : IView list` answers nothing for no line, else one vertical `StackPanel` carrying `id` that holds one wrapping `TextBlock` per line (`line.text`, max width 380). (c) `MaterialsWindowModel` gains `entryExportStatus : ControlCaption option` and `entryExportError : LibraryExportError option`, both `None` when the window opens, each with a one-line doc. (d) `member this.exportableSelection : LibraryEntryEnvelope option` is, in Browse mode, the selected material's latest envelope through `context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope id.toLibraryEntryId` (step 116), and `None` in Select mode, without a selection, for a material the seam does not hold, or on a read error. (e) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `ExportSelectedMaterial of FileName` (the selected material's latest version to the file chosen in the save dialog) and `ExportShownMaterials of CatalogueExportTarget` (the materials the window shows, its text filter and facets applied, to a catalogue folder; a category facet makes it that category's export). (f) `updateMaterialsWindow`. `ExportSelectedMaterial file` is inert without a selection, and otherwise calls `context.catalogueImports.exportEntry id.toLibraryEntryId file`. `ExportShownMaterials target` calls `exportEntries` over `m.filteredEntries` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:476`), each `e.id.toLibraryEntryId`, and `target`. `Ok` sets `entryExportStatus` to the outcome's `exportedCaption` and clears `entryExportError`; `Error e` sets `entryExportError` to `Some e` and clears `entryExportStatus`. Neither arms or disarms a gate, or changes the selection or the mode. (g) The view. In the verbs row (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:971`), in Browse mode and after Categories…: while `exportableSelection` is `Some envelope`, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.materialsExportButton (ControlCaption \"Export…\")` resolves the owner window from the press, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton` does, and calls `pickEntryExportFile owner context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt envelope (fun file -> dispatch (ExportSelectedMaterial file))`. While `filteredEntries` is not empty, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.materialsExportShownButton (ControlCaption \"Export shown to catalogue…\")` calls `pickLibraryFolder owner (ControlCaption \"Export to catalogue folder\") context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` and dispatches `ExportShownMaterials (CatalogueExportTarget.ofFolder folder)` (step 117). After step 110's import status, when either is set, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialsExportStatusText` shows `entryExportError`'s caption in `messageColor`, or else `entryExportStatus`. The view panel (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:1096`), after the description, holds `attributionPanel ConstructorUiId.materialsAttributionPanel` over `context.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf [ shownEntry.id.toLibraryEntryId ]` (step 114), and nothing on a read error. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group (`UiIds.fs:525`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.3: `materialsExportButton` (`\"MaterialsExportButton\"`), `materialsExportShownButton` (`\"MaterialsExportShownButton\"`), `materialsExportStatusText` (`\"MaterialsExportStatusText\"`) and `materialsAttributionPanel` (`\"MaterialsAttributionPanel\"`). (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`. The export and attribution facts compose `stubContext` (step 110) over the in-memory double: with `let stores = CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, the context takes `stores.materials`, `stores.categories` and `CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy`, the Built-in catalogue is imported through its `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and test entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries`. Files go into fresh GUID folders under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"MaterialsWindowTests\")`. `the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids`: the four ids' texts. `ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version`: with `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` selected (`SelectEntry`), `ExportSelectedMaterial` of `<folder>/Lab glass.material-json` writes the file, which the context's `readEntryFile` reads back equal to the held envelope. `entryExportStatus` is `Exported Lab glass version 1 to <file>; that version is now pinned.`, and `Lab glass`, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through `stores.materials`, resolves at versions 1 and 2. `ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category`: `userCategoryContent` `Lab category` holds `Lab glass` and `Lab quartz` (their `categoryOpt` set to it), and `Other glass` stays in Silicon's category. With the material-category facet applied to `Lab category` (`ApplyFacetValue`), `ExportShownMaterials` of a target folder writes a catalogue holding exactly the two materials and the category, and the status counts 3 entries. `a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing`: with a committed text filter `Lab glass` showing two user materials of that name, `ExportShownMaterials` sets `entryExportError` to `Some (ExportCatalogueRefusedErr _)`, the status is `None`, and the target folder does not exist; a following `ExportSelectedMaterial` that succeeds clears the error. `a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only`: `exportableSelection` is the held envelope of the selected `Lab glass`, `None` without a selection, and `None` for a Select-mode model over the same context and selection. `the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone`: `materialsWindowView` mounted headless, as the class's mounting facts mount the window's view, with `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` (`CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`) selected, shows `materialsAttributionPanel` holding the text `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`. With `RII glass` (`CC0-1.0`) selected it holds `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0` and no `cite:`, and with `Lab glass` selected no `materialsAttributionPanel` is present.", "acceptance": "After the Materials window is wired, its Export… and Export shown to catalogue… verbs MUST export through `exportEntry` and `exportEntries`, and its view panel MUST show the selected material's attribution; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids`, `ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version`, `ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category`, `a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing`, `a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only`, `the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.pickEntryExportFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.attributionPanel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 120, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.3h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [119], "how_to": "The Library window exports the selected entry, the shown entries and the user's whole library, and credits the licensed materials of a selected sample (001 §B 'Export', 'Licence attribution'; 001 §C '\"Export my library\" writes the user entries to a catalogue folder'; .spec-md §10.1: 'Export my library…' is in the Library window; the S3.3 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowError` gains `LibraryExportRefusedErr of LibraryExportError`, documented, and its `caption` renders it through `LibraryExportError.caption` (step 119). (b) `LibraryWindowModel` gains `entryExportStatus : ControlCaption option`, `None` when the window opens, with a one-line doc. (c) `member this.exportableSelection : LibraryEntryEnvelope option` is, in Browse mode, the selected entry's latest envelope through `entry.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId` (step 24) and `context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope` (step 116), and `None` otherwise, as step 119's is. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry of FileName`, `ExportShownLibraryEntries of CatalogueExportTarget` and `ExportMyLibrary of CatalogueExportTarget`. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry file` is inert without an `exportableSelection`, and otherwise calls `context.catalogueImports.exportEntry` of its id and `file`. `ExportShownLibraryEntries target` calls `exportEntries` over the ids of `m.filteredEntries` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:518`), each `e.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId`. `ExportMyLibrary target` calls `exportUserLibrary target` (step 117). `Ok` sets `entryExportStatus` to the outcome's `exportedCaption` (step 119) and clears `lastError`; `Error e` sets `lastError` to `Some (LibraryExportRefusedErr e)` and clears `entryExportStatus`. None of them arms or disarms a gate, or changes the selection or the mode. (f) The view. In the verbs row (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1104`), in Browse mode and after step 101's Register catalogue folder… and step 111's Review imports…, through `MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn` and the pickers of steps 118 and 119 opened at `context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt`: `libraryExportButton` (`Export…`) while `exportableSelection` is `Some`, dispatching `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry`; `libraryExportShownButton` (`Export shown to catalogue…`) while `filteredEntries` is not empty, dispatching `ExportShownLibraryEntries`; and `libraryExportMyLibraryButton` (`Export my library…`), always, its picker titled `Export my library to a catalogue folder`, dispatching `ExportMyLibrary`. Each catalogue target is `CatalogueExportTarget.ofFolder` of the picked folder. `entryExportStatus`, when `Some`, shows in a `TextBlock` carrying `libraryExportStatusText` after step 101's `libraryImportStatusText`. The view panel (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1240`), after the description, holds `MaterialsWindowView.attributionPanel ConstructorUiId.libraryAttributionPanel` over `context.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf entry.attributedEntryIds` (steps 113, 114), and nothing on a read error, so a selected sample credits the licensed materials of its layers. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group (`UiIds.fs:498`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.3: `libraryExportButton` (`\"LibraryExportButton\"`), `libraryExportShownButton` (`\"LibraryExportShownButton\"`), `libraryExportMyLibraryButton` (`\"LibraryExportMyLibraryButton\"`), `libraryExportStatusText` (`\"LibraryExportStatusText\"`) and `libraryAttributionPanel` (`\"LibraryAttributionPanel\"`). (3) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`. The export and attribution facts compose `stubContext` (steps 101, 111) over the in-memory double: with `let stores = CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, the context takes `samples = stores.samples`, `materials = stores.materials`, `library = stores.libraryEntries` and `catalogueImports = CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy`, the Built-in catalogue is imported through its `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and test entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries`. Files go into fresh GUID folders under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryWindowTests\")`. `the export and attribution UiIds of the Library window are the stable intent-named ids`: the five ids' texts. `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry writes the selected entry's file and pins its version`: with `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack` over `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` selected (`SelectLibraryEntry`), `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry` of `<folder>/Lab stack.sample-json` writes the file, which the context's `readEntryFile` reads back equal to the held envelope. `entryExportStatus` is `Exported Lab stack version 1 to <file>; that version is now pinned.`, and `stores.samples.removeSample` of `Lab stack` answers `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. `ExportShownLibraryEntries writes the shown entries and the user materials they reference`: with the text filter `Lab stack` committed (`CommitLibraryTextFilter`), `ExportShownLibraryEntries` of a target folder writes a catalogue holding exactly `Lab stack` and `Lab glass`, and the status counts 2 entries. `ExportMyLibrary writes every user entry to a catalogue folder`: over `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass`, `ExportMyLibrary` writes a catalogue whose ids are exactly `heldUserEntries ()`'s three, none under `BuiltInProvenance`. `a refused Library export shows its reason as the window message`: over a library holding only the Built-in catalogue, `ExportMyLibrary` sets `lastError` to `Some (LibraryExportRefusedErr (EmptyLibraryExportErr _))`, `entryExportStatus` is `None`, and the target folder does not exist. `the Library window shows the citation of a CC-BY material of the selected sample`: `libraryWindowView` mounted headless, as the class's mounting facts mount the window's view, with `PTB stack` (a `sampleContentOver` `PTB glass`, `CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`) selected, shows `libraryAttributionPanel` holding `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`; with a built-in source selected no `libraryAttributionPanel` is present. `Export my library over the app library writes a catalogue folder that a new library registers with every user entry`: over `AppContext.create` of one `TestAppScope.fileLocations` scope, a user material `Lab glass` saved through the context's `materials.saveMaterial` and a sample `Lab stack` over it saved through `samples.saveSample` reach the database seam. `stubContext` updated with the app context's stores and `catalogueImports` takes `ExportMyLibrary` of a target folder under the test output, and its status counts 2 entries. Over a second, fresh scope, a second `AppContext.create`'s `catalogueImports.registerFolder` of that folder answers `Ok (CatalogueImported _)`, and its `materials.tryGetMaterial` and `samples.tryGetSample` resolve both entries unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the Library window is wired, its Export…, Export shown to catalogue… and Export my library… verbs MUST export through `exportEntry`, `exportEntries` and `exportUserLibrary`, and its view panel MUST credit the licensed materials of a selected sample; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the export and attribution UiIds of the Library window are the stable intent-named ids`, `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry writes the selected entry's file and pins its version`, `ExportShownLibraryEntries writes the shown entries and the user materials they reference`, `ExportMyLibrary writes every user entry to a catalogue folder`, `a refused Library export shows its reason as the window message`, `the Library window shows the citation of a CC-BY material of the selected sample`, `Export my library over the app library writes a catalogue folder that a new library registers with every user entry`, the count rising by 7; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the export and attribution UiIds of the Library window are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.ExportSelectedLibraryEntry writes the selected entry's file and pins its version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.ExportShownLibraryEntries writes the shown entries and the user materials they reference", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.ExportMyLibrary writes every user entry to a catalogue folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a refused Library export shows its reason as the window message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the Library window shows the citation of a CC-BY material of the selected sample", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.Export my library over the app library writes a catalogue folder that a new library registers with every user entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 121, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.3i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [120], "how_to": "The Details bay credits the licensed entries of the selected element's binding: the bound entry and, for a sample, the materials of its layers (001 §B 'Licence attribution': in the Details view; the S3.3 brief: the Details view of a bound element). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, in the `type TableAndElementRotationModel with` block that holds `detailsState` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3187`): the public `member model.detailsAttributionLines : EntryAttributionLine list`. For `ElementSelected i` whose element has a bound entry (`boundEntry`, `:2449`), it is `model.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf entry.attributedEntryIds` (steps 101, 113, 114). It is `[]` on a read error, for an unbound element, and without an element selection. `detailsState` appends each line's `text` on its own line after the title and the out-of-band warning, so the Details bay (`BayNames.details`) shows the credit under what the element is. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) Tests, in `LayerBandsControlsTests`, over `initMain ()`, whose `catalogueImports` is the in-memory double its stores were imported through (step 101's `DefaultStores`). Step 113's `putSealedEntries` puts `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` (`CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`), `licensedMaterialContent` `RII glass` (`CC0-1.0`), and `sampleContentOver` `PTB stack` and `RII stack` over them; the double pushes each new entry into the model's stores. `the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation`: after `AddElement Sample` and the class's `bind` of the new element to `PTB stack`, `detailsAttributionLines` is exactly one line whose text is `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`. Bound to `RII stack`, it is `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0`, and bound to `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s sample, it is `[]`. `the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material`: the Details bay, mounted headless as `the Details bay renders the bound multilayer sample's bands and description` mounts it but without the `ui-smoke` trait, shows a `layerBandsTitle` whose text holds `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test` for an element bound to `PTB stack`.", "acceptance": "After the Details bay is wired, `detailsAttributionLines` MUST credit a bound entry and the licensed materials of a bound sample, and the Details bay MUST show them; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation` and `the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests.the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-DETAILS-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests.the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-DETAILS-ATTRIBUTION"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
